#: src/macros-by-example.md:1438
msgid "With `macro_export`, path-based resolution works."
msgstr "有了 `macro_export`，基于路径的解析就能工作。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1457
msgid ""
"The `macro_export` attribute causes a macro to be exported from the crate "
"root so that it can be referred to in other crates by path."
msgstr ""
"`macro_export` 属性会使宏从 crate 根导出，从而可以在其他 crate 中通过路径引用"
"它。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1463 src/macros-by-example.md:1494
msgid "Given the following in a `log` crate:"
msgstr "给定 `log` crate 中的以下内容："

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1468 src/macros-by-example.md:1499
msgid "\"WARN: {}\""
msgstr "\"WARN: {}\""

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1472
msgid "From another crate, you can refer to the macro by path:"
msgstr "在另一个 crate 中，可以通过路径引用该宏："

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1477 src/macros-by-example.md:1513
msgid "\"example warning\""
msgstr "\"example warning\""

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1488
msgid ""
"`macro_export` allows the use of [`macro_use`](macros-by-example.md#r-"
"macro.decl.scope.macro_use) on an `extern crate` to import the macro into "
"the [`macro_use` prelude](names/preludes.md#macro_use-prelude)."
msgstr ""
"`macro_export` 允许在 `extern crate` 上使用 [`macro_use`](macros-by-"
"example.md#r-macro.decl.scope.macro_use)，以将该宏导入 [`macro_use` prelude]"
"(names/preludes.md#macro_use-prelude)。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1503
msgid ""
"Using `macro_use` in a dependent crate allows you to use the macro from the "
"prelude:"
msgstr "在依赖 crate 中使用 `macro_use`，可以让你从 prelude 使用该宏："

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1512
msgid "// Resolved via macro prelude.\n"
msgstr "// Resolved via macro prelude.\n"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1525
msgid ""
"Adding `local_inner_macros` to the `macro_export` attribute causes all "
"single-segment macro invocations in the macro definition to have an implicit "
"`$crate::` prefix."
msgstr ""
"向 `macro_export` 属性添加 `local_inner_macros`，会使宏定义中的所有单段宏调用"
"都带有隐式的 `$crate::` 前缀。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1531
msgid ""
"This is intended primarily as a tool to migrate code written before "
"[`$crate`](macros-by-example.md#r-macro.decl.hygiene.crate) was added to the "
"language to work with Rust 2018's path-based imports of macros. Its use is "
"discouraged in new code."
msgstr ""
"这主要是作为一种迁移工具，用于迁移在 [`$crate`](macros-by-example.md#r-"
"macro.decl.hygiene.crate) 加入语言之前编写的代码，使其能够与 Rust 2018 的基于"
"路径的宏导入配合工作。不鼓励在新代码中使用它。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1543
msgid "// Automatically converted to $crate::helper!().\n"
msgstr "// Automatically converted to $crate::helper!().\n"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1559
msgid "Hygiene"
msgstr "卫生性"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1565
msgid ""
"Macros by example have _mixed-site hygiene_. This means that [loop labels]"
"(expressions/loop-expr.md#loop-labels), [block labels](expressions/loop-"
"expr.md#r-expr.loop.block-labels), and local variables are looked up at the "
"macro definition site while other symbols are looked up at the macro "
"invocation site. For example:"
msgstr ""
"示例宏具有<em>混合位置卫生性</em>。这意味着[循环标签](expressions/loop-"
"expr.md#loop-labels)、[块标签](expressions/loop-expr.md#r-expr.loop.block-"
"labels) 和局部变量会在宏定义位置查找，而其他符号会在宏调用位置查找。例如："

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1570
msgid "\"this is never called\""
msgstr "\"this is never called\""

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1575
msgid "// Uses `x` from the definition site.\n"
msgstr "// Uses `x` from the definition site.\n"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1576
msgid "// Uses `func` from the invocation site.\n"
msgstr "// Uses `func` from the invocation site.\n"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1582
msgid "/* does not panic */"
msgstr "/* does not panic */"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1587
msgid ""
"Labels and local variables defined in macro expansion are not shared between "
"invocations, so this code doesn’t compile:"
msgstr ""
"宏展开中定义的标签和局部变量不会在各次调用之间共享，因此这段代码无法编译："

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1607
msgid ""
"A special case is the `$crate` metavariable. It refers to the crate defining "
"the macro, and can be used at the start of the path to look up items or "
"macros which are not in scope at the invocation site."
msgstr ""
"一个特殊情况是 `$crate` 元变量。它指代定义该宏的 crate，并且可以用在路径开"
"头，用于查找在调用位置不在作用域内的条目或宏。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1611
msgid "//// Definitions in the `helper_macro` crate.\n"
msgstr "//// Definitions in the `helper_macro` crate.\n"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1614
msgid ""
"// () => { helper!() } // This might lead to an error due to 'helper' not "
"being in scope.\n"
msgstr ""
"// () => { helper!() } // This might lead to an error due to 'helper' not "
"being in scope.\n"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1622
msgid ""
"//// Usage in another crate.\n"
"// Note that `helper_macro::helper` is not imported!\n"
msgstr ""
"//// Usage in another crate.\n"
"// Note that `helper_macro::helper` is not imported!\n"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1632
msgid ""
"Note that, because `$crate` refers to the current crate, it must be used "
"with a fully qualified module path when referring to non-macro items:"
msgstr ""
"注意，因为 `$crate` 指代当前 crate，所以引用非宏条目时必须将它与完全限定模块"
"路径一起使用："

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1649
msgid ""
"Additionally, even though `$crate` allows a macro to refer to items within "
"its own crate when expanding, its use has no effect on visibility. An item "
"or macro referred to must still be visible from the invocation site. In the "
"following example, any attempt to invoke `call_foo!()` from outside its "
"crate will fail because `foo()` is not public."
msgstr ""
"此外，即使 `$crate` 允许宏在展开时引用其自身 crate 内的条目，它的使用也不会影"
"响可见性。被引用的条目或宏仍然必须从调用位置可见。在下面的示例中，任何从其 "
"crate 外部调用 `call_foo!()` 的尝试都会失败，因为 `foo()` 不是公开的。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1664
msgid ""
"Prior to Rust 1.30, `$crate` and [`local_inner_macros`](macros-by-"
"example.md#r-macro.decl.scope.macro_export.local_inner_macros) were "
"unsupported. They were added alongside [path-based imports of macros](macros-"
"by-example.md#r-macro.decl.scope.macro_export), to ensure that helper macros "
"did not need to be manually imported by users of a macro-exporting crate. "
"Crates written for earlier versions of Rust that use helper macros need to "
"be modified to use `$crate` or `local_inner_macros` to work well with path-"
"based imports."
msgstr ""
"在 Rust 1.30 之前，`$crate` 和 [`local_inner_macros`](macros-by-example.md#r-"
"macro.decl.scope.macro_export.local_inner_macros) 尚不受支持。它们是与[宏的基"
"于路径的导入](macros-by-example.md#r-macro.decl.scope.macro_export)一同加入"
"的，以确保导出宏的 crate 的用户不需要手动导入辅助宏。为较早 Rust 版本编写且使"
"用辅助宏的 crate，需要修改为使用 `$crate` 或 `local_inner_macros`，才能与基于"
"路径的导入良好配合。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1673
msgid "Follow-set ambiguity restrictions"
msgstr "Follow 集歧义限制"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1679
msgid ""
"The parser used by the macro system is reasonably powerful, but it is "
"limited in order to prevent ambiguity in current or future versions of the "
"language."
msgstr ""
"宏系统使用的解析器相当强大，但为了防止当前或未来语言版本中的歧义，它也受到限"
"制。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1685
msgid ""
"In particular, in addition to the rule about ambiguous expansions, a "
"nonterminal matched by a metavariable must be followed by a token which has "
"been decided can be safely used after that kind of match."
msgstr ""
"特别是，除了关于歧义展开的规则外，由元变量匹配的非终结符后面必须跟随一个已被"
"判定可安全用于该类匹配之后的 token。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1687
msgid ""
"As an example, a macro matcher like `$i:expr [ , ]` could in theory be "
"accepted in Rust today, since `[,]` cannot be part of a legal expression and "
"therefore the parse would always be unambiguous. However, because `[` can "
"start trailing expressions, `[` is not a character which can safely be ruled "
"out as coming after an expression. If `[,]` were accepted in a later version "
"of Rust, this matcher would become ambiguous or would misparse, breaking "
"working code. Matchers like `$i:expr,` or `$i:expr;` would be legal, "
"however, because `,` and `;` are legal expression separators. The specific "
"rules are:"
msgstr ""
"举例来说，像 `$i:expr [ , ]` 这样的宏匹配器在今天的 Rust 中理论上可以被接受，"
"因为 `[,]` 不能成为合法表达式的一部分，因此解析总是无歧义的。不过，因为 `[` "
"可以开始尾随表达式，不能安全地排除 `[` 出现在表达式之后的可能性。如果在较后"
"的 Rust 版本中接受了 `[,]`，这个匹配器就会变得有歧义，或被错误解析，从而破坏"
"可工作的代码。不过，像 `$i:expr,` 或 `$i:expr;` 这样的匹配器是合法的，因为 "
"`,` 和 `;` 是合法的表达式分隔符。具体规则如下："

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1693
msgid "`expr` and `stmt` may only be followed by one of: `=>`, `,`, or `;`."
msgstr "`expr` 和 `stmt` 后面只能跟随以下之一：`=>`、`,` 或 `;`。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1699
msgid ""
"`pat_param` may only be followed by one of: `=>`, `,`, `=`, `|`, `if`, or "
"`in`."
msgstr "`pat_param` 后面只能跟随以下之一：`=>`、`,`、`=`、`|`、`if` 或 `in`。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1705
msgid "`pat` may only be followed by one of: `=>`, `,`, `=`, `if`, or `in`."
msgstr "`pat` 后面只能跟随以下之一：`=>`、`,`、`=`、`if` 或 `in`。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1711
msgid ""
"`path` and `ty` may only be followed by one of: `=>`, `,`, `=`, `|`, `;`, "
"`:`, `>`, `>>`, `[`, `{`, `as`, `where`, or a macro variable of `block` "
"fragment specifier."
msgstr ""
"`path` 和 `ty` 后面只能跟随以下之一：`=>`、`,`、`=`、`|`、`;`、`:`、`>`、"
"`>>`、`[`、`{`、`as`、`where`，或片段说明符为 `block` 的宏变量。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1717
msgid ""
"`vis` may only be followed by one of: `,`, an identifier other than a non-"
"raw `priv`, any token that can begin a type, or a metavariable with a "
"`ident`, `ty`, or `path` fragment specifier."
msgstr ""
"`vis` 后面只能跟随以下之一：`,`、除一个非 raw 的 `priv` 之外的标识符、任何可"
"以开始类型的 token，或带有 `ident`、`ty` 或 `path` 片段说明符的元变量。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1723
msgid "All other fragment specifiers have no restrictions."
msgstr "所有其他片段说明符没有限制。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1733
msgid "Before the 2021 edition, `pat` may also be followed by `|`."
msgstr "在 2021 edition 之前，`pat` 后面也可以跟随 `|`。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1742
msgid ""
"When repetitions are involved, then the rules apply to every possible number "
"of expansions, taking separators into account. This means:"
msgstr ""
"涉及重复时，这些规则会在考虑分隔符的情况下应用于每一种可能的展开次数。这意味"
"着："

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1744
msgid ""
"If the repetition includes a separator, that separator must be able to "
"follow the contents of the repetition."
msgstr "如果重复包含分隔符，则该分隔符必须能够跟随在重复内容之后。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1745
msgid ""
"If the repetition can repeat multiple times (`*` or `+`), then the contents "
"must be able to follow themselves."
msgstr "如果重复可以重复多次（`*` 或 `+`），则其内容必须能够跟随其自身。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1746
msgid ""
"The contents of the repetition must be able to follow whatever comes before, "
"and whatever comes after must be able to follow the contents of the "
"repetition."
msgstr ""
"重复的内容必须能够跟随在其前面的任何内容之后，而其后面的任何内容也必须能够跟"
"随在重复内容之后。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1747
msgid ""
"If the repetition can match zero times (`*` or `?`), then whatever comes "
"after must be able to follow whatever comes before."
msgstr ""
"如果重复可以匹配零次（`*` 或 `?`），则其后面的任何内容必须能够跟随在其前面的"
"任何内容之后。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:1749
msgid "For more detail, see the [formal specification](macro-ambiguity.md)."
msgstr "更多细节见[形式化规约](macro-ambiguity.md)。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:11
msgid ""
"_Procedural macros_ allow creating syntax extensions as execution of a "
"function. Procedural macros come in one of three flavors:"
msgstr "<em>过程宏</em>允许通过执行函数来创建语法扩展。过程宏有以下三种形式："

#: src/procedural-macros.md:13
msgid "[Function-like macros](#the-proc_macro-attribute) - `custom!(...)`"
msgstr "[类函数宏](#the-proc_macro-attribute) - `custom!(...)`"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:14
msgid ""
"[Derive macros](procedural-macros.md#r-macro.proc.derive) - "
"`#[derive(CustomDerive)]`"
msgstr ""
"[derive 宏](procedural-macros.md#r-macro.proc.derive) - "
"`#[derive(CustomDerive)]`"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:15
msgid ""
"[Attribute macros](#the-proc_macro_attribute-attribute) - "
"`#[CustomAttribute]`"
msgstr "[属性宏](#the-proc_macro_attribute-attribute) - `#[CustomAttribute]`"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:17
msgid ""
"Procedural macros allow you to run code at compile time that operates over "
"Rust syntax, both consuming and producing Rust syntax. You can sort of think "
"of procedural macros as functions from an AST to another AST."
msgstr ""
"过程宏允许你在编译时运行操作 Rust 语法的代码，既消费 Rust 语法，也产生 Rust "
"语法。可以大致将过程宏看作从一个 AST 到另一个 AST 的函数。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:23
msgid ""
"Procedural macros must be defined in the root of a crate with the [crate "
"type](linkage.md) of `proc-macro`. The macros may not be used from the crate "
"where they are defined, and can only be used when imported in another crate."
msgstr ""
"过程宏必须定义在 [crate 类型](linkage.md)为 `proc-macro` 的 crate 根。这些宏"
"不得在定义它们的 crate 中使用，并且只能在另一个 crate 中导入后使用。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:29
msgid ""
"When using Cargo, Procedural macro crates are defined with the `proc-macro` "
"key in your manifest:"
msgstr "使用 Cargo 时，过程宏 crate 通过清单中的 `proc-macro` 键定义："

#: src/procedural-macros.md:43
msgid ""
"As functions, they must either return syntax, panic, or loop endlessly. "
"Returned syntax either replaces or adds the syntax depending on the kind of "
"procedural macro. Panics are caught by the compiler and are turned into a "
"compiler error. Endless loops are not caught by the compiler which hangs the "
"compiler."
msgstr ""
"作为函数，它们必须返回语法、panic，或者无限循环。返回的语法会根据过程宏的种类"
"替换或添加语法。panic 会被编译器捕获并转换为编译器错误。无限循环不会被编译器"
"捕获，从而会使编译器挂起。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:45
msgid ""
"Procedural macros run during compilation, and thus have the same resources "
"that the compiler has. For example, standard input, error, and output are "
"the same that the compiler has access to. Similarly, file access is the "
"same. Because of this, procedural macros have the same security concerns "
"that [Cargo's build scripts](../cargo/reference/build-scripts.html) have."
msgstr ""
"过程宏在编译期间运行，因此拥有与编译器相同的资源。例如，标准输入、标准错误和"
"标准输出与编译器可访问的是同一组资源。类似地，文件访问也是相同的。因此，过程"
"宏具有与 [Cargo 的构建脚本](../cargo/reference/build-scripts.html)相同的安全"
"隐患。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:51
msgid ""
"Procedural macros have two ways of reporting errors. The first is to panic. "
"The second is to emit a [`compile_error`](../core/macro.compile_error.html) "
"macro invocation."
msgstr ""
"过程宏有两种报告错误的方式。第一种是 panic。第二种是发出 [`compile_error`]"
"(../core/macro.compile_error.html) 宏调用。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:57
msgid "The `proc_macro` crate"
msgstr "`proc_macro` crate"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:63
msgid ""
"Procedural macro crates almost always will link to the compiler-provided "
"[`proc_macro` crate](../proc_macro/index.html). The `proc_macro` crate "
"provides types required for writing procedural macros and facilities to make "
"it easier."
msgstr ""
"过程宏 crate 几乎总是会链接到编译器提供的 [`proc_macro` crate](../proc_macro/"
"index.html)。`proc_macro` crate 提供编写过程宏所需的类型，以及让编写过程宏更"
"容易的工具。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:69
msgid ""
"This crate primarily contains a [`TokenStream`](../proc_macro/"
"struct.TokenStream.html) type. Procedural macros operate over _token "
"streams_ instead of AST nodes, which is a far more stable interface over "
"time for both the compiler and for procedural macros to target. A _token "
"stream_ is roughly equivalent to `Vec<TokenTree>` where a `TokenTree` can "
"roughly be thought of as lexical token. For example `foo` is an `Ident` "
"token, `.` is a `Punct` token, and `1.2` is a `Literal` token. The "
"`TokenStream` type, unlike `Vec<TokenTree>`, is cheap to clone."
msgstr ""
"这个 crate 主要包含 [`TokenStream`](../proc_macro/struct.TokenStream.html) 类"
"型。过程宏操作的是<em>token 流</em>而不是 AST 节点；随着时间推移，对编译器和"
"过程宏而言，token 流都是更稳定得多的目标接口。<em>token 流</em>大致等价于 "
"`Vec<TokenTree>`，其中 `TokenTree` 大致可以看作词法 token。例如，`foo` 是 "
"`Ident` token，`.` 是 `Punct` token，`1.2` 是 `Literal` token。与 "
"`Vec<TokenTree>` 不同，`TokenStream` 类型的克隆成本很低。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:75
msgid ""
"All tokens have an associated `Span`. A `Span` is an opaque value that "
"cannot be modified but can be manufactured. `Span`s represent an extent of "
"source code within a program and are primarily used for error reporting. "
"While you cannot modify a `Span` itself, you can always change the `Span` "
"_associated_ with any token, such as through getting a `Span` from another "
"token."
msgstr ""
"所有 token 都有关联的 `Span`。`Span` 是一个不能被修改但可以被构造的不透明值。"
"`Span` 表示程序中一段源代码的范围，主要用于错误报告。虽然你不能修改 `Span` 本"
"身，但始终可以更改与任何 token <em>关联</em>的 `Span`，例如通过从另一个 "
"token 获取 `Span` 来更改。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:81
msgid "Procedural macro hygiene"
msgstr "过程宏卫生性"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:83
msgid ""
"Procedural macros are _unhygienic_. This means they behave as if the output "
"token stream was simply written inline to the code it's next to. This means "
"that it's affected by external items and also affects external imports."
msgstr ""
"过程宏是<em>非卫生的</em>。这意味着它们的行为就像输出 token 流被直接内联写入"
"其旁边的代码一样。这意味着它会受到外部项的影响，也会影响外部导入。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:85
msgid ""
"Macro authors need to be careful to ensure their macros work in as many "
"contexts as possible given this limitation. This often includes using "
"absolute paths to items in libraries (for example, `::std::option::Option` "
"instead of `Option`) or by ensuring that generated functions have names that "
"are unlikely to clash with other functions (like `__internal_foo` instead of "
"`foo`)."
msgstr ""
"在这种限制下，宏作者需要谨慎地确保他们的宏能在尽可能多的上下文中工作。这通常"
"包括对库中的项使用绝对路径（例如使用 `::std::option::Option` 而不是 "
"`Option`），或者确保生成的函数具有不太可能与其他函数冲突的名称（例如使用 "
"`__internal_foo` 而不是 `foo`）。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:93
msgid "The `proc_macro` attribute"
msgstr "`proc_macro` 属性"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:99
msgid ""
"The _`proc_macro` [attribute](attributes.md)_ defines a [function-like]"
"(macros.md#r-macro.invocation) procedural macro."
msgstr ""
"<em>`proc_macro` [属性](attributes.md)</em>定义一个[类函数](macros.md#r-"
"macro.invocation)过程宏。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:105
msgid ""
"This macro definition ignores its input and emits a function `answer` into "
"its scope."
msgstr "这个宏定义会忽略其输入，并在其作用域中发出一个函数 `answer`。"

