#: src/procedural-macros.md:185
msgid "The `proc_macro_derive` attribute"
msgstr "`proc_macro_derive` 属性"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:191
msgid ""
"Applying the _`proc_macro_derive` [attribute](attributes.md)_ to a function "
"defines a _derive macro_ that can be invoked by the [`derive` attribute]"
"(attributes/derive.md). These macros are given the token stream of a [struct]"
"(items/structs.md), [enum](items/enumerations.md), or [union](items/"
"unions.md) definition and can emit new [items](items.md) after it. They can "
"also declare and use [derive macro helper attributes](#derive-macro-helper-"
"attributes)."
msgstr ""
"将 <em>`proc_macro_derive` [属性](attributes.md)</em>应用于函数，会定义一个可"
"由 [`derive` 属性](attributes/derive.md)调用的 <em>derive 宏</em>。这些宏会得"
"到 [struct](items/structs.md)、[enum](items/enumerations.md) 或 [union]"
"(items/unions.md) 定义的 token 流，并可以在其后发出新的[项](items.md)。它们还"
"可以声明和使用 [derive 宏辅助属性](#derive-macro-helper-attributes)。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:197
msgid ""
"This derive macro ignores its input and appends tokens that define a "
"function."
msgstr "这个 derive 宏会忽略其输入，并追加用于定义一个函数的 token。"

