#: src/attributes.md:986
msgid "Active and inert attributes"
msgstr "活跃属性和惰性属性"

#: src/attributes.md:992
msgid ""
"An attribute is either active or inert. During attribute processing, _active "
"attributes_ remove themselves from the form they are on while _inert "
"attributes_ stay on."
msgstr ""
"属性要么是活跃的，要么是惰性的。在属性处理过程中，_活跃属性_ 会从其所在的形式"
"上移除自身，而 _惰性属性_ 会保留下来。"

#: src/attributes.md:994
msgid ""
"The [`cfg`](conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg-attribute) and [`cfg_attr`]"
"(conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg_attr-attribute) attributes are active. "
"[Attribute macros](procedural-macros.md#the-proc_macro_attribute-attribute) "
"are active. All other attributes are inert."
msgstr ""
"[`cfg`](conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg-attribute) 和 [`cfg_attr`]"
"(conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg_attr-attribute) 属性是活跃的。[属性宏]"
"(procedural-macros.md#the-proc_macro_attribute-attribute)是活跃的。所有其他属"
"性都是惰性的。"

#: src/attributes.md:1000
msgid "Tool attributes"
msgstr "工具属性"

#: src/attributes.md:1006
msgid ""
"The compiler may allow attributes for external tools where each tool resides "
"in its own module in the [tool prelude](names/preludes.md#tool-prelude). The "
"first segment of the attribute path is the name of the tool, with one or "
"more additional segments whose interpretation is up to the tool."
msgstr ""
"编译器可以允许外部工具使用属性，其中每个工具都位于 [tool prelude](names/"
"preludes.md#tool-prelude) 中自己的模块内。属性路径的第一个段是工具名称，后面"
"可以有一个或多个附加段，其解释由工具决定。"

#: src/attributes.md:1012
msgid ""
"When a tool is not in use, the tool's attributes are accepted without a "
"warning. When the tool is in use, the tool is responsible for processing and "
"interpretation of its attributes."
msgstr ""
"未使用某个工具时，该工具的属性会被接受且不发出警告。使用该工具时，该工具负责"
"处理和解释它的属性。"

#: src/attributes.md:1018
msgid ""
"Tool attributes are not available if the [`no_implicit_prelude`](names/"
"preludes.md#the-no_implicit_prelude-attribute) attribute is used."
msgstr ""
"如果使用了 [`no_implicit_prelude`](names/preludes.md#the-no_implicit_prelude-"
"attribute) 属性，则工具属性不可用。"

#: src/attributes.md:1021
msgid "// Tells the rustfmt tool to not format the following element.\n"
msgstr "// 告诉 rustfmt 工具不要格式化以下元素。\n"

#: src/attributes.md:1025
msgid ""
"// Controls the \"cyclomatic complexity\" threshold for the clippy tool.\n"
msgstr "// 控制 clippy 工具的“圈复杂度”阈值。\n"

#: src/attributes.md:1027
msgid "\"100\""
msgstr "\"100\""

#: src/attributes.md:1035
msgid ""
"`rustc` currently recognizes the tools \"clippy\", \"rustfmt\", "
"\"diagnostic\", \"miri\", and \"rust_analyzer\"."
msgstr ""
"`rustc` 目前识别工具 \"clippy\"、\"rustfmt\"、\"diagnostic\"、\"miri\" 和 "
"\"rust_analyzer\"。"

#: src/attributes.md:1044
msgid "Built-in attributes index"
msgstr "内置属性索引"

#: src/attributes.md:1046
msgid "The following is an index of all built-in attributes."
msgstr "以下是所有内置属性的索引。"

#: src/attributes.md:1049
msgid ""
"[`cfg`](conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg-attribute) --- Controls "
"conditional compilation."
msgstr ""
"[`cfg`](conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg-attribute) --- 控制条件编译。"

#: src/attributes.md:1050
msgid ""
"[`cfg_attr`](conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg_attr-attribute) --- "
"Conditionally includes attributes."
msgstr ""
"[`cfg_attr`](conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg_attr-attribute) --- 有条件地"
"包含属性。"

#: src/attributes.md:1053
msgid ""
"[`test`](attributes/testing.md#the-test-attribute) --- Marks a function as a "
"test."
msgstr ""
"[`test`](attributes/testing.md#the-test-attribute) --- 将函数标记为测试。"

#: src/attributes.md:1054
msgid ""
"[`ignore`](attributes/testing.md#the-ignore-attribute) --- Disables a test "
"function."
msgstr ""
"[`ignore`](attributes/testing.md#the-ignore-attribute) --- 禁用测试函数。"

#: src/attributes.md:1055
msgid ""
"[`should_panic`](attributes/testing.md#the-should_panic-attribute) --- "
"Indicates a test should generate a panic."
msgstr ""
"[`should_panic`](attributes/testing.md#the-should_panic-attribute) --- 指示测"
"试应产生 panic。"

#: src/attributes.md:1058
msgid "[`derive`](attributes/derive.md) --- Automatic trait implementations."
msgstr "[`derive`](attributes/derive.md) --- 自动实现 trait。"

#: src/attributes.md:1059
msgid ""
"[`automatically_derived`](attributes/derive.md#the-automatically_derived-"
"attribute) --- Marker for implementations created by `derive`."
msgstr ""
"[`automatically_derived`](attributes/derive.md#the-automatically_derived-"
"attribute) --- 由 `derive` 创建的实现的标记。"

#: src/attributes.md:1062
msgid ""
"[`macro_export`](macros-by-example.md#the-macro_export-attribute) --- "
"Exports a `macro_rules` macro for cross-crate use."
msgstr ""
"[`macro_export`](macros-by-example.md#the-macro_export-attribute) --- 导出 "
"`macro_rules` 宏，以供跨 crate 使用。"

#: src/attributes.md:1063
msgid ""
"[`macro_use`](macros-by-example.md#the-macro_use-attribute) --- Expands "
"macro visibility, or imports macros from other crates."
msgstr ""
"[`macro_use`](macros-by-example.md#the-macro_use-attribute) --- 扩展宏可见"
"性，或从其他 crate 导入宏。"

#: src/attributes.md:1064
msgid ""
"[`proc_macro`](procedural-macros.md#the-proc_macro-attribute) --- Defines a "
"function-like macro."
msgstr ""
"[`proc_macro`](procedural-macros.md#the-proc_macro-attribute) --- 定义类函数"
"宏。"

#: src/attributes.md:1065
msgid ""
"[`proc_macro_derive`](procedural-macros.md#r-macro.proc.derive) --- Defines "
"a derive macro."
msgstr ""
"[`proc_macro_derive`](procedural-macros.md#r-macro.proc.derive) --- 定义派生"
"宏。"

#: src/attributes.md:1066
msgid ""
"[`proc_macro_attribute`](procedural-macros.md#the-proc_macro_attribute-"
"attribute) --- Defines an attribute macro."
msgstr ""
"[`proc_macro_attribute`](procedural-macros.md#the-proc_macro_attribute-"
"attribute) --- 定义属性宏。"

#: src/attributes.md:1069
msgid ""
"[`allow`](attributes/diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`expect`]"
"(attributes/diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`warn`](attributes/"
"diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`deny`](attributes/"
"diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`forbid`](attributes/"
"diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes) --- Alters the default lint level."
msgstr ""
"[`allow`](attributes/diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`expect`]"
"(attributes/diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`warn`](attributes/"
"diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`deny`](attributes/"
"diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`forbid`](attributes/"
"diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes) --- 更改默认 lint 级别。"

#: src/attributes.md:1070
msgid ""
"[`deprecated`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-deprecated-attribute) --- "
"Generates deprecation notices."
msgstr ""
"[`deprecated`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-deprecated-attribute) --- 生成弃"
"用通知。"

#: src/attributes.md:1071
msgid ""
"[`must_use`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-must_use-attribute) --- Generates "
"a lint for unused values."
msgstr ""
"[`must_use`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-must_use-attribute) --- 为未使用的"
"值生成 lint。"

#: src/attributes.md:1072
msgid ""
"[`diagnostic::on_unimplemented`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-"
"diagnosticon_unimplemented-attribute) --- Hints the compiler to emit a "
"certain error message if a trait is not implemented."
msgstr ""
"[`diagnostic::on_unimplemented`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-"
"diagnosticon_unimplemented-attribute) --- 如果某个 trait 未实现，则提示编译器"
"发出特定错误消息。"

#: src/attributes.md:1073
msgid ""
"[`diagnostic::do_not_recommend`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-"
"diagnosticdo_not_recommend-attribute) --- Hints the compiler to not show a "
"certain trait impl in error messages."
msgstr ""
"[`diagnostic::do_not_recommend`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-"
"diagnosticdo_not_recommend-attribute) --- 提示编译器不要在错误消息中显示某个 "
"trait impl。"

#: src/attributes.md:1075
msgid "ABI, linking, symbols, and FFI"
msgstr "ABI、链接、符号和 FFI"

#: src/attributes.md:1076
msgid ""
"[`link`](items/external-blocks.md#the-link-attribute) --- Specifies a native "
"library to link with an `extern` block."
msgstr ""
"[`link`](items/external-blocks.md#the-link-attribute) --- 指定要与 `extern` "
"块链接的原生库。"

#: src/attributes.md:1077
msgid ""
"[`link_name`](items/external-blocks.md#the-link_name-attribute) --- "
"Specifies the name of the symbol for functions or statics in an `extern` "
"block."
msgstr ""
"[`link_name`](items/external-blocks.md#the-link_name-attribute) --- 指定 "
"`extern` 块中函数或静态项的符号名称。"

#: src/attributes.md:1078
msgid ""
"[`link_ordinal`](items/external-blocks.md#the-link_ordinal-attribute) --- "
"Specifies the ordinal of the symbol for functions or statics in an `extern` "
"block."
msgstr ""
"[`link_ordinal`](items/external-blocks.md#the-link_ordinal-attribute) --- 指"
"定 `extern` 块中函数或静态项的符号序号。"

#: src/attributes.md:1079
msgid ""
"[`no_link`](items/extern-crates.md#the-no_link-attribute) --- Prevents "
"linking an extern crate."
msgstr ""
"[`no_link`](items/extern-crates.md#the-no_link-attribute) --- 阻止链接 "
"extern crate。"

#: src/attributes.md:1080
msgid "[`repr`](type-layout.md#representations) --- Controls type layout."
msgstr "[`repr`](type-layout.md#representations) --- 控制类型布局。"

#: src/attributes.md:1081
msgid ""
"[`crate_type`](linkage.md) --- Specifies the type of crate (library, "
"executable, etc.)."
msgstr "[`crate_type`](linkage.md) --- 指定 crate 的类型（库、可执行文件等）。"

#: src/attributes.md:1082
msgid ""
"[`no_main`](crates-and-source-files.md#the-no_main-attribute) --- Disables "
"emitting the `main` symbol."
msgstr ""
"[`no_main`](crates-and-source-files.md#the-no_main-attribute) --- 禁用发出 "
"`main` 符号。"

#: src/attributes.md:1083
msgid ""
"[`export_name`](abi.md#the-export_name-attribute) --- Specifies the exported "
"symbol name for a function or static."
msgstr ""
"[`export_name`](abi.md#the-export_name-attribute) --- 指定函数或静态项的导出"
"符号名称。"

#: src/attributes.md:1084
msgid ""
"[`link_section`](abi.md#the-link_section-attribute) --- Specifies the "
"section of an object file to use for a function or static."
msgstr ""
"[`link_section`](abi.md#the-link_section-attribute) --- 指定函数或静态项要使"
"用的目标文件节。"

#: src/attributes.md:1085
msgid ""
"[`no_mangle`](abi.md#the-no_mangle-attribute) --- Disables symbol name "
"encoding."
msgstr "[`no_mangle`](abi.md#the-no_mangle-attribute) --- 禁用符号名称编码。"

#: src/attributes.md:1086
msgid ""
"[`used`](abi.md#the-used-attribute) --- Forces the compiler to keep a static "
"item in the output object file."
msgstr ""
"[`used`](abi.md#the-used-attribute) --- 强制编译器在输出目标文件中保留静态"
"项。"

#: src/attributes.md:1087
msgid ""
"[`crate_name`](crates-and-source-files.md#the-crate_name-attribute) --- "
"Specifies the crate name."
msgstr ""
"[`crate_name`](crates-and-source-files.md#the-crate_name-attribute) --- 指定 "
"crate 名称。"

#: src/attributes.md:1090
msgid ""
"[`inline`](attributes/codegen.md#the-inline-attribute) --- Hint to inline "
"code."
msgstr ""
"[`inline`](attributes/codegen.md#the-inline-attribute) --- 提示内联代码。"

#: src/attributes.md:1091
msgid ""
"[`cold`](attributes/codegen.md#the-cold-attribute) --- Hint that a function "
"is unlikely to be called."
msgstr ""
"[`cold`](attributes/codegen.md#the-cold-attribute) --- 提示某函数不太可能被调"
"用。"

#: src/attributes.md:1092
msgid ""
"[`naked`](attributes/codegen.md#the-naked-attribute) --- Prevent the "
"compiler from emitting a function prologue and epilogue."
msgstr ""
"[`naked`](attributes/codegen.md#the-naked-attribute) --- 防止编译器发出函数序"
"言和尾声。"

#: src/attributes.md:1093
msgid ""
"[`no_builtins`](attributes/codegen.md#the-no_builtins-attribute) --- "
"Disables use of certain built-in functions."
msgstr ""
"[`no_builtins`](attributes/codegen.md#the-no_builtins-attribute) --- 禁用某些"
"内置函数的使用。"

#: src/attributes.md:1094
msgid ""
"[`target_feature`](attributes/codegen.md#the-target_feature-attribute) --- "
"Configure platform-specific code generation."
msgstr ""
"[`target_feature`](attributes/codegen.md#the-target_feature-attribute) --- 配"
"置平台特定的代码生成。"

#: src/attributes.md:1095
msgid ""
"[`track_caller`](attributes/codegen.md#the-track_caller-attribute) --- Pass "
"the parent call location to `std::panic::Location::caller()`."
msgstr ""
"[`track_caller`](attributes/codegen.md#the-track_caller-attribute) --- 将父级"
"调用位置传递给 `std::panic::Location::caller()`。"

#: src/attributes.md:1096
msgid ""
"[`instruction_set`](attributes/codegen.md#the-instruction_set-attribute) --- "
"Specify the instruction set used to generate a function's code."
msgstr ""
"[`instruction_set`](attributes/codegen.md#the-instruction_set-attribute) --- "
"指定用于生成函数代码的指令集。"

#: src/attributes.md:1098
msgid "Documentation"
msgstr "文档"

#: src/attributes.md:1099
msgid ""
"`doc` --- Specifies documentation. See [The Rustdoc Book](../rustdoc/the-doc-"
"attribute.html) for more information. [Doc comments](comments.md#doc-"
"comments) are transformed into `doc` attributes."
msgstr ""
"`doc` --- 指定文档。更多信息见 [The Rustdoc Book](../rustdoc/the-doc-"
"attribute.html)。[文档注释](comments.md#doc-comments)会转换为 `doc` 属性。"

#: src/attributes.md:1102
msgid ""
"[`no_std`](names/preludes.md#the-no_std-attribute) --- Removes std from the "
"prelude."
msgstr ""
"[`no_std`](names/preludes.md#the-no_std-attribute) --- 从 prelude 中移除 "
"std。"

#: src/attributes.md:1103
msgid ""
"[`no_implicit_prelude`](names/preludes.md#the-no_implicit_prelude-attribute) "
"--- Disables prelude lookups within a module."
msgstr ""
"[`no_implicit_prelude`](names/preludes.md#the-no_implicit_prelude-attribute) "
"--- 禁用模块内的 prelude 查找。"

#: src/attributes.md:1106
msgid ""
"[`path`](items/modules.md#the-path-attribute) --- Specifies the filename for "
"a module."
msgstr "[`path`](items/modules.md#the-path-attribute) --- 指定模块的文件名。"

#: src/attributes.md:1109
msgid ""
"[`recursion_limit`](attributes/limits.md#the-recursion_limit-attribute) --- "
"Sets the maximum recursion limit for certain compile-time operations."
msgstr ""
"[`recursion_limit`](attributes/limits.md#the-recursion_limit-attribute) --- "
"设置某些编译期操作的最大递归限制。"

#: src/attributes.md:1110
msgid ""
"[`type_length_limit`](attributes/limits.md#the-type_length_limit-attribute) "
"--- Sets the maximum size of a polymorphic type."
msgstr ""
"[`type_length_limit`](attributes/limits.md#the-type_length_limit-attribute) "
"--- 设置多态类型的最大大小。"

#: src/attributes.md:1112
msgid "Runtime"
msgstr "运行时"

#: src/attributes.md:1113
msgid ""
"[`panic_handler`](panic.md#the-panic_handler-attribute) --- Sets the "
"function to handle panics."
msgstr ""
"[`panic_handler`](panic.md#the-panic_handler-attribute) --- 设置用于处理 "
"panic 的函数。"

#: src/attributes.md:1114
msgid ""
"[`global_allocator`](runtime.md#the-global_allocator-attribute) --- Sets the "
"global memory allocator."
msgstr ""
"[`global_allocator`](runtime.md#the-global_allocator-attribute) --- 设置全局"
"内存分配器。"

#: src/attributes.md:1115
msgid ""
"[`windows_subsystem`](runtime.md#the-windows_subsystem-attribute) --- "
"Specifies the windows subsystem to link with."
msgstr ""
"[`windows_subsystem`](runtime.md#the-windows_subsystem-attribute) --- 指定要"
"链接的 Windows 子系统。"

#: src/attributes.md:1117
msgid "Features"
msgstr "特性"

#: src/attributes.md:1118
msgid ""
"`feature` --- Used to enable unstable or experimental compiler features. See "
"[The Unstable Book](../unstable-book/index.html) for features implemented in "
"`rustc`."
msgstr ""
"`feature` --- 用于启用不稳定或实验性编译器特性。有关 `rustc` 中实现的特性，"
"见 [The Unstable Book](../unstable-book/index.html)。"

#: src/attributes.md:1120
msgid "Type System"
msgstr "类型系统"

#: src/attributes.md:1121
msgid ""
"[`non_exhaustive`](attributes/type_system.md#the-non_exhaustive-attribute) "
"--- Indicate that a type will have more fields/variants added in future."
msgstr ""
"[`non_exhaustive`](attributes/type_system.md#the-non_exhaustive-attribute) "
"--- 指示未来会为类型添加更多字段/变体。"

#: src/attributes.md:1124
msgid ""
"[`debugger_visualizer`](attributes/debugger.md#the-debugger_visualizer-"
"attribute) --- Embeds a file that specifies debugger output for a type."
msgstr ""
"[`debugger_visualizer`](attributes/debugger.md#the-debugger_visualizer-"
"attribute) --- 嵌入一个指定类型调试器输出的文件。"

#: src/attributes.md:1125
msgid ""
"[`collapse_debuginfo`](attributes/debugger.md#the-collapse_debuginfo-"
"attribute) --- Controls how macro invocations are encoded in debuginfo."
msgstr ""
"[`collapse_debuginfo`](attributes/debugger.md#the-collapse_debuginfo-"
"attribute) --- 控制宏调用如何编码到 debuginfo 中。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:5
msgid "Testing attributes"
msgstr "测试属性"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:7
msgid ""
"The following [attributes](../attributes.md) are used for specifying "
"functions for performing tests. Compiling a crate in \"test\" mode enables "
"building the test functions along with a test harness for executing the "
"tests. Enabling the test mode also enables the [`test` conditional "
"compilation option](../conditional-compilation.md#test)."
msgstr ""
"以下[属性](../attributes.md)用于指定执行测试的函数。以 \"test\" 模式编译 "
"crate 会启用测试函数的构建，并同时构建用于执行测试的测试框架。启用测试模式也"
"会启用 [`test` 条件编译选项](../conditional-compilation.md#test)。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:17
msgid "The `test` attribute"
msgstr "`test` 属性"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:23
msgid ""
"The _`test` [attribute](../attributes.md)_ marks a function to be executed "
"as a test."
msgstr "_`test` [属性](../attributes.md)_ 将函数标记为要作为测试执行。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:45
msgid ""
"The `test` attribute uses the [MetaWord](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaWord) "
"syntax."
msgstr "`test` 属性使用 [MetaWord](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaWord) 语法。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:51
msgid ""
"The `test` attribute may only be applied to [free functions](../"
"glossary.md#free-item) that are monomorphic, that take no arguments, and "
"where the return type implements the [`Termination`](../../std/process/"
"trait.Termination.html) trait."
msgstr ""
"`test` 属性只能应用于单态、不接受参数且返回类型实现了 [`Termination`](../../"
"std/process/trait.Termination.html) trait 的[自由函数](../glossary.md#free-"
"item)。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:57
msgid ""
"Some of types that implement the [`Termination`](../../std/process/"
"trait.Termination.html) trait include:"
msgstr ""
"实现 [`Termination`](../../std/process/trait.Termination.html) trait 的一些类"
"型包括："

#: src/attributes/testing.md:68
msgid "Only the first use of `test` on a function has effect."
msgstr "在一个函数上，只有第一次使用 `test` 会生效。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:85
msgid ""
"The `test` attribute is exported from the standard library prelude as "
"[`std::prelude::v1::test`](../../core/macros/builtin/attr.test.html)."
msgstr ""
"`test` 属性由标准库 prelude 以 [`std::prelude::v1::test`](../../core/macros/"
"builtin/attr.test.html) 导出。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:91
msgid "These functions are only compiled when in test mode."
msgstr "这些函数只在测试模式下编译。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:97
msgid ""
"The test mode is enabled by passing the `--test` argument to `rustc` or "
"using `cargo test`."
msgstr ""
"通过向 `rustc` 传递 `--test` 参数或使用 `cargo test` 可以启用测试模式。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:106
msgid ""
"The test harness calls the returned value's [`report`](../../std/process/"
"trait.Termination.html#tymethod.report) method, and classifies the test as "
"passed or failed depending on whether the resulting [`ExitCode`](../../std/"
"process/struct.ExitCode.html) represents successful termination. In "
"particular:"
msgstr ""
"测试框架会调用返回值的 [`report`](../../std/process/"
"trait.Termination.html#tymethod.report) 方法，并根据产生的 [`ExitCode`]"
"(../../std/process/struct.ExitCode.html) 是否表示成功终止，将测试归类为通过或"
"失败。具体来说："

#: src/attributes/testing.md:108
msgid "Tests that return `()` pass as long as they terminate and do not panic."
msgstr "返回 `()` 的测试只要会终止且不 panic，就会通过。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:109
msgid ""
"Tests that return a `Result<(), E>` pass as long as they return `Ok(())`."
msgstr "返回 `Result<(), E>` 的测试只要返回 `Ok(())`，就会通过。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:110
msgid ""
"Tests that return `ExitCode::SUCCESS` pass, and tests that return "
"`ExitCode::FAILURE` fail."
msgstr ""
"返回 `ExitCode::SUCCESS` 的测试会通过，而返回 `ExitCode::FAILURE` 的测试会失"
"败。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:111
msgid "Tests that do not terminate neither pass nor fail."
msgstr "不会终止的测试既不通过也不失败。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:123 src/attributes/testing.md:124
msgid "// expected to succeed\n"
msgstr "// expected to succeed\n"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:137
msgid "The `ignore` attribute"
msgstr "`ignore` 属性"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:143
msgid ""
"The _`ignore` [attribute](../attributes.md)_ can be used with the [`test` "
"attribute](testing.md#r-attributes.testing.test) to tell the test harness to "
"not execute that function as a test."
msgstr ""
"_`ignore` [属性](../attributes.md)_ 可以与 [`test` 属性](testing.md#r-"
"attributes.testing.test)一起使用，用来告知测试框架不要将该函数作为测试执行。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:164
msgid ""
"The `rustc` test harness supports the `--include-ignored` flag to force "
"ignored tests to be run."
msgstr ""
"`rustc` 测试框架支持 `--include-ignored` 标志，用于强制运行被忽略的测试。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:173
msgid ""
"The `ignore` attribute uses the [MetaWord](../attributes.md#grammar-"
"MetaWord) and [MetaNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaNameValueStr) "
"syntaxes."
msgstr ""
"`ignore` 属性使用 [MetaWord](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaWord) 和 "
"[MetaNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaNameValueStr) 语法。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:179
msgid ""
"The [MetaNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaNameValueStr) form of "
"the `ignore` attribute provides a way to specify a reason why the test is "
"ignored."
msgstr ""
"`ignore` 属性的 [MetaNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-"
"MetaNameValueStr) 形式提供了一种指定测试被忽略原因的方式。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:187
msgid "\"not yet implemented\""
msgstr "\"not yet implemented\""

#: src/attributes/testing.md:200
msgid ""
"The `ignore` attribute may only be applied to functions annotated with the "
"`test` attribute."
msgstr "`ignore` 属性只能应用于以 `test` 属性标注的函数。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:215
msgid "Only the first use of `ignore` on a function has effect."
msgstr "在一个函数上，只有第一次使用 `ignore` 会生效。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:230
msgid ""
"Ignored tests are still compiled when in test mode, but they are not "
"executed."
msgstr "在测试模式下，被忽略的测试仍会被编译，但不会被执行。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:237
msgid "The `should_panic` attribute"
msgstr "`should_panic` 属性"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:243
msgid ""
"The _`should_panic` [attribute](../attributes.md)_ causes a test to pass "
"only if the [test function](testing.md#r-attributes.testing.test) to which "
"the attribute is applied panics."
msgstr ""
"_`should_panic` [属性](../attributes.md)_ 使测试仅在应用该属性的[测试函数]"
"(testing.md#r-attributes.testing.test) panic 时通过。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:251 src/attributes/testing.md:253
msgid "\"values don't match\""
msgstr "\"values don't match\""

#: src/attributes/testing.md:264
msgid "The `should_panic` attribute has these forms:"
msgstr "`should_panic` 属性有以下形式："

#: src/attributes/testing.md:266
msgid "[MetaWord](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaWord)"
msgstr "[MetaWord](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaWord)"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:274 src/attributes/testing.md:288
#: src/attributes/testing.md:302
msgid "\"error: some message, and more\""
msgstr "\"error: some message, and more\""

#: src/attributes/testing.md:280
msgid ""
"[MetaNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaNameValueStr) --- The given "
"string must appear within the panic message for the test to pass."
msgstr ""
"[MetaNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaNameValueStr) --- 给定字符串"
"必须出现在 panic 消息中，测试才会通过。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:287 src/attributes/testing.md:301
msgid "\"some message\""
msgstr "\"some message\""

#: src/attributes/testing.md:294
msgid ""
"[MetaListNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaListNameValueStr) --- As "
"with the [MetaNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaNameValueStr) "
"syntax, the given string must appear within the panic message."
msgstr ""
"[MetaListNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaListNameValueStr) --- 与 "
"[MetaNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaNameValueStr) 语法一样，给定"
"字符串必须出现在 panic 消息中。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:312
msgid ""
"The `should_panic` attribute may only be applied to functions annotated with "
"the `test` attribute."
msgstr "`should_panic` 属性只能应用于以 `test` 属性标注的函数。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:327
msgid "Only the first use of `should_panic` on a function has effect."
msgstr "在一个函数上，只有第一次使用 `should_panic` 会生效。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:342
msgid ""
"When the [MetaNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaNameValueStr) form "
"or the [MetaListNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaListNameValueStr) "
"form with the `expected` key is used, the given string must appear somewhere "
"within the panic message for the test to pass."
msgstr ""
"使用 [MetaNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaNameValueStr) 形式，或使"
"用带有 `expected` 键的 [MetaListNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-"
"MetaListNameValueStr) 形式时，给定字符串必须出现在 panic 消息中的某处，测试才"
"会通过。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:348
msgid "The return type of the test function must be `()`."
msgstr "测试函数的返回类型必须是 `()`。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:12
msgid ""
"The _`derive` [attribute](../attributes.md#r-attributes)_ invokes one or "
"more [derive macros](../procedural-macros.md#r-macro.proc.derive), allowing "
"new [items](../items.md) to be automatically generated for data structures. "
"You can create `derive` macros with [procedural macros](../procedural-"
"macros.md#r-macro.proc.derive)."
msgstr ""
"_`derive` [属性](../attributes.md#r-attributes)_ 会调用一个或多个[派生宏](../"
"procedural-macros.md#r-macro.proc.derive)，允许为数据结构自动生成新的[项](../"
"items.md)。可以使用[过程宏](../procedural-macros.md#r-macro.proc.derive)创建 "
"`derive` 宏。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:18
msgid ""
"The [`PartialEq`](../../core/cmp/derive.PartialEq.html) derive macro emits "
"an [implementation](../items/implementations.md) of [`PartialEq`](../../core/"
"cmp/trait.PartialEq.html) for `Foo<T> where T: PartialEq`. The [`Clone`]"
"(../../core/clone/derive.Clone.html) derive macro does likewise for [`Clone`]"
"(../../core/clone/trait.Clone.html)."
msgstr ""
"[`PartialEq`](../../core/cmp/derive.PartialEq.html) 派生宏会为 `Foo<T> where "
"T: PartialEq` 生成 [`PartialEq`](../../core/cmp/trait.PartialEq.html) 的[实"
"现](../items/implementations.md)。[`Clone`](../../core/clone/"
"derive.Clone.html) 派生宏同样会为 [`Clone`](../../core/clone/"
"trait.Clone.html) 生成相应实现。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:28
msgid "The generated `impl` items are equivalent to:"
msgstr "生成的 `impl` 项等价于："

#: src/attributes/derive.md:52
msgid ""
"The `derive` attribute uses the [MetaListPaths](../attributes.md#grammar-"
"MetaListPaths) syntax to specify a list of paths to [derive macros](../"
"procedural-macros.md#r-macro.proc.derive) to invoke."
msgstr ""
"`derive` 属性使用 [MetaListPaths](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaListPaths) 语"
"法来指定要调用的[派生宏](../procedural-macros.md#r-macro.proc.derive)路径列"
"表。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:58
msgid ""
"The `derive` attribute may only be applied to [structs](../items/"
"structs.md#r-items.struct), [enums](../items/enumerations.md#r-items.enum), "
"and [unions](../items/unions.md#r-items.union)."
msgstr ""
"`derive` 属性只能应用于 [struct](../items/structs.md#r-items.struct)、[enum]"
"(../items/enumerations.md#r-items.enum) 和 [union](../items/unions.md#r-"
"items.union)。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:64
msgid ""
"The `derive` attribute may be used any number of times on an item. All "
"derive macros listed in all attributes are invoked."
msgstr ""
"`derive` 属性可以在一个项上使用任意次数。所有属性中列出的全部派生宏都会被调"
"用。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:70
msgid "The `derive` attribute is exported in the standard library as:"
msgstr "`derive` 属性在标准库中以下列名称导出："

#: src/attributes/derive.md:72
msgid "[`core::derive`](../../core/macros/builtin/attr.derive.html)"
msgstr "[`core::derive`](../../core/macros/builtin/attr.derive.html)"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:73
msgid "[`std::derive`](../../core/macros/builtin/attr.derive.html)"
msgstr "[`std::derive`](../../core/macros/builtin/attr.derive.html)"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:74
msgid ""
"[`core::prelude::v1::derive`](../../core/macros/builtin/attr.derive.html)"
msgstr ""
"[`core::prelude::v1::derive`](../../core/macros/builtin/attr.derive.html)"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:75
msgid ""
"[`std::prelude::v1::derive`](../../core/macros/builtin/attr.derive.html)"
msgstr ""
"[`std::prelude::v1::derive`](../../core/macros/builtin/attr.derive.html)"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:81
msgid ""
"Built-in derives are defined in the [language prelude](../names/"
"preludes.md#r-names.preludes.lang). The list of built-in derives are:"
msgstr ""
"内置派生定义在[语言 prelude](../names/preludes.md#r-names.preludes.lang) 中。"
"内置派生的列表如下："

#: src/attributes/derive.md:83
msgid "[`Clone`](../../core/clone/trait.Clone.html)"
msgstr "[`Clone`](../../core/clone/trait.Clone.html)"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:84
msgid "[`Copy`](../../core/marker/trait.Copy.html)"
msgstr "[`Copy`](../../core/marker/trait.Copy.html)"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:85
msgid "[`Debug`](../../core/fmt/macros/derive.Debug.html)"
msgstr "[`Debug`](../../core/fmt/macros/derive.Debug.html)"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:86
msgid "[`Default`](../../core/default/trait.Default.html)"
msgstr "[`Default`](../../core/default/trait.Default.html)"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:87
msgid "[`Eq`](../../core/cmp/trait.Eq.html)"
msgstr "[`Eq`](../../core/cmp/trait.Eq.html)"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:88
msgid "[`Hash`](../../core/hash/macros/derive.Hash.html)"
msgstr "[`Hash`](../../core/hash/macros/derive.Hash.html)"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:89
msgid "[`Ord`](../../core/cmp/trait.Ord.html)"
msgstr "[`Ord`](../../core/cmp/trait.Ord.html)"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:90
msgid "[`PartialEq`](../../core/cmp/trait.PartialEq.html)"
msgstr "[`PartialEq`](../../core/cmp/trait.PartialEq.html)"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:91
msgid "[`PartialOrd`](../../core/cmp/trait.PartialOrd.html)"
msgstr "[`PartialOrd`](../../core/cmp/trait.PartialOrd.html)"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:97
msgid ""
"The built-in derives include the [`automatically_derived` attribute]"
"(derive.md#r-attributes.derive.automatically_derived) on the implementations "
"they generate."
msgstr ""
"内置派生会在它们生成的实现上包含 [`automatically_derived` 属性](derive.md#r-"
"attributes.derive.automatically_derived)。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:103
msgid ""
"During macro expansion, for each element in the list of derives, the "
"corresponding derive macro expands to zero or more [items](../items.md)."
msgstr ""
"在宏展开期间，对于派生列表中的每个元素，相应的派生宏会展开为零个或多个[项]"
"(../items.md)。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:110
msgid "The `automatically_derived` attribute"
msgstr "`automatically_derived` 属性"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:116
msgid ""
"The _`automatically_derived` [attribute](../attributes.md#r-attributes)_ is "
"used to annotate an [implementation](../items/implementations.md) to "
"indicate that it was automatically created by a [derive macro](../procedural-"
"macros.md#r-macro.proc.derive). It has no direct effect, but it may be used "
"by tools and diagnostic lints to detect these automatically generated "
"implementations."
msgstr ""
"_`automatically_derived` [属性](../attributes.md#r-attributes)_ 用于标注[实"
"现](../items/implementations.md)，以表明该实现是由[派生宏](../procedural-"
"macros.md#r-macro.proc.derive)自动创建的。它没有直接效果，但工具和诊断 lint "
"可以使用它来检测这些自动生成的实现。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:122
msgid ""
"Given [`#[derive(Clone)]`](../../core/clone/derive.Clone.html) on `struct "
"Example`, the [derive macro](../procedural-macros.md#r-macro.proc.derive) "
"may produce:"
msgstr ""
"给定 `struct Example` 上的 [`#[derive(Clone)]`](../../core/clone/"
"derive.Clone.html)，[派生宏](../procedural-macros.md#r-macro.proc.derive)可以"
"生成："

#: src/attributes/derive.md:142
msgid ""
"The `automatically_derived` attribute uses the [MetaWord](../"
"attributes.md#grammar-MetaWord) syntax."
msgstr ""
"`automatically_derived` 属性使用 [MetaWord](../attributes.md#grammar-"
"MetaWord) 语法。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:148
msgid ""
"The `automatically_derived` attribute may only be applied to an "
"[implementation](../items/implementations.md)."
msgstr ""
"`automatically_derived` 属性只能应用于[实现](../items/implementations.md)。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:163
msgid ""
"Using `automatically_derived` more than once on an implementation has the "
"same effect as using it once."
msgstr "在一个实现上多次使用 `automatically_derived` 与使用一次具有相同效果。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:178
msgid "The `automatically_derived` attribute has no behavior."
msgstr "`automatically_derived` 属性没有任何行为。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:5
msgid "Diagnostic attributes"
msgstr "诊断属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:7
msgid ""
"The following [attributes](../attributes.md) are used for controlling or "
"generating diagnostic messages during compilation."
msgstr "以下[属性](../attributes.md)用于在编译期间控制或生成诊断消息。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:14
msgid "Lint check attributes"
msgstr "Lint 检查属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:16
msgid ""
"A lint check names a potentially undesirable coding pattern, such as "
"unreachable code or omitted documentation."
msgstr "lint 检查命名一种可能不合需要的编码模式，例如不可达代码或缺失文档。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:23
msgid ""
"The lint attributes `allow`, `expect`, `warn`, `deny`, and `forbid` use the "
"[MetaListPaths](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaListPaths) syntax to specify a "
"list of lint names to change the lint level for the entity to which the "
"attribute applies."
msgstr ""
"`allow`、`expect`、`warn`、`deny` 和 `forbid` 这些 lint 属性使用 "
"[MetaListPaths](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaListPaths) 语法来指定 lint 名称"
"列表，以更改该属性所适用实体的 lint 级别。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:28
msgid "For any lint check `C`:"
msgstr "对于任意 lint 检查 `C`："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:34
msgid ""
"`#[allow(C)]` overrides the check for `C` so that violations will go "
"unreported."
msgstr "`#[allow(C)]` 会覆盖对 `C` 的检查，使违规不会被报告。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:41
msgid ""
"`#[expect(C)]` indicates that lint `C` is expected to be emitted. The "
"attribute will suppress the emission of `C` or issue a warning, if the "
"expectation is unfulfilled."
msgstr ""
"`#[expect(C)]` 表示预期会发出 lint `C`。该属性会抑制 `C` 的发出；如果期望未满"
"足，则会发出警告。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:49
msgid "`#[warn(C)]` warns about violations of `C` but continues compilation."
msgstr "`#[warn(C)]` 会对 `C` 的违规发出警告，但继续编译。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:55
msgid "`#[deny(C)]` signals an error after encountering a violation of `C`,"
msgstr "`#[deny(C)]` 在遇到 `C` 的违规后发出错误，"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:61
msgid ""
"`#[forbid(C)]` is the same as `deny(C)`, but also forbids changing the lint "
"level afterwards,"
msgstr "`#[forbid(C)]` 与 `deny(C)` 相同，但还禁止之后更改 lint 级别，"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:68
msgid ""
"The lint checks supported by `rustc` can be found via `rustc -W help`, along "
"with their default settings and are documented in the [rustc book](../../"
"rustc/lints/index.html)."
msgstr ""
"`rustc` 支持的 lint 检查及其默认设置可通过 `rustc -W help` 查看，并记录在 "
"[rustc book](../../rustc/lints/index.html) 中。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:75 src/attributes/diagnostics.md:107
msgid "// Missing documentation is ignored here\n"
msgstr "// 此处会忽略缺失文档\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:79 src/attributes/diagnostics.md:116
msgid "// Missing documentation signals a warning here\n"
msgstr "// 此处缺失文档会发出警告\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:83
msgid "// Missing documentation signals an error here\n"
msgstr "// 此处缺失文档会发出错误\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:93
msgid ""
"Lint attributes can override the level specified from a previous attribute, "
"as long as the level does not attempt to change a forbidden lint (except for "
"`deny`, which is allowed inside a `forbid` context, but ignored). Previous "
"attributes are those from a higher level in the syntax tree, or from a "
"previous attribute on the same entity as listed in left-to-right source "
"order."
msgstr ""
"只要该级别不会试图更改已被 `forbid` 的 lint（`deny` 例外，它在 `forbid` 上下"
"文内允许使用，但会被忽略），lint 属性就可以覆盖先前属性指定的级别。先前属性是"
"指语法树中更高层级的属性，或同一实体上按源码从左到右顺序列出的较早属性。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:99
msgid ""
"This example shows how one can use `allow` and `warn` to toggle a particular "
"check on and off:"
msgstr "此示例展示如何使用 `allow` 和 `warn` 开关某个特定检查："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:110
msgid ""
"// Missing documentation signals a warning here,\n"
"        // despite the allow above.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此处缺失文档会发出警告，\n"
"        // 尽管上方有 allow。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:121
msgid ""
"This example shows how one can use `forbid` to disallow uses of `allow` or "
"`expect` for that lint check:"
msgstr ""
"此示例展示如何使用 `forbid` 来禁止为该 lint 检查使用 `allow` 或 `expect`："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:127
msgid "// Attempting to toggle warning signals an error here\n"
msgstr "// 试图切换警告级别会在此处发出错误\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:129
msgid "/// Returns 2.\n"
msgstr "/// 返回 2。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:138
msgid ""
"`rustc` allows setting lint levels on the [command-line](../../rustc/lints/"
"levels.html#via-compiler-flag), and also supports [setting caps](../../rustc/"
"lints/levels.html#capping-lints) on the lints that are reported."
msgstr ""
"`rustc` 允许在[命令行](../../rustc/lints/levels.html#via-compiler-flag)上设"
"置 lint 级别，也支持对已报告的 lint [设置上限](../../rustc/lints/"
"levels.html#capping-lints)。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:147
msgid "Lint reasons"
msgstr "Lint 原因"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:149
msgid ""
"All lint attributes support an additional `reason` parameter, to give "
"context why a certain attribute was added. This reason will be displayed as "
"part of the lint message if the lint is emitted at the defined level."
msgstr ""
"所有 lint 属性都支持额外的 `reason` 参数，用于说明添加某个属性的上下文。如果"
"该 lint 按定义的级别发出，此原因会作为 lint 消息的一部分显示。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:154
msgid ""
"// `keyword_idents` is allowed by default. Here we deny it to\n"
"// avoid migration of identifiers when we update the edition.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 默认允许 `keyword_idents`。这里将其设为 deny，\n"
"// 以避免更新 edition 时迁移标识符。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:158
msgid "\"we want to avoid these idents to be future compatible\""
msgstr "\"we want to avoid these idents to be future compatible\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:160
msgid ""
"// This name was allowed in Rust's 2015 edition. We still aim to avoid\n"
"// this to be future compatible and not confuse end users.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此名称在 Rust 2015 edition 中是允许的。我们仍希望避免\n"
"// 这样做，以保持未来兼容性并避免困惑最终用户。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:166
msgid "Here is another example, where the lint is allowed with a reason:"
msgstr "这里还有一个示例，其中 lint 带有原因地被允许："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:172
msgid ""
"// The `reason` parameter on `allow` attributes acts as documentation for "
"the reader.\n"
msgstr "// `allow` 属性上的 `reason` 参数充当给读者看的文档。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:173
msgid "\"this is only modified on some platforms\""
msgstr "\"this is only modified on some platforms\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:174
msgid "\"git\""
msgstr "\"git\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:177
msgid "\"exe\""
msgstr "\"exe\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:187
msgid "The `#[expect]` attribute"
msgstr "`#[expect]` 属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:193
msgid ""
"The `#[expect(C)]` attribute creates a lint expectation for lint `C`. The "
"expectation will be fulfilled, if a `#[warn(C)]` attribute at the same "
"location would result in a lint emission. If the expectation is unfulfilled, "
"because lint `C` would not be emitted, the `unfulfilled_lint_expectations` "
"lint will be emitted at the attribute."
msgstr ""
"`#[expect(C)]` 属性会为 lint `C` 创建一个 lint 期望。如果同一位置的 "
"`#[warn(C)]` 属性会导致 lint 发出，则该期望会被满足。如果由于 lint `C` 不会被"
"发出而导致期望未满足，则会在该属性处发出 `unfulfilled_lint_expectations` "
"lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:201
msgid ""
"// This `#[expect]` attribute creates a lint expectation, that the "
"`unused_variables`\n"
"    // lint would be emitted by the following statement. This expectation "
"is\n"
"    // unfulfilled, since the `question` variable is used by the `println!` "
"macro.\n"
"    // Therefore, the `unfulfilled_lint_expectations` lint will be emitted "
"at the\n"
"    // attribute.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此 `#[expect]` 属性创建一个 lint 期望，即以下语句会发出\n"
"    // `unused_variables` lint。由于 `question` 变量被 `println!` 宏使用，\n"
"    // 此期望未满足。因此，会在该属性处发出\n"
"    // `unfulfilled_lint_expectations` lint。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:207
msgid "\"who lives in a pineapple under the sea?\""
msgstr "\"who lives in a pineapple under the sea?\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:208
msgid "\"{question}\""
msgstr "\"{question}\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:210
msgid ""
"// This `#[expect]` attribute creates a lint expectation that will be "
"fulfilled, since\n"
"    // the `answer` variable is never used. The `unused_variables` lint, "
"that would usually\n"
"    // be emitted, is suppressed. No warning will be issued for the "
"statement or attribute.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此 `#[expect]` 属性创建一个会被满足的 lint 期望，因为\n"
"    // `answer` 变量从未被使用。通常会发出的 `unused_variables` lint\n"
"    // 会被抑制。该语句或属性不会产生警告。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:214
msgid "\"SpongeBob SquarePants!\""
msgstr "\"SpongeBob SquarePants!\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:222
msgid ""
"The lint expectation is only fulfilled by lint emissions which have been "
"suppressed by the `expect` attribute. If the lint level is modified in the "
"scope with other level attributes like `allow` or `warn`, the lint emission "
"will be handled accordingly and the expectation will remain unfulfilled."
msgstr ""
"lint 期望只会由已被 `expect` 属性抑制的 lint 发出满足。如果作用域中的 lint 级"
"别被 `allow` 或 `warn` 等其他级别属性修改，则该 lint 发出会按相应方式处理，而"
"该期望仍保持未满足。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:230
msgid ""
"// This will emit the `unused_variables` lint at the warn level\n"
"    // as defined by the `warn` attribute. This will not fulfill the\n"
"    // expectation above the function.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这会按 `warn` 属性定义，以 warn 级别发出 `unused_variables` lint。\n"
"    // 这不会满足函数上方的期望。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:234
msgid "\"Crab Rave\""
msgstr "\"Crab Rave\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:236
msgid ""
"// The `allow` attribute suppresses the lint emission. This will not\n"
"    // fulfill the expectation as it has been suppressed by the `allow`\n"
"    // attribute and not the `expect` attribute above the function.\n"
msgstr ""
"// `allow` 属性会抑制 lint 发出。这不会满足期望，\n"
"    // 因为它是被 `allow` 属性抑制的，而不是被函数上方的\n"
"    // `expect` 属性抑制的。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:240
msgid "\"Noisestorm\""
msgstr "\"Noisestorm\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:242
msgid ""
"// This `expect` attribute will suppress the `unused_variables` lint "
"emission\n"
"    // at the variable. The `expect` attribute above the function will still "
"not\n"
"    // be fulfilled, since this lint emission has been suppressed by the "
"local\n"
"    // expect attribute.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此 `expect` 属性会在变量处抑制 `unused_variables` lint 的发出。\n"
"    // 函数上方的 `expect` 属性仍不会被满足，\n"
"    // 因为此 lint 发出已被局部 `expect` 属性抑制。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:247
msgid "\"Monstercat Release\""
msgstr "\"Monstercat Release\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:255
msgid ""
"If the `expect` attribute contains several lints, each one is expected "
"separately. For a lint group it's enough if one lint inside the group has "
"been emitted:"
msgstr ""
"如果 `expect` 属性包含多个 lint，则会分别对每个 lint 建立期望。对于 lint 组，"
"只要组内有一个 lint 已被发出就足够了："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:259
msgid ""
"// This expectation will be fulfilled by the unused value inside the "
"function\n"
"// since the emitted `unused_variables` lint is inside the `unused` lint "
"group.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此期望会由函数内部的未使用值满足，\n"
"// 因为发出的 `unused_variables` lint 属于 `unused` lint 组。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:263
msgid "\"I'm running out of examples\""
msgstr "\"I'm running out of examples\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:267
msgid ""
"// This attribute creates two lint expectations. The `unused_mut` lint will "
"be\n"
"    // suppressed and with that fulfill the first expectation. The "
"`unused_variables`\n"
"    // wouldn't be emitted, since the variable is used. That expectation "
"will therefore\n"
"    // be unsatisfied, and a warning will be emitted.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此属性创建两个 lint 期望。`unused_mut` lint 会被\n"
"    // 抑制，并由此满足第一个期望。`unused_variables`\n"
"    // 不会被发出，因为该变量被使用了。因此该期望\n"
"    // 会未满足，并会发出警告。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:272
msgid "\"https://www.rust-lang.org/\""
msgstr "\"https://www.rust-lang.org/\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:274
msgid "\"Welcome to our community: {link}\""
msgstr "\"Welcome to our community: {link}\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:282
msgid ""
"The behavior of `#[expect(unfulfilled_lint_expectations)]` is currently "
"defined to always generate the `unfulfilled_lint_expectations` lint."
msgstr ""
"`#[expect(unfulfilled_lint_expectations)]` 的行为目前定义为始终生成 "
"`unfulfilled_lint_expectations` lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:291
msgid "Lint groups"
msgstr "Lint 组"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:293
msgid ""
"Lints may be organized into named groups so that the level of related lints "
"can be adjusted together. Using a named group is equivalent to listing out "
"the lints within that group."
msgstr ""
"lint 可以组织成具名组，以便一起调整相关 lint 的级别。使用具名组等价于列出该组"
"内的所有 lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:298
msgid "// This allows all lints in the \"unused\" group.\n"
msgstr "// 这允许 \"unused\" 组中的所有 lint。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:299
msgid ""
"// This overrides the \"unused_must_use\" lint from the \"unused\"\n"
"// group to deny.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这会把 \"unused\" 组中的 \"unused_must_use\" lint\n"
"// 覆盖为 deny。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:304
msgid ""
"// This does not generate a warning because the \"unused_variables\"\n"
"    // lint is in the \"unused\" group.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这不会生成警告，因为 \"unused_variables\"\n"
"    // lint 位于 \"unused\" 组中。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:307
msgid ""
"// This generates an error because the result is unused and\n"
"    // \"unused_must_use\" is marked as \"deny\".\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这会生成错误，因为结果未被使用，且\n"
"    // \"unused_must_use\" 被标记为 \"deny\"。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:309
msgid "\"some_file\""
msgstr "\"some_file\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:309
msgid "// ERROR: unused `Result` that must be used\n"
msgstr "// 错误：未使用必须使用的 `Result`\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:317
msgid ""
"There is a special group named \"warnings\" which includes all lints at the "
"\"warn\" level. The \"warnings\" group ignores attribute order and applies "
"to all lints that would otherwise warn within the entity."
msgstr ""
"有一个名为 \"warnings\" 的特殊组，它包括所有处于 \"warn\" 级别的 lint。"
"\"warnings\" 组会忽略属性顺序，并应用于实体中所有在其他情况下会发出警告的 "
"lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:322
msgid "// The order of these two attributes does not matter.\n"
msgstr "// 这两个属性的顺序并不重要。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:324
msgid "// The unsafe_code lint is normally \"allow\" by default.\n"
msgstr "// unsafe_code lint 通常默认为 \"allow\"。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:328
msgid ""
"// This is an error because the `unsafe_code` warning has\n"
"    // been lifted to \"deny\".\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这是错误，因为 `unsafe_code` 警告已被\n"
"    // 提升到 \"deny\"。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:330
msgid "// ERROR: use of `unsafe` block\n"
msgstr "// 错误：使用 `unsafe` 块\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:338
msgid "Tool lint attributes"
msgstr "工具 lint 属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:344
msgid ""
"Tool lints allows using scoped lints, to `allow`, `warn`, `deny` or `forbid` "
"lints of certain tools."
msgstr ""
"工具 lint 允许使用带作用域的 lint，来对特定工具的 lint 设置 `allow`、`warn`、"
"`deny` 或 `forbid`。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:351
msgid ""
"Tool lints only get checked when the associated tool is active. If a lint "
"attribute, such as `allow`, references a nonexistent tool lint, the compiler "
"will not warn about the nonexistent lint until you use the tool."
msgstr ""
"工具 lint 只有在关联工具处于活动状态时才会被检查。如果 `allow` 等 lint 属性引"
"用了不存在的工具 lint，编译器在你使用该工具之前不会对这个不存在的 lint 发出警"
"告。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:355
msgid "Otherwise, they work just like regular lint attributes:"
msgstr "除此之外，它们的工作方式与常规 lint 属性相同："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:358
msgid "// set the entire `pedantic` clippy lint group to warn\n"
msgstr "// 将整个 `pedantic` clippy lint 组设为 warn\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:359
msgid "// silence warnings from the `filter_map` clippy lint\n"
msgstr "// 静默来自 `filter_map` clippy lint 的警告\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:366
msgid "// silence the `cmp_nan` clippy lint just for this function\n"
msgstr "// 仅对这个函数静默 `cmp_nan` clippy lint\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:378
msgid ""
"`rustc` currently recognizes the tool lints for \"[clippy](https://"
"github.com/rust-lang/rust-clippy)\" and \"[rustdoc](../../rustdoc/lints.html)"
"\"."
msgstr ""
"`rustc` 目前识别 \"[clippy](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-clippy)\" 和 "
"\"[rustdoc](../../rustdoc/lints.html)\" 的工具 lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:387
msgid "The `deprecated` attribute"
msgstr "`deprecated` 属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:393
msgid ""
"The _`deprecated` attribute_ marks an item as deprecated. `rustc` will issue "
"warnings on use of `#[deprecated]` items. `rustdoc` will show item "
"deprecation, including the `since` version and `note`, if available."
msgstr ""
"_`deprecated` 属性_ 将项标记为已弃用。使用 `#[deprecated]` 项时，`rustc` 会发"
"出警告。`rustdoc` 会显示项的弃用信息，包括 `since` 版本和 `note`（如果可"
"用）。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:401
msgid "The `deprecated` attribute has several forms:"
msgstr "`deprecated` 属性有几种形式："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:403
msgid "`deprecated` --- Issues a generic message."
msgstr "`deprecated` --- 发出通用消息。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:404
msgid ""
"`deprecated = \"message\"` --- Includes the given string in the deprecation "
"message."
msgstr "`deprecated = \"message\"` --- 在弃用消息中包含给定字符串。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:406
msgid ""
"[MetaListNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaListNameValueStr) syntax "
"with two optional fields:"
msgstr ""
"带有两个可选字段的 [MetaListNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-"
"MetaListNameValueStr) 语法："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:407
msgid ""
"`since` --- Specifies a version number when the item was deprecated. `rustc` "
"does not currently interpret the string, but external tools like [Clippy]"
"(https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-clippy) may check the validity of the "
"value."
msgstr ""
"`since` --- 指定项被弃用时的版本号。`rustc` 目前不会解释该字符串，但 [Clippy]"
"(https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-clippy) 等外部工具可以检查该值的有效性。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:410
msgid ""
"`note` --- Specifies a string that should be included in the deprecation "
"message. This is typically used to provide an explanation about the "
"deprecation and preferred alternatives."
msgstr ""
"`note` --- 指定应包含在弃用消息中的字符串。这通常用于提供关于弃用和首选替代方"
"案的说明。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:418
msgid ""
"The `deprecated` attribute may be applied to any [item](../items.md), [trait "
"item](../items/traits.md), [enum variant](../items/enumerations.md), [struct "
"field](../items/structs.md), [external block item](../items/external-"
"blocks.md), or [macro definition](../macros-by-example.md). It cannot be "
"applied to [trait implementation items](../items/implementations.md#trait-"
"implementations). When applied to an item containing other items, such as a "
"[module](../items/modules.md) or [implementation](../items/"
"implementations.md), all child items inherit the deprecation attribute."
msgstr ""
"`deprecated` 属性可以应用于任何[项](../items.md)、[trait 项](../items/"
"traits.md)、[enum 变体](../items/enumerations.md)、[struct 字段](../items/"
"structs.md)、[外部块项](../items/external-blocks.md)或[宏定义](../macros-by-"
"example.md)。它不能应用于 [trait 实现项](../items/implementations.md#trait-"
"implementations)。当应用于包含其他项的项（如[模块](../items/modules.md)或[实"
"现](../items/implementations.md)）时，所有子项都会继承该弃用属性。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:431
msgid "\"5.2.0\""
msgstr "\"5.2.0\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:431
msgid "\"foo was rarely used. Users should instead use bar\""
msgstr "\"foo was rarely used. Users should instead use bar\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:437
msgid ""
"The [RFC](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/1270-"
"deprecation.md) contains motivations and more details."
msgstr ""
"[RFC](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/1270-"
"deprecation.md) 包含动机和更多细节。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:446
msgid "The `must_use` attribute"
msgstr "`must_use` 属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:452
msgid ""
"The _`must_use` [attribute](../attributes.md)_ marks a value that should be "
"used."
msgstr "_`must_use` [属性](../attributes.md)_ 标记一个应当被使用的值。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:458
msgid ""
"The `must_use` attribute uses the [MetaWord](../attributes.md#grammar-"
"MetaWord) and [MetaNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaNameValueStr) "
"syntaxes."
msgstr ""
"`must_use` 属性使用 [MetaWord](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaWord) 和 "
"[MetaNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaNameValueStr) 语法。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:468
msgid "\"explanation of why it should be used\""
msgstr "\"explanation of why it should be used\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:479
msgid "The `must_use` attribute may be applied to a:"
msgstr "`must_use` 属性可以应用于："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:481
msgid "[Struct](../items/structs.md)"
msgstr "[struct](../items/structs.md)"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:482
msgid "[Enumeration](../items/enumerations.md)"
msgstr "[enum](../items/enumerations.md)"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:483
msgid "[Union](../items/unions.md)"
msgstr "[union](../items/unions.md)"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:484
msgid "[Function](../items/functions.md#grammar-Function)"
msgstr "[函数](../items/functions.md#grammar-Function)"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:485
msgid "[Trait](../items/traits.md#grammar-Trait)"
msgstr "[trait](../items/traits.md#grammar-Trait)"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:500
msgid "The `must_use` attribute may be used only once on an item."
msgstr "`must_use` 属性在一个项上只能使用一次。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:515
msgid ""
"The `must_use` attribute may include a message by using the "
"[MetaNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaNameValueStr) syntax, e.g., "
"`#[must_use = \"example message\"]`. The message may be emitted as part of "
"the lint."
msgstr ""
"`must_use` 属性可以使用 [MetaNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-"
"MetaNameValueStr) 语法包含一条消息，例如 `#[must_use = \"example "
"message\"]`。该消息可以作为 lint 的一部分发出。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:521
msgid ""
"When the attribute is applied to a [struct](../items/structs.md), "
"[enumeration](../items/enumerations.md), or [union](../items/unions.md), if "
"the [expression](../expressions.md) of an [expression statement](../"
"statements.md#expression-statements) has that type, the use triggers the "
"`unused_must_use` lint."
msgstr ""
"当该属性应用于 [struct](../items/structs.md)、[enum](../items/"
"enumerations.md) 或 [union](../items/unions.md) 时，如果[表达式语句](../"
"statements.md#expression-statements)的[表达式](../expressions.md)具有该类型，"
"则该使用会触发 `unused_must_use` lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:527
msgid "// ERROR: Unused value that must be used.\n"
msgstr "// 错误：未使用必须使用的值。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:534
msgid ""
"As an exception to [attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type](diagnostics.md#r-"
"attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type), the lint does not fire for "
"`Result<(), E>` when `E` is [uninhabited](../glossary.md#r-"
"glossary.uninhabited) or for `ControlFlow<B, ()>` when `B` is [uninhabited]"
"(../glossary.md#r-glossary.uninhabited). A `#[non_exhaustive]` type from an "
"external crate is not considered uninhabited for this purpose, because it "
"may gain constructors in the future."
msgstr ""
"作为 [attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type](diagnostics.md#r-"
"attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type) 的例外，当 `E` [无值](../glossary.md#r-"
"glossary.uninhabited) 时，lint 不会针对 `Result<(), E>` 触发；当 `B` [无值]"
"(../glossary.md#r-glossary.uninhabited) 时，也不会针对 `ControlFlow<B, ()>` "
"触发。来自外部 crate 的 `#[non_exhaustive]` 类型在此目的下不被认为是无值的，"
"因为它将来可能获得构造器。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:541 src/attributes/diagnostics.md:543
msgid "// OK: `Empty` is uninhabited.\n"
msgstr "// OK：`Empty` 是无值类型。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:550
msgid ""
"If the [expression](../expressions.md) of an [expression statement](../"
"statements.md#expression-statements) is a [call expression](../expressions/"
"call-expr.md) or [method call expression](../expressions/method-call-"
"expr.md) whose function operand is a function to which the attribute is "
"applied, the use triggers the `unused_must_use` lint."
msgstr ""
"如果[表达式语句](../statements.md#expression-statements)的[表达式](../"
"expressions.md)是[调用表达式](../expressions/call-expr.md)或[方法调用表达式]"
"(../expressions/method-call-expr.md)，且其函数操作数是应用了该属性的函数，则"
"该使用会触发 `unused_must_use` lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:556 src/attributes/diagnostics.md:591
msgid "// ERROR: Unused return value that must be used.\n"
msgstr "// 错误：未使用必须使用的返回值。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:563
msgid ""
"If the [expression](../expressions.md) of an [expression statement](../"
"statements.md#expression-statements) is a [call expression](../expressions/"
"call-expr.md) or [method call expression](../expressions/method-call-"
"expr.md) whose function operand is a function that returns an [impl trait]"
"(../types/impl-trait.md) or a [dyn trait](../types/trait-object.md) type "
"where one or more traits in the bound are marked with the attribute, the use "
"triggers the `unused_must_use` lint."
msgstr ""
"如果[表达式语句](../statements.md#expression-statements)的[表达式](../"
"expressions.md)是[调用表达式](../expressions/call-expr.md)或[方法调用表达式]"
"(../expressions/method-call-expr.md)，且其函数操作数是一个返回 [impl trait]"
"(../types/impl-trait.md) 或 [dyn trait](../types/trait-object.md) 类型的函"
"数，并且约束中的一个或多个 trait 标记了该属性，则该使用会触发 "
"`unused_must_use` lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:571
msgid "// ERROR: Unused implementor that must be used.\n"
msgstr "// 错误：未使用必须使用的实现者。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:578
msgid ""
"When the attribute is applied to a function in a trait declaration, the "
"rules described in [attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn](diagnostics.md#r-"
"attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn) also apply when the function operand of "
"the [call expression](../expressions/call-expr.md) or [method call "
"expression](../expressions/method-call-expr.md) is an implementation of that "
"function."
msgstr ""
"当该属性应用于 trait 声明中的函数时，如果[调用表达式](../expressions/call-"
"expr.md)或[方法调用表达式](../expressions/method-call-expr.md)的函数操作数是"
"该函数的实现，[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn](diagnostics.md#r-"
"attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn) 中描述的规则也适用。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:605
msgid "//          ^^^^^^^^^^^ ERROR: Unused return value that must be used.\n"
msgstr "//          ^^^^^^^^^^^ 错误：未使用必须使用的返回值。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:613
msgid ""
"When checking the [expression](../expressions.md) of an [expression "
"statement](../statements.md#expression-statements) for "
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type](diagnostics.md#r-"
"attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type), [attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn]"
"(diagnostics.md#r-attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn), "
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait](diagnostics.md#r-"
"attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait), and "
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait-function](diagnostics.md#r-"
"attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait-function), the lint looks through "
"[block expressions](../expressions/block-expr.md) (including [`unsafe` "
"blocks](../expressions/block-expr.md#unsafe-blocks) and [labeled block "
"expressions](../expressions/block-expr.md#labeled-block-expressions)) to the "
"trailing expression of each. This applies recursively for nested block "
"expressions."
msgstr ""
"在针对 [attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type](diagnostics.md#r-"
"attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type)、[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn]"
"(diagnostics.md#r-attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn)、"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait](diagnostics.md#r-"
"attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait) 和 "
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait-function](diagnostics.md#r-"
"attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait-function) 检查[表达式语句](../"
"statements.md#expression-statements)的[表达式](../expressions.md)时，lint 会"
"透过[块表达式](../expressions/block-expr.md)（包括 [`unsafe` 块](../"
"expressions/block-expr.md#unsafe-blocks)和[带标签块表达式](../expressions/"
"block-expr.md#labeled-block-expressions)）查看每个块的尾表达式。这会递归应用"
"于嵌套块表达式。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:620
msgid "// ERROR: The lint looks through block expressions.\n"
msgstr "// 错误：lint 会透过块表达式。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:621
msgid "// ERROR: The lint looks through `unsafe` blocks.\n"
msgstr "// 错误：lint 会透过 `unsafe` 块。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:622
msgid "// ERROR: The lint looks through nested blocks.\n"
msgstr "// 错误：lint 会透过嵌套块。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:629
msgid ""
"When used on a function in a trait implementation, the attribute does "
"nothing."
msgstr "当用于 trait 实现中的函数时，该属性没有效果。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:638
msgid "// This has no effect.\n"
msgstr "// 这没有效果。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:649
msgid ""
"`rustc` lints against use on functions in trait implementations. This may "
"become an error in the future."
msgstr ""
"`rustc` 会对 trait 实现中函数上的使用发出 lint。这在将来可能会变成错误。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:662
msgid ""
"Wrapping the result of a `#[must_use]` function in certain expressions can "
"suppress the [fn-based check](diagnostics.md#r-"
"attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn), because the [expression](../"
"expressions.md) of the [expression statement](../statements.md#expression-"
"statements) is not a [call expression](../expressions/call-expr.md) or "
"[method call expression](../expressions/method-call-expr.md) to a "
"`#[must_use]` function.  The [type-based check](diagnostics.md#r-"
"attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type) still applies if the type of the "
"overall expression is `#[must_use]`."
msgstr ""
"将 `#[must_use]` 函数的结果包裹在某些表达式中可能会抑制[基于 fn 的检查]"
"(diagnostics.md#r-attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn)，因为[表达式语句](../"
"statements.md#expression-statements)的[表达式](../expressions.md)不是对 "
"`#[must_use]` 函数的[调用表达式](../expressions/call-expr.md)或[方法调用表达"
"式](../expressions/method-call-expr.md)。如果整体表达式的类型为 "
"`#[must_use]`，[基于类型的检查](diagnostics.md#r-"
"attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type)仍然适用。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:669
msgid "// The fn-based check does not fire for any of these, because the\n"
msgstr "// 对于下面这些情况，基于 fn 的检查都不会触发，因为\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:670
msgid "// expression of the expression statement is not a call to a\n"
msgstr "// 表达式语句的表达式不是对\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:671
msgid "// `#[must_use]` function.\n"
msgstr "// `#[must_use]` 函数的调用。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:672
msgid "// Expression is a tuple, not a call.\n"
msgstr "// 表达式是元组，不是调用。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:673
msgid "// Callee `Some` is not `#[must_use]`.\n"
msgstr "// 被调用者 `Some` 不是 `#[must_use]`。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:674
msgid "// Expression is an `if`, not a call.\n"
msgstr "// 表达式是 `if`，不是调用。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:675
msgid "// Expression is a `match`, not a call.\n"
msgstr "// 表达式是 `match`，不是调用。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:686
msgid "// Despite the `if` expression not being a call, the type-based check\n"
msgstr "// 尽管 `if` 表达式不是调用，基于类型的检查\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:687
msgid "// fires because the type of the expression is `MustUse`, which has\n"
msgstr "// 仍会触发，因为表达式的类型是 `MustUse`，而该类型具有\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:688
msgid "// the `#[must_use]` attribute.\n"
msgstr "// `#[must_use]` 属性。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:689
msgid "// ERROR: Must be used.\n"
msgstr "// 错误：必须使用。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:703
msgid ""
"Using a [let statement](../statements.md#let-statements) or [destructuring "
"assignment](../expressions/operator-expr.md#r-expr.assign.destructure) with "
"a pattern of `_` when a must-used value is purposely discarded is idiomatic."
msgstr ""
"当有意丢弃必须使用的值时，使用带 `_` 模式的 [let 语句](../statements.md#let-"
"statements)或[解构赋值](../expressions/operator-expr.md#r-"
"expr.assign.destructure)是惯用做法。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:720
msgid "The `diagnostic` tool attribute namespace"
msgstr "`diagnostic` 工具属性命名空间"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:726
msgid ""
"The `#[diagnostic]` attribute namespace is a home for attributes to "
"influence compile-time error messages. The hints provided by these "
"attributes are not guaranteed to be used."
msgstr ""
"`#[diagnostic]` 属性命名空间用于放置影响编译时错误消息的属性。这些属性提供的"
"提示不保证会被使用。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:733
msgid ""
"Unknown attributes in this namespace are accepted, though they may emit "
"warnings for unused attributes. Additionally, invalid inputs to known "
"attributes will typically be a warning (see the attribute definitions for "
"details). This is meant to allow adding or discarding attributes and "
"changing inputs in the future to allow changes without the need to keep the "
"non-meaningful attributes or options working."
msgstr ""
"此命名空间中的未知属性会被接受，但它们可能会因未使用属性而发出警告。此外，对"
"已知属性的无效输入通常会是警告（详见属性定义）。这样做是为了允许未来添加或丢"
"弃属性以及更改输入，从而允许作出更改，而不需要保持无意义的属性或选项继续可"
"用。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:741
msgid "The `diagnostic::on_unimplemented` attribute"
msgstr "`diagnostic::on_unimplemented` 属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:747
msgid ""
"The `#[diagnostic::on_unimplemented]` attribute is a hint to the compiler to "
"supplement the error message that would normally be generated in scenarios "
"where a trait is required but not implemented on a type."
msgstr ""
"`#[diagnostic::on_unimplemented]` 属性是给编译器的提示，用于在需要某个 trait "
"但某个类型未实现它的场景中，补充通常会生成的错误消息。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:753
msgid ""
"The attribute should be placed on a [trait declaration](../items/traits.md), "
"though it is not an error to be located in other positions."
msgstr ""
"该属性应放在 [trait 声明](../items/traits.md)上，不过位于其他位置也不是错误。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:759
msgid ""
"The attribute uses the [MetaListNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-"
"MetaListNameValueStr) syntax to specify its inputs, though any malformed "
"input to the attribute is not considered as an error to provide both "
"forwards and backwards compatibility."
msgstr ""
"该属性使用 [MetaListNameValueStr](../attributes.md#grammar-"
"MetaListNameValueStr) 语法指定其输入，不过为同时提供向前和向后兼容性，任何格"
"式错误的属性输入都不被视为错误。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:765
msgid "The following keys have the given meaning:"
msgstr "以下键具有给定含义："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:766
msgid "`message` --- The text for the top level error message."
msgstr "`message` --- 顶层错误消息的文本。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:767
msgid ""
"`label` --- The text for the label shown inline in the broken code in the "
"error message."
msgstr "`label` --- 错误消息中在出错代码内联显示的标签文本。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:768
msgid "`note` --- Provides additional notes."
msgstr "`note` --- 提供附加注释。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:774
msgid ""
"The `note` option can appear several times, which results in several note "
"messages being emitted."
msgstr "`note` 选项可以出现多次，这会导致发出多条 note 消息。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:780
msgid ""
"If any of the other options appears several times the first occurrence of "
"the relevant option specifies the actually used value. Subsequent "
"occurrences generates a warning."
msgstr ""
"如果任何其他选项出现多次，相关选项的第一次出现指定实际使用的值。后续出现会生"
"成警告。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:786
msgid "A warning is generated for any unknown keys."
msgstr "任何未知键都会生成警告。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:792
msgid ""
"All three options accept a string as an argument, interpreted using the same "
"formatting as a [`std::fmt`](../../alloc/fmt/index.html) string."
msgstr ""
"三个选项都接受字符串作为实参，并使用与 [`std::fmt`](../../alloc/fmt/"
"index.html) 字符串相同的格式化方式解释。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:798
msgid ""
"Format parameters with the given named parameter will be replaced with the "
"following text:"
msgstr "带有给定命名参数的格式参数会被替换为以下文本："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:799
msgid "`{Self}` --- The name of the type implementing the trait."
msgstr "`{Self}` --- 实现该 trait 的类型名称。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:800
msgid ""
"`{` _GenericParameterName_ `}` --- The name of the generic argument's type "
"for the given generic parameter."
msgstr ""
"`{` _GenericParameterName_ `}` --- 给定泛型参数对应的泛型实参类型名称。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:806
msgid ""
"Any other format parameter will generate a warning, but will otherwise be "
"included in the string as-is."
msgstr "任何其他格式参数都会生成警告，但除此之外会按原样包含在字符串中。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:812
msgid ""
"Invalid format strings may generate a warning, but are otherwise allowed, "
"but may not display as intended. Format specifiers may generate a warning, "
"but are otherwise ignored."
msgstr ""
"无效的格式字符串可能生成警告，但除此之外是允许的，不过可能不会按预期显示。格"
"式说明符可能生成警告，但除此之外会被忽略。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:819
msgid "\"My Message for `ImportantTrait<{A}>` implemented for `{Self}`\""
msgstr "\"My Message for `ImportantTrait<{A}>` implemented for `{Self}`\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:820
msgid "\"My Label\""
msgstr "\"My Label\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:821
msgid "\"Note 1\""
msgstr "\"Note 1\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:822
msgid "\"Note 2\""
msgstr "\"Note 2\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:833
msgid "the compiler may generate an error message which looks like this:"
msgstr "编译器可能生成如下所示的错误消息："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:853
msgid "The `diagnostic::do_not_recommend` attribute"
msgstr "`diagnostic::do_not_recommend` 属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:859
msgid ""
"The `#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` attribute is a hint to the compiler to "
"not show the annotated trait implementation as part of a diagnostic message."
msgstr ""
"`#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` 属性是给编译器的提示，使其不要将带注解的 "
"trait 实现作为诊断消息的一部分显示。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:865
msgid ""
"Suppressing the recommendation can be useful if you know that the "
"recommendation would normally not be useful to the programmer. This often "
"occurs with broad, blanket impls. The recommendation may send the programmer "
"down the wrong path, or the trait implementation may be an internal detail "
"that you don't want to expose, or the bounds may not be able to be satisfied "
"by the programmer."
msgstr ""
"如果你知道推荐通常对程序员没有用，抑制该推荐可能很有用。这经常发生在宽泛的 "
"blanket impl 中。推荐可能会把程序员引向错误方向，或者该 trait 实现可能是你不"
"想暴露的内部细节，或者程序员可能无法满足这些约束。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:867
msgid ""
"For example, in an error message about a type not implementing a required "
"trait, the compiler may find a trait implementation that would satisfy the "
"requirements if it weren't for specific bounds in the trait implementation. "
"The compiler may tell the user that there is an impl, but the problem is the "
"bounds in the trait implementation. The `#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` "
"attribute can be used to tell the compiler to _not_ tell the user about the "
"trait implementation, and instead simply tell the user the type doesn't "
"implement the required trait."
msgstr ""
"例如，在关于某个类型未实现所需 trait 的错误消息中，编译器可能找到一个 trait "
"实现：如果不是该 trait 实现中的特定约束，它本可以满足要求。编译器可能告诉用户"
"存在一个 impl，但问题在于该 trait 实现中的约束。可以使用 "
"`#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` 属性告诉编译器_不要_把该 trait 实现告诉用"
"户，而只是告诉用户该类型没有实现所需 trait。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:876
msgid ""
"The attribute should be placed on a [trait implementation item](../items/"
"implementations.md#trait-implementations), though it is not an error to be "
"located in other positions."
msgstr ""
"该属性应放在 [trait 实现项](../items/implementations.md#trait-"
"implementations)上，不过位于其他位置也不是错误。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:882
msgid ""
"The attribute does not accept any arguments, though unexpected arguments are "
"not considered as an error."
msgstr "该属性不接受任何实参，不过非预期实参不被视为错误。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:884
msgid ""
"In the following example, there is a trait called `AsExpression` which is "
"used for casting arbitrary types to the `Expression` type used in an SQL "
"library. There is a method called `check` which takes an `AsExpression`."
msgstr ""
"在下面的示例中，有一个名为 `AsExpression` 的 trait，用于把任意类型转换为 SQL "
"库中使用的 `Expression` 类型。有一个名为 `check` 的方法，它接受一个 "
"`AsExpression`。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:918
msgid ""
"// Uncomment this line to change the recommendation.\n"
"// #[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]\n"
msgstr ""
"// 取消注释此行以更改推荐。\n"
"// #[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:938 src/types/closure.md:554
#: src/types/closure.md:573 src/types/closure.md:928 src/types/closure.md:1022
msgid "\"bar\""
msgstr "\"bar\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:942
msgid ""
"The `SelectInt` type's `check` method is expecting an `Integer` type. "
"Calling it with an i32 type works, as it gets converted to an `Integer` by "
"the `AsExpression` trait. However, calling it with a string does not, and "
"generates a an error that may look like this:"
msgstr ""
"`SelectInt` 类型的 `check` 方法期望一个 `Integer` 类型。用 i32 类型调用它可以"
"工作，因为该值会通过 `AsExpression` trait 转换为 `Integer`。然而，用字符串调"
"用它则不行，并会生成一个可能如下所示的错误："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:944
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"error[E0277]: the trait bound `&str: Expression` is not satisfied\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:53:15\n"
"   |\n"
"53 |     SelectInt.check(\"bar\");\n"
"   |               ^^^^^ the trait `Expression` is not implemented for "
"`&str`\n"
"   |\n"
"   = help: the following other types implement trait `Expression`:\n"
"             Bound<T>\n"
"             SelectInt\n"
"note: required for `&str` to implement `AsExpression<Integer>`\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:45:13\n"
"   |\n"
"45 | impl<T, ST> AsExpression<ST> for T\n"
"   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^     ^\n"
"46 | where\n"
"47 |     T: Expression<SqlType = ST>,\n"
"   |        ------------------------ unsatisfied trait bound introduced "
"here\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"error[E0277]: the trait bound `&str: Expression` is not satisfied\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:53:15\n"
"   |\n"
"53 |     SelectInt.check(\"bar\");\n"
"   |               ^^^^^ the trait `Expression` is not implemented for "
"`&str`\n"
"   |\n"
"   = help: the following other types implement trait `Expression`:\n"
"             Bound<T>\n"
"             SelectInt\n"
"note: required for `&str` to implement `AsExpression<Integer>`\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:45:13\n"
"   |\n"
"45 | impl<T, ST> AsExpression<ST> for T\n"
"   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^     ^\n"
"46 | where\n"
"47 |     T: Expression<SqlType = ST>,\n"
"   |        ------------------------ unsatisfied trait bound introduced "
"here\n"
"```"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:964
msgid ""
"By adding the `#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` attribute to the blanket "
"`impl` for `AsExpression`, the message changes to:"
msgstr ""
"通过向 `AsExpression` 的 blanket `impl` 添加 "
"`#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` 属性，消息会变为："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:966
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"error[E0277]: the trait bound `&str: AsExpression<Integer>` is not "
"satisfied\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:53:15\n"
"   |\n"
"53 |     SelectInt.check(\"bar\");\n"
"   |               ^^^^^ the trait `AsExpression<Integer>` is not "
"implemented for `&str`\n"
"   |\n"
"   = help: the trait `AsExpression<Integer>` is not implemented for `&str`\n"
"           but trait `AsExpression<Text>` is implemented for it\n"
"   = help: for that trait implementation, expected `Text`, found `Integer`\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"error[E0277]: the trait bound `&str: AsExpression<Integer>` is not "
"satisfied\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:53:15\n"
"   |\n"
"53 |     SelectInt.check(\"bar\");\n"
"   |               ^^^^^ the trait `AsExpression<Integer>` is not "
"implemented for `&str`\n"
"   |\n"
"   = help: the trait `AsExpression<Integer>` is not implemented for `&str`\n"
"           but trait `AsExpression<Text>` is implemented for it\n"
"   = help: for that trait implementation, expected `Text`, found `Integer`\n"
"```"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:978
msgid ""
"The first error message includes a somewhat confusing error message about "
"the relationship of `&str` and `Expression`, as well as the unsatisfied "
"trait bound in the blanket impl. After adding "
"`#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]`, it no longer considers the blanket impl "
"for the recommendation. The message should be a little clearer, with an "
"indication that a string cannot be converted to an `Integer`."
msgstr ""
"第一条错误消息包含一段有些令人困惑的错误消息，涉及 `&str` 与 `Expression` 的"
"关系，以及 blanket impl 中未满足的 trait 约束。添加 "
"`#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` 后，它在推荐中不再考虑该 blanket impl。该消"
"息应该会清楚一些，并指出字符串不能转换为 `Integer`。"

