#: src/attributes/type_system.md:19
msgid ""
"The _`non_exhaustive` attribute_ indicates that a type or variant may have "
"more fields or variants added in the future."
msgstr ""
"_`non_exhaustive` 属性_表示一个类型或变体将来可能会添加更多字段或变体。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:26
msgid ""
"It can be applied to [`struct`s](../items/structs.md), [`enum`s](../items/"
"enumerations.md), and `enum` variants."
msgstr ""
"它可以应用于 [`struct`](../items/structs.md)、[`enum`](../items/"
"enumerations.md) 和 `enum` 变体。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:32
msgid ""
"The `non_exhaustive` attribute uses the [MetaWord](../attributes.md#grammar-"
"MetaWord) syntax and thus does not take any inputs."
msgstr ""
"`non_exhaustive` 属性使用 [MetaWord](../attributes.md#grammar-MetaWord) 语"
"法，因此不接受任何输入。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:39
msgid "Within the defining crate, `non_exhaustive` has no effect."
msgstr "在定义它的 crate 内，`non_exhaustive` 没有效果。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:65
msgid ""
"// Non-exhaustive structs can be constructed as normal within the defining "
"crate.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Non-exhaustive structs can be constructed as normal within the defining "
"crate.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:70
msgid ""
"// Non-exhaustive structs can be matched on exhaustively within the defining "
"crate.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Non-exhaustive structs can be matched on exhaustively within the defining "
"crate.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:78
msgid ""
"// Non-exhaustive enums can be matched on exhaustively within the defining "
"crate.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Non-exhaustive enums can be matched on exhaustively within the defining "
"crate.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:86
msgid ""
"// Non-exhaustive variants can be matched on exhaustively within the "
"defining crate.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Non-exhaustive variants can be matched on exhaustively within the "
"defining crate.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:97
msgid ""
"Outside of the defining crate, types annotated with `non_exhaustive` have "
"limitations that preserve backwards compatibility when new fields or "
"variants are added."
msgstr ""
"在定义它的 crate 之外，带有 `non_exhaustive` 标注的类型会受到一些限制，以便在"
"添加新字段或变体时保持向后兼容性。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:104
msgid ""
"Non-exhaustive types cannot be constructed outside of the defining crate:"
msgstr "非穷尽类型不能在定义它的 crate 之外构造："

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:106
msgid ""
"Non-exhaustive variants ([`struct`](../items/structs.md) or [`enum` variant]"
"(../items/enumerations.md)) cannot be constructed with a [StructExpression]"
"(../expressions/struct-expr.md#grammar-StructExpression) (including with "
"[functional update syntax](../expressions/struct-expr.md#functional-update-"
"syntax))."
msgstr ""
"非穷尽变体（[`struct`](../items/structs.md) 或 [`enum` 变体](../items/"
"enumerations.md)）不能用 [StructExpression](../expressions/struct-"
"expr.md#grammar-StructExpression) 构造（包括使用[函数式更新语法](../"
"expressions/struct-expr.md#functional-update-syntax)）。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:108
msgid ""
"The implicitly defined same-named constant of a [unit-like struct](../items/"
"structs.md), or the same-named constructor function of a [tuple struct](../"
"items/structs.md), has a [visibility](../visibility-and-privacy.md) no "
"greater than `pub(crate)`. That is, if the struct’s visibility is `pub`, "
"then the constant or constructor’s visibility is `pub(crate)`, and otherwise "
"the visibility of the two items is the same (as is the case without "
"`#[non_exhaustive]`)."
msgstr ""
"隐式定义的 [unit-like struct](../items/structs.md) 的同名常量，或者 [tuple "
"struct](../items/structs.md) 的同名构造函数，具有不大于 `pub(crate)` 的[可见"
"性](../visibility-and-privacy.md)。也就是说，如果该 struct 的可见性是 `pub`，"
"那么该常量或构造函数的可见性就是 `pub(crate)`；否则这两个项的可见性相同（与没"
"有 `#[non_exhaustive]` 时一样）。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:114
msgid "[`enum`](../items/enumerations.md) instances can be constructed."
msgstr "可以构造 [`enum`](../items/enumerations.md) 实例。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:116
msgid ""
"The following examples of construction do not compile when outside the "
"defining crate:"
msgstr "以下构造示例在定义它们的 crate 之外无法编译："

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:120 src/attributes/type_system.md:166
msgid ""
"// These are types defined in an upstream crate that have been annotated as\n"
"// `#[non_exhaustive]`.\n"
msgstr ""
"// These are types defined in an upstream crate that have been annotated as\n"
"// `#[non_exhaustive]`.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:123
msgid ""
"// Cannot construct an instance of `Config`; if new fields were added in\n"
"// a new version of `upstream` then this would fail to compile, so it is\n"
"// disallowed.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Cannot construct an instance of `Config`; if new fields were added in\n"
"// a new version of `upstream` then this would fail to compile, so it is\n"
"// disallowed.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:128
msgid ""
"// Cannot construct an instance of `Token`; if new fields were added, then\n"
"// it would not be a unit-like struct any more, so the same-named constant\n"
"// created by it being a unit-like struct is not public outside the crate;\n"
"// this code fails to compile.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Cannot construct an instance of `Token`; if new fields were added, then\n"
"// it would not be a unit-like struct any more, so the same-named constant\n"
"// created by it being a unit-like struct is not public outside the crate;\n"
"// this code fails to compile.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:134
msgid ""
"// Cannot construct an instance of `Id`; if new fields were added, then\n"
"// its constructor function signature would change, so its constructor\n"
"// function is not public outside the crate; this code fails to compile.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Cannot construct an instance of `Id`; if new fields were added, then\n"
"// its constructor function signature would change, so its constructor\n"
"// function is not public outside the crate; this code fails to compile.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:139
msgid ""
"// Can construct an instance of `Error`; new variants being introduced "
"would\n"
"// not result in this failing to compile.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Can construct an instance of `Error`; new variants being introduced "
"would\n"
"// not result in this failing to compile.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:143
msgid ""
"// Cannot construct an instance of `Message::Send` or `Message::Reaction`;\n"
"// if new fields were added in a new version of `upstream` then this would\n"
"// fail to compile, so it is disallowed.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Cannot construct an instance of `Message::Send` or `Message::Reaction`;\n"
"// if new fields were added in a new version of `upstream` then this would\n"
"// fail to compile, so it is disallowed.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:149
msgid ""
"// Cannot construct an instance of `Message::Quit`; if this were converted "
"to\n"
"// a tuple enum variant `upstream`, this would fail to compile.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Cannot construct an instance of `Message::Quit`; if this were converted "
"to\n"
"// a tuple enum variant `upstream`, this would fail to compile.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:159
msgid ""
"There are limitations when matching on non-exhaustive types outside of the "
"defining crate:"
msgstr "在定义它们的 crate 之外对非穷尽类型进行匹配时存在一些限制："

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:161
msgid ""
"When pattern matching on a non-exhaustive variant ([`struct`](../items/"
"structs.md) or [`enum` variant](../items/enumerations.md)), a [StructPattern]"
"(../patterns.md#grammar-StructPattern) must be used which must include a "
"`..`. A tuple enum variant's constructor's [visibility](../visibility-and-"
"privacy.md) is reduced to be no greater than `pub(crate)`."
msgstr ""
"对非穷尽变体（[`struct`](../items/structs.md) 或 [`enum` 变体](../items/"
"enumerations.md)）进行模式匹配时，必须使用包含 `..` 的 [StructPattern](../"
"patterns.md#grammar-StructPattern)。元组 enum 变体的构造函数的[可见性](../"
"visibility-and-privacy.md)会降低到不大于 `pub(crate)`。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:162
msgid ""
"When pattern matching on a non-exhaustive [`enum`](../items/"
"enumerations.md), matching on a variant does not contribute towards the "
"exhaustiveness of the arms. The following examples of matching do not "
"compile when outside the defining crate:"
msgstr ""
"对非穷尽 [`enum`](../items/enumerations.md) 进行模式匹配时，匹配某个变体不会"
"有助于分支的穷尽性。以下匹配示例在定义它们的 crate 之外无法编译："

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:169
msgid ""
"// Cannot match on a non-exhaustive enum without including a wildcard arm.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Cannot match on a non-exhaustive enum without including a wildcard arm.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:174
msgid "// would compile with: `_ => {},`\n"
msgstr "// would compile with: `_ => {},`\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:176
msgid "// Cannot match on a non-exhaustive struct without a wildcard.\n"
msgstr "// Cannot match on a non-exhaustive struct without a wildcard.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:179
msgid "// would compile with: `..`\n"
msgstr "// would compile with: `..`\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:181
msgid ""
"// Cannot match a non-exhaustive unit-like or tuple struct except by using\n"
"// braced struct syntax with a wildcard.\n"
"// This would compile as `let Token { .. } = token;`\n"
msgstr ""
"// Cannot match a non-exhaustive unit-like or tuple struct except by using\n"
"// braced struct syntax with a wildcard.\n"
"// This would compile as `let Token { .. } = token;`\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:185
msgid "// This would compile as `let Id { 0: id_number, .. } = id;`\n"
msgstr "// This would compile as `let Id { 0: id_number, .. } = id;`\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:190
msgid ""
"// Cannot match on a non-exhaustive struct enum variant without including a "
"wildcard.\n"
msgstr ""
"// Cannot match on a non-exhaustive struct enum variant without including a "
"wildcard.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:192
msgid "// Cannot match on a non-exhaustive tuple or unit enum variant.\n"
msgstr "// Cannot match on a non-exhaustive tuple or unit enum variant.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:198
msgid ""
"It's also not allowed to use numeric casts (`as`) on enums that contain any "
"non-exhaustive variants."
msgstr "也不允许对包含任何非穷尽变体的 enum 使用数值转换（`as`）。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:200
msgid ""
"For example, the following enum can be cast because it doesn't contain any "
"non-exhaustive variants:"
msgstr "例如，以下 enum 可以转换，因为它不包含任何非穷尽变体："

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:210
msgid ""
"However, if the enum contains even a single non-exhaustive variant, casting "
"will result in an error. Consider this modified version of the same enum:"
msgstr ""
"但是，如果 enum 中哪怕只包含一个非穷尽变体，转换也会导致错误。请看同一 enum "
"的这个修改版本："

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:224
msgid ""
"// Error: cannot cast an enum with a non-exhaustive variant when it's "
"defined in another crate\n"
msgstr ""
"// Error: cannot cast an enum with a non-exhaustive variant when it's "
"defined in another crate\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:229
msgid ""
"Non-exhaustive types are always considered inhabited in downstream crates."
msgstr "在下游 crate 中，非穷尽类型始终被视为有值。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:5
msgid "Debugger attributes"
msgstr "调试器属性"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:7
msgid ""
"The following [attributes](../attributes.md) are used for enhancing the "
"debugging experience when using third-party debuggers like GDB or WinDbg."
msgstr ""
"以下[属性](../attributes.md)用于在使用 GDB 或 WinDbg 等第三方调试器时增强调试"
"体验。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:14
msgid "The `debugger_visualizer` attribute"
msgstr "`debugger_visualizer` 属性"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:20
msgid ""
"The _`debugger_visualizer` [attribute](../attributes.md)_ can be used to "
"embed a debugger visualizer file into the debug information. This improves "
"the debugger experience when displaying values."
msgstr ""
"_`debugger_visualizer` [属性](../attributes.md)_可用于将调试器可视化器文件嵌"
"入到调试信息中。这会改善显示值时的调试器体验。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:28
msgid "\"Example.natvis\""
msgstr "\"Example.natvis\""

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:29
msgid "\"example.py\""
msgstr "\"example.py\""

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:39
msgid ""
"The `debugger_visualizer` attribute uses the [MetaListNameValueStr](../"
"attributes.md#grammar-MetaListNameValueStr) syntax to specify its inputs. "
"One of the following keys must be specified:"
msgstr ""
"`debugger_visualizer` 属性使用 [MetaListNameValueStr](../"
"attributes.md#grammar-MetaListNameValueStr) 语法来指定其输入。必须指定以下键"
"之一："

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:41
msgid ""
"[`natvis_file`](debugger.md#r-attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.natvis)"
msgstr ""
"[`natvis_file`](debugger.md#r-attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.natvis)"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:42
msgid ""
"[`gdb_script_file`](debugger.md#r-"
"attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.gdb)"
msgstr ""
"[`gdb_script_file`](debugger.md#r-"
"attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.gdb)"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:48
msgid ""
"The `debugger_visualizer` attribute may only be applied to a [module](../"
"items/modules.md) or to the crate root."
msgstr ""
"`debugger_visualizer` 属性只能应用于[模块](../items/modules.md)或 crate 根。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:54
msgid ""
"The `debugger_visualizer` attribute may be used any number of times on a "
"form. All specified visualizer files will be loaded."
msgstr ""
"`debugger_visualizer` 属性可以在一个形式上使用任意次数。所有指定的可视化器文"
"件都会被加载。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:60
msgid "Using `debugger_visualizer` with Natvis"
msgstr "将 `debugger_visualizer` 与 Natvis 一起使用"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:66
msgid ""
"Natvis is an XML-based framework for Microsoft debuggers (such as Visual "
"Studio and WinDbg) that uses declarative rules to customize the display of "
"types. For detailed information on the Natvis format, refer to Microsoft's "
"[Natvis documentation](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/"
"debugger/create-custom-views-of-native-objects)."
msgstr ""
"Natvis 是用于 Microsoft 调试器（如 Visual Studio 和 WinDbg）的基于 XML 的框"
"架，它使用声明式规则来自定义类型的显示。有关 Natvis 格式的详细信息，请参阅 "
"Microsoft 的 [Natvis 文档](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/"
"debugger/create-custom-views-of-native-objects)。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:72
msgid ""
"This attribute only supports embedding Natvis files on `-windows-msvc` "
"targets."
msgstr "此属性只支持在 `-windows-msvc` 目标上嵌入 Natvis 文件。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:78
msgid ""
"The path to the Natvis file is specified with the `natvis_file` key, which "
"is a path relative to the source file."
msgstr ""
"Natvis 文件的路径通过 `natvis_file` 键指定，该路径是相对于源文件的路径。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:85
msgid ""
"```rust ignore\n"
"#![debugger_visualizer(natvis_file = \"Rectangle.natvis\")]\n"
"\n"
"struct FancyRect {\n"
"    x: f32,\n"
"    y: f32,\n"
"    dx: f32,\n"
"    dy: f32,\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn main() {\n"
"    let fancy_rect = FancyRect { x: 10.0, y: 10.0, dx: 5.0, dy: 5.0 };\n"
"    println!(\"set breakpoint here\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rust ignore\n"
"#![debugger_visualizer(natvis_file = \"Rectangle.natvis\")]\n"
"\n"
"struct FancyRect {\n"
"    x: f32,\n"
"    y: f32,\n"
"    dx: f32,\n"
"    dy: f32,\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn main() {\n"
"    let fancy_rect = FancyRect { x: 10.0, y: 10.0, dx: 5.0, dy: 5.0 };\n"
"    println!(\"set breakpoint here\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"

