#: src/expressions/if-expr.md:468
msgid ""
"// The semicolon above is important: The type of the `if` expression is\n"
"    // `()`, despite being diverging. When the final body expression is\n"
"    // elided, the type of the body is inferred to ! because the function "
"body\n"
"    // diverges. Without the semicolon, the `if` would be the tail "
"expression\n"
"    // with type `()`, which would fail to match the return type `!`.\n"
msgstr ""
"// The semicolon above is important: The type of the `if` expression is\n"
"    // `()`, despite being diverging. When the final body expression is\n"
"    // elided, the type of the body is inferred to ! because the function "
"body\n"
"    // diverges. Without the semicolon, the `if` would be the tail "
"expression\n"
"    // with type `()`, which would fail to match the return type `!`.\n"

