msgid "\"color change, red: {}, green: {}\""
msgstr "\"color change, red: {}, green: {}\""

#: src/patterns.md:426
msgid "Refutability"
msgstr "可反驳性"

#: src/patterns.md:428
msgid ""
"A pattern is said to be _refutable_ when it has the possibility of not being "
"matched by the value it is being matched against. _Irrefutable_ patterns, on "
"the other hand, always match the value they are being matched against. "
"Examples:"
msgstr ""
"当一个模式有可能不匹配它所匹配的值时，称该模式是_可反驳的_。另一方面，_不可反"
"驳的_模式始终匹配它所匹配的值。示例："

#: src/patterns.md:431
msgid "// \"(x, y)\" is an irrefutable pattern\n"
msgstr "// \"(x, y)\" is an irrefutable pattern\n"

#: src/patterns.md:433
msgid "// \"(a, 3)\" is refutable, and will not match\n"
msgstr "// \"(a, 3)\" is refutable, and will not match\n"

#: src/patterns.md:434
msgid "\"Shouldn't reach here\""
msgstr "\"Shouldn't reach here\""

#: src/patterns.md:435
msgid "// \"(a, 4)\" is refutable, and will match\n"
msgstr "// \"(a, 4)\" is refutable, and will match\n"

#: src/patterns.md:436
msgid "\"Matched ({}, 4)\""
msgstr "\"Matched ({}, 4)\""

#: src/patterns.md:444
msgid "Literal patterns"
msgstr "字面量模式"

#: src/patterns.md:452
msgid ""
"**<sup>Syntax</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-LiteralPattern\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[LiteralPattern]"
"(patterns.md#railroad-LiteralPattern)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">\\-</span><sup>?</sup> <span class=\"grammar-"
"text\">[LiteralExpression](expressions/literal-expr.md#grammar-"
"LiteralExpression)</span>"
msgstr ""
"**<sup>语法</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-LiteralPattern\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[LiteralPattern]"
"(patterns.md#railroad-LiteralPattern)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">\\-</span><sup>?</sup> <span class=\"grammar-"
"text\">[LiteralExpression](expressions/literal-expr.md#grammar-"
"LiteralExpression)</span>"

#: src/patterns.md:501
msgid ""
"_Literal patterns_ match exactly the same value as what is created by the "
"literal. Since negative numbers are not [literals](expressions/literal-"
"expr.md), literals in patterns may be prefixed by an optional minus sign, "
"which acts like the negation operator."
msgstr ""
"_字面量模式_精确匹配由该字面量创建的同一个值。由于负数不是[字面量]"
"(expressions/literal-expr.md)，模式中的字面量可以带有一个可选的前置减号，其作"
"用类似于取负运算符。"

#: src/patterns.md:507
msgid ""
"C string and raw C string literals are accepted in literal patterns, but "
"`&CStr` doesn't implement structural equality (`#[derive(Eq, PartialEq)]`) "
"and therefore any such `match` on a `&CStr` will be rejected with a type "
"error."
msgstr ""
"字面量模式接受 C 字符串和原始 C 字符串字面量，但 `&CStr` 没有实现结构相等性"
"（`#[derive(Eq, PartialEq)]`），因此任何这类针对 `&CStr` 的 `match` 都会因类"
"型错误而被拒绝。"

#: src/patterns.md:516
msgid "Literal patterns are always refutable."
msgstr "字面量模式始终是可反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:523
msgid "\"It's minus one\""
msgstr "\"It's minus one\""

#: src/patterns.md:524
msgid "\"It's a one\""
msgstr "\"It's a one\""

#: src/patterns.md:525
msgid "\"It's either a two or a four\""
msgstr "\"It's either a two or a four\""

#: src/patterns.md:526
msgid "\"Matched none of the arms\""
msgstr "\"Matched none of the arms\""

#: src/patterns.md:535
msgid "Identifier patterns"
msgstr "标识符模式"

#: src/patterns.md:543
msgid ""
"**<sup>Syntax</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-IdentifierPattern\" onclick=\"show_railroad()"
"\">[IdentifierPattern](patterns.md#railroad-IdentifierPattern)</span> → "
"<span class=\"grammar-literal\">ref</span><sup>?</sup> <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">mut</span><sup>?</sup> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[IDENTIFIER]"
"(identifiers.md#grammar-IDENTIFIER)</span> ( <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">@</span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[PatternNoTopAlt]"
"(patterns.md#grammar-PatternNoTopAlt)</span> )<sup>?</sup>"
msgstr ""
"**<sup>语法</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-IdentifierPattern\" onclick=\"show_railroad()"
"\">[IdentifierPattern](patterns.md#railroad-IdentifierPattern)</span> → "
"<span class=\"grammar-literal\">ref</span><sup>?</sup> <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">mut</span><sup>?</sup> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[IDENTIFIER]"
"(identifiers.md#grammar-IDENTIFIER)</span> ( <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">@</span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[PatternNoTopAlt]"
"(patterns.md#grammar-PatternNoTopAlt)</span> )<sup>?</sup>"

#: src/patterns.md:620
msgid ""
"Identifier patterns bind the value they match to a variable in the [value "
"namespace](names/namespaces.md#r-names.namespaces.kinds)."
msgstr ""
"标识符模式会把它们匹配的值绑定到[值命名空间](names/namespaces.md#r-"
"names.namespaces.kinds)中的一个变量。"

#: src/patterns.md:626
msgid "The identifier must be unique within the pattern."
msgstr "该标识符在模式中必须是唯一的。"

#: src/patterns.md:632
msgid ""
"The variable will shadow any variables of the same name in scope. The [scope]"
"(names/scopes.md) of the new binding depends on the context of where the "
"pattern is used (such as a `let` binding or a `match` arm)."
msgstr ""
"该变量会遮蔽作用域内任何同名变量。新绑定的[作用域](names/scopes.md)取决于模式"
"使用位置的上下文（例如 `let` 绑定或 `match` 分支）。"

#: src/patterns.md:638
msgid ""
"Patterns that consist of only an identifier, possibly with a `mut`, match "
"any value and bind it to that identifier. This is the most commonly used "
"pattern in variable declarations and parameters for functions and closures."
msgstr ""
"仅由一个标识符组成、可能带有 `mut` 的模式会匹配任何值，并将其绑定到该标识符。"
"这是变量声明以及函数和闭包参数中最常用的模式。"

#: src/patterns.md:651
msgid ""
"To bind the matched value of a pattern to a variable, use the syntax "
"`variable @ subpattern`. For example, the following binds the value 2 to `e` "
"(not the entire range: the range here is a range subpattern)."
msgstr ""
"若要把模式匹配到的值绑定到变量，请使用语法 `variable @ subpattern`。例如，以"
"下代码会把值 2 绑定到 `e`（不是整个范围：这里的范围是一个范围子模式）。"

#: src/patterns.md:657
msgid "\"got a range element {}\""
msgstr "\"got a range element {}\""

#: src/patterns.md:658
msgid "\"anything\""
msgstr "\"anything\""

#: src/patterns.md:666
msgid ""
"By default, identifier patterns bind a variable to a copy of or move from "
"the matched value depending on whether the matched value implements [`Copy`]"
"(special-types-and-traits.md#copy)."
msgstr ""
"默认情况下，标识符模式会根据被匹配值是否实现 [`Copy`](special-types-and-"
"traits.md#copy)，把变量绑定到被匹配值的副本，或者从被匹配值移动而来。"

#: src/patterns.md:672
msgid ""
"This can be changed to bind to a reference by using the `ref` keyword, or to "
"a mutable reference using `ref mut`. For example:"
msgstr ""
"可以使用 `ref` 关键字将其改为绑定到引用，或使用 `ref mut` 绑定到可变引用。例"
"如："

#: src/patterns.md:687
msgid ""
"In the first match expression, the value is copied (or moved). In the second "
"match, a reference to the same memory location is bound to the variable "
"value. This syntax is needed because in destructuring subpatterns the `&` "
"operator can't be applied to the value's fields. For example, the following "
"is not valid:"
msgstr ""
"在第一个 match 表达式中，该值会被复制（或移动）。在第二个 match 中，指向同一"
"内存位置的引用会被绑定到变量 value。需要这种语法，是因为在解构子模式中，`&` "
"运算符不能应用到值的字段。例如，以下代码无效："

#: src/patterns.md:698
msgid "To make it valid, write the following:"
msgstr "若要使其有效，请写成以下形式："

#: src/patterns.md:713
msgid ""
"Thus, `ref` is not something that is being matched against. Its objective is "
"exclusively to make the matched binding a reference, instead of potentially "
"copying or moving what was matched."
msgstr ""
"因此，`ref` 并不是被匹配的内容。它的目的仅仅是让匹配到的绑定成为引用，而不是"
"可能复制或移动被匹配的内容。"

#: src/patterns.md:719
msgid ""
"[Path patterns](#path-patterns) take precedence over identifier patterns."
msgstr "[路径模式](#path-patterns)优先于标识符模式。"

#: src/patterns.md:725
msgid ""
"When a pattern is a single-segment identifier, the grammar is ambiguous "
"whether it means an [IdentifierPattern](patterns.md#grammar-"
"IdentifierPattern) or a [PathPattern](patterns.md#grammar-PathPattern). This "
"ambiguity can only be resolved after [name resolution](names/name-"
"resolution.md)."
msgstr ""
"当一个模式是单段标识符时，语法上无法确定它表示 [IdentifierPattern]"
"(patterns.md#grammar-IdentifierPattern) 还是 [PathPattern]"
"(patterns.md#grammar-PathPattern)。这种歧义只能在[名称解析](names/name-"
"resolution.md)之后解决。"

#: src/patterns.md:729
msgid "//    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ That this constant is in scope affects how the\n"
msgstr "//    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ That this constant is in scope affects how the\n"

#: src/patterns.md:730
msgid "//                   patterns below are treated.\n"
msgstr "//                   patterns below are treated.\n"

#: src/patterns.md:735
msgid "//  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Parsed as a `PathPattern` that resolves to\n"
msgstr "//  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Parsed as a `PathPattern` that resolves to\n"

#: src/patterns.md:736
msgid "//                 the constant `42`.\n"
msgstr "//                 the constant `42`.\n"

#: src/patterns.md:738
msgid "//  ^^^^^^^^^^^ Parsed as an `IdentifierPattern`.\n"
msgstr "//  ^^^^^^^^^^^ Parsed as an `IdentifierPattern`.\n"

#: src/patterns.md:742
msgid "// If `EXPECTED_VALUE` were treated as an `IdentifierPattern` above,\n"
msgstr "// If `EXPECTED_VALUE` were treated as an `IdentifierPattern` above,\n"

#: src/patterns.md:743
msgid "// that pattern would always match, making the function always return\n"
msgstr ""
"// that pattern would always match, making the function always return\n"

#: src/patterns.md:744
msgid "// `Ok(_) regardless of the input.\n"
msgstr "// `Ok(_) regardless of the input.\n"

#: src/patterns.md:756
msgid ""
"It is an error if `ref` or `ref mut` is specified and the identifier shadows "
"a constant."
msgstr "如果指定了 `ref` 或 `ref mut`，且该标识符遮蔽了一个常量，则这是错误。"

#: src/patterns.md:762
msgid ""
"Identifier patterns are irrefutable if the `@` subpattern is irrefutable or "
"the subpattern is not specified."
msgstr ""
"如果 `@` 子模式不可反驳，或者未指定该子模式，则标识符模式是不可反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:768
msgid "Binding modes"
msgstr "绑定模式"

#: src/patterns.md:774
msgid ""
"To service better ergonomics, patterns operate in different _binding modes_ "
"in order to make it easier to bind references to values. When a reference "
"value is matched by a non-reference pattern, it will be automatically "
"treated as a `ref` or `ref mut` binding. Example:"
msgstr ""
"为了改善易用性，模式会以不同的_绑定模式_运行，以便更容易将引用绑定到值。当一"
"个引用值由非引用模式匹配时，它会被自动视为 `ref` 或 `ref mut` 绑定。示例："

#: src/patterns.md:779
msgid "// y was converted to `ref y` and its type is &i32\n"
msgstr "// y was converted to `ref y` and its type is &i32\n"

#: src/patterns.md:787
msgid ""
"_Non-reference patterns_ include all patterns except bindings, [wildcard "
"patterns](#wildcard-pattern) (`_`), [`const` patterns](#path-patterns) of "
"reference types, and [reference patterns](#reference-patterns)."
msgstr ""
"_非引用模式_包括除绑定、[通配符模式](#wildcard-pattern)（`_`）、引用类型的 "
"[`const` 模式](#path-patterns)以及[引用模式](#reference-patterns)之外的所有模"
"式。"

#: src/patterns.md:793
msgid ""
"If a binding pattern does not explicitly have `ref`, `ref mut`, or `mut`, "
"then it uses the _default binding mode_ to determine how the variable is "
"bound."
msgstr ""
"如果一个绑定型模式没有显式带有 `ref`、`ref mut` 或 `mut`，则它会使用_默认绑定"
"模式_来确定变量如何绑定。"

#: src/patterns.md:799
msgid ""
"The default binding mode starts in \"move\" mode which uses move semantics."
msgstr "默认绑定模式从 \"move\" 模式开始，该模式使用移动语义。"

#: src/patterns.md:805
msgid ""
"When matching a pattern, the compiler starts from the outside of the pattern "
"and works inwards."
msgstr "匹配模式时，编译器会从模式外层开始并向内处理。"

#: src/patterns.md:811
msgid ""
"Each time a reference is matched using a non-reference pattern, it will "
"automatically dereference the value and update the default binding mode."
msgstr ""
"每当使用非引用模式匹配一个引用时，它都会自动解引用该值并更新默认绑定模式。"

#: src/patterns.md:817
msgid "References will set the default binding mode to `ref`."
msgstr "引用会将默认绑定模式设为 `ref`。"

#: src/patterns.md:823
msgid ""
"Mutable references will set the mode to `ref mut` unless the mode is already "
"`ref` in which case it remains `ref`."
msgstr ""
"可变引用会将模式设为 `ref mut`，除非该模式已经是 `ref`，在这种情况下它会保持"
"为 `ref`。"

#: src/patterns.md:829
msgid ""
"If the automatically dereferenced value is still a reference, it is "
"dereferenced and this process repeats."
msgstr "如果自动解引用后的值仍然是引用，则会继续解引用，并重复此过程。"

#: src/patterns.md:835
msgid ""
"The binding pattern may only explicitly specify a `ref` or `ref mut` binding "
"mode, or specify mutability with `mut`, when the default binding mode is "
"\"move\". For example, these are not accepted:"
msgstr ""
"只有当默认绑定模式为 \"move\" 时，绑定型模式才可以显式指定 `ref` 或 `ref "
"mut` 绑定模式，或用 `mut` 指定可变性。例如，以下形式不被接受："

#: src/patterns.md:851
msgid ""
"Before the 2024 edition, bindings could explicitly specify a `ref` or `ref "
"mut` binding mode even when the default binding mode was not \"move\", and "
"they could specify mutability on such bindings with `mut`. In these "
"editions, specifying `mut` on a binding set the binding mode to \"move\" "
"regardless of the current default binding mode."
msgstr ""
"在 2024 edition 之前，即使默认绑定模式不是 \"move\"，绑定也可以显式指定 "
"`ref` 或 `ref mut` 绑定模式，并且可以在这类绑定上用 `mut` 指定可变性。在这些 "
"edition 中，无论当前默认绑定模式如何，在绑定上指定 `mut` 都会把绑定模式设为 "
"\"move\"。"

#: src/patterns.md:860
msgid ""
"Similarly, a reference pattern may only appear when the default binding mode "
"is \"move\". For example, this is not accepted:"
msgstr ""
"类似地，引用模式只可以在默认绑定模式为 \"move\" 时出现。例如，以下形式不被接"
"受："

#: src/patterns.md:874
msgid ""
"Before the 2024 edition, reference patterns could appear even when the "
"default binding mode was not \"move\", and had both the effect of matching "
"against the scrutinee and of causing the default binding mode to be reset to "
"\"move\"."
msgstr ""
"在 2024 edition 之前，即使默认绑定模式不是 \"move\"，引用模式也可以出现，并且"
"同时具有匹配被匹配值以及导致默认绑定模式重置为 \"move\" 的效果。"

#: src/patterns.md:883
msgid ""
"Move bindings and reference bindings can be mixed together in the same "
"pattern. Doing so will result in partial move of the object bound to and the "
"object cannot be used afterwards. This applies only if the type cannot be "
"copied."
msgstr ""
"移动绑定和引用绑定可以混合出现在同一个模式中。这样做会导致被绑定对象发生部分"
"移动，该对象之后不能再使用。只有当该类型不能被复制时，这一点才适用。"

#: src/patterns.md:885
msgid ""
"In the example below, `name` is moved out of `person`. Trying to use "
"`person` as a whole or `person.name` would result in an error because of "
"_partial move_."
msgstr ""
"在下面的示例中，`name` 被从 `person` 中移出。尝试把 `person` 作为整体使用或使"
"用 `person.name` 会因为_部分移动_而导致错误。"

#: src/patterns.md:894
msgid "// `name` is moved from person and `age` referenced\n"
msgstr "// `name` is moved from person and `age` referenced\n"

#: src/patterns.md:903
msgid "Wildcard pattern"
msgstr "通配符模式"

#: src/patterns.md:911
msgid ""
"**<sup>Syntax</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-WildcardPattern\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[WildcardPattern]"
"(patterns.md#railroad-WildcardPattern)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">\\_</span>"
msgstr ""
"**<sup>语法</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-WildcardPattern\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[WildcardPattern]"
"(patterns.md#railroad-WildcardPattern)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">\\_</span>"

#: src/patterns.md:947
msgid ""
"The _wildcard pattern_ (an underscore symbol) matches any value. It is used "
"to ignore values when they don't matter."
msgstr "_通配符模式_（下划线符号）匹配任何值。它用于忽略无关紧要的值。"

#: src/patterns.md:953
msgid ""
"Inside other patterns, it matches a single data field (as opposed to the "
"`..`, which matches the remaining fields)."
msgstr "在其他模式内部，它匹配单个数据字段（相对于匹配剩余字段的 `..`）。"

#: src/patterns.md:959
msgid ""
"Unlike identifier patterns, it does not copy, move, or borrow the value it "
"matches."
msgstr "不同于标识符模式，它不会复制、移动或借用它所匹配的值。"

#: src/patterns.md:965
msgid "// the x is always matched by _\n"
msgstr "// the x is always matched by _\n"

#: src/patterns.md:967
msgid "// ignore a function/closure param\n"
msgstr "// ignore a function/closure param\n"

#: src/patterns.md:970
msgid "// ignore a field from a struct\n"
msgstr "// ignore a field from a struct\n"

#: src/patterns.md:983
msgid "// accept any Some, with any value\n"
msgstr "// accept any Some, with any value\n"

#: src/patterns.md:993
msgid "The wildcard pattern is always irrefutable."
msgstr "通配符模式始终是不可反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:999
msgid "Rest pattern"
msgstr "剩余模式"

#: src/patterns.md:1007
msgid ""
"**<sup>Syntax</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-RestPattern\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[RestPattern]"
"(patterns.md#railroad-RestPattern)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">..</span>"
msgstr ""
"**<sup>语法</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-RestPattern\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[RestPattern]"
"(patterns.md#railroad-RestPattern)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">..</span>"

#: src/patterns.md:1043
msgid ""
"The _rest pattern_ (the `..` token) acts as a variable-length pattern which "
"matches zero or more elements that haven't been matched already before and "
"after."
msgstr ""
"_剩余模式_（`..` token）作为可变长度模式，匹配其前后尚未被匹配的零个或多个元"
"素。"

#: src/patterns.md:1049
msgid ""
"It may only be used in [tuple](#tuple-patterns), [tuple struct](#tuple-"
"struct-patterns), and [slice](#slice-patterns) patterns, and may only appear "
"once as one of the elements in those patterns. It is also allowed in an "
"[identifier pattern](#identifier-patterns) for [slice patterns](#slice-"
"patterns) only."
msgstr ""
"它只可以用于[元组](#tuple-patterns)、[元组结构体](#tuple-struct-patterns)和"
"[切片](#slice-patterns)模式，并且在这些模式中只能作为其中一个元素出现一次。它"
"也允许出现在[标识符模式](#identifier-patterns)中，但仅限于[切片模式](#slice-"
"patterns)。"

#: src/patterns.md:1055
msgid "The rest pattern is always irrefutable."
msgstr "剩余模式始终是不可反驳的。"

