"literal\">&&</span> ) <span class=\"grammar-literal\">mut</span><sup>?</sup> "
"<span class=\"grammar-text\">[PatternWithoutModernRange](patterns.md#grammar-"
"PatternWithoutModernRange)</span>"

#: src/patterns.md:1768
msgid ""
"Reference patterns dereference the pointers that are being matched and, "
"thus, borrow them."
msgstr "引用模式会解引用正在被匹配的指针，并因此借用它们。"

#: src/patterns.md:1770
msgid "For example, these two matches on `x: &i32` are equivalent:"
msgstr "例如，以下两个针对 `x: &i32` 的匹配是等价的："

#: src/patterns.md:1775 src/patterns.md:1776
msgid "\"zero\""
msgstr "\"zero\""

#: src/patterns.md:1775 src/patterns.md:1776
msgid "\"some\""
msgstr "\"some\""

#: src/patterns.md:1785
msgid ""
"The grammar production for reference patterns has to match the token `&&` to "
"match a reference to a reference because it is a token by itself, not two "
"`&` tokens."
msgstr ""
"引用模式的语法产生式必须匹配 token `&&` 才能匹配对引用的引用，因为它本身就是"
"一个 token，而不是两个 `&` token。"

#: src/patterns.md:1791
msgid ""
"Adding the `mut` keyword dereferences a mutable reference. The mutability "
"must match the mutability of the reference."
msgstr "添加 `mut` 关键字会解引用可变引用。可变性必须与该引用的可变性匹配。"

#: src/patterns.md:1797
msgid "Reference patterns are always irrefutable."
msgstr "引用模式始终是不可反驳的。"

