#: src/patterns.md:2596
msgid ""
"Tuple patterns match tuple values that match all criteria defined by its "
"subpatterns. They are also used to [destructure](#destructuring) a tuple."
msgstr ""
"元组模式匹配满足其子模式所定义全部条件的元组值。它们也用于[解构]"
"(#destructuring)元组。"

#: src/patterns.md:2602
msgid ""
"The form `(..)` with a single [RestPattern](patterns.md#grammar-RestPattern) "
"is a special form that does not require a comma, and matches a tuple of any "
"size."
msgstr ""
"带有单个 [RestPattern](patterns.md#grammar-RestPattern) 的形式 `(..)` 是一种"
"特殊形式，它不需要逗号，并匹配任意大小的元组。"

#: src/patterns.md:2608
msgid ""
"The tuple pattern is refutable when one of its subpatterns is refutable."
msgstr "当元组模式的某个子模式可反驳时，该元组模式是可反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:2610
msgid "An example of using tuple patterns:"
msgstr "使用元组模式的示例："

#: src/patterns.md:2624
msgid "Grouped patterns"
msgstr "分组模式"

#: src/patterns.md:2632
msgid ""
"**<sup>Syntax</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-GroupedPattern\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[GroupedPattern]"
"(patterns.md#railroad-GroupedPattern)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">(</span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[Pattern]"
"(patterns.md#grammar-Pattern)</span> <span class=\"grammar-literal\">)</span>"
msgstr ""
"**<sup>语法</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-GroupedPattern\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[GroupedPattern]"
"(patterns.md#railroad-GroupedPattern)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">(</span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[Pattern]"
"(patterns.md#grammar-Pattern)</span> <span class=\"grammar-literal\">)</span>"

#: src/patterns.md:2684
msgid ""
"Enclosing a pattern in parentheses can be used to explicitly control the "
"precedence of compound patterns. For example, a reference pattern next to a "
"range pattern such as `&0..=5` is ambiguous and is not allowed, but can be "
"expressed with parentheses."
msgstr ""
"将模式括在圆括号中可以用于显式控制复合模式的优先级。例如，像 `&0..=5` 这样引"
"用模式紧邻范围模式的形式是有歧义的，因而不允许使用，但可以用圆括号表达。"

#: src/patterns.md:2698
msgid "Slice patterns"
msgstr "切片模式"

#: src/patterns.md:2706
msgid ""
"**<sup>Syntax</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-SlicePattern\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[SlicePattern]"
"(patterns.md#railroad-SlicePattern)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">\\[</span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[SlicePatternItems]"
"(patterns.md#grammar-SlicePatternItems)</span><sup>?</sup> <span "
"class=\"grammar-literal\">\\]</span>"
msgstr ""
"**<sup>语法</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-SlicePattern\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[SlicePattern]"
"(patterns.md#railroad-SlicePattern)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">\\[</span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[SlicePatternItems]"
"(patterns.md#grammar-SlicePatternItems)</span><sup>?</sup> <span "
"class=\"grammar-literal\">\\]</span>"

#: src/patterns.md:2710
msgid ""
"<span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" id=\"grammar-"
"SlicePatternItems\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[SlicePatternItems]"
"(patterns.md#railroad-SlicePatternItems)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"text\">[Pattern](patterns.md#grammar-Pattern)</span> ( <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">,</span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[Pattern]"
"(patterns.md#grammar-Pattern)</span> )<sup>\\*</sup> <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">,</span><sup>?</sup>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" id=\"grammar-"
"SlicePatternItems\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[SlicePatternItems]"
"(patterns.md#railroad-SlicePatternItems)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"text\">[Pattern](patterns.md#grammar-Pattern)</span> ( <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">,</span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[Pattern]"
"(patterns.md#grammar-Pattern)</span> )<sup>\\*</sup> <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">,</span><sup>?</sup>"

#: src/patterns.md:2820
msgid ""
"Slice patterns can match both arrays of fixed size and slices of dynamic "
"size."
msgstr "切片模式既可以匹配固定大小的数组，也可以匹配动态大小的切片。"

#: src/patterns.md:2823
msgid "// Fixed size\n"
msgstr "// Fixed size\n"

#: src/patterns.md:2826
msgid "\"starts with one\""
msgstr "\"starts with one\""

#: src/patterns.md:2827
msgid "\"starts with something else\""
msgstr "\"starts with something else\""

#: src/patterns.md:2831
msgid "// Dynamic size\n"
msgstr "// Dynamic size\n"

#: src/patterns.md:2834
msgid "/* this arm will not apply because the length doesn't match */"
msgstr "/* this arm will not apply because the length doesn't match */"

#: src/patterns.md:2835
msgid "/* this arm will apply */"
msgstr "/* this arm will apply */"

#: src/patterns.md:2836
msgid ""
"/* this wildcard is required, since the length is not known statically */"
msgstr ""
"/* this wildcard is required, since the length is not known statically */"

#: src/patterns.md:2844
msgid ""
"Slice patterns are irrefutable when matching an array as long as each "
"element is irrefutable."
msgstr "匹配数组时，只要每个元素都是不可反驳的，切片模式就是不可反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:2850
msgid ""
"When matching a slice, it is irrefutable only in the form with a single `..` "
"[rest pattern](patterns.md#r-patterns.rest) or [identifier pattern]"
"(#identifier-patterns) with the `..` rest pattern as a subpattern."
msgstr ""
"匹配切片时，只有带有单个 `..` [剩余模式](patterns.md#r-patterns.rest)的形式，"
"或以 `..` 剩余模式作为子模式的[标识符模式](#identifier-patterns)，才是不可反"
"驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:2856
msgid ""
"Within a slice, a range pattern without both lower and upper bound must be "
"enclosed in parentheses, as in `(a..)`, to clarify it is intended to match "
"against a single slice element. A range pattern with both lower and upper "
"bound, like `a..=b`, is not required to be enclosed in parentheses."
msgstr ""
"在切片内部，没有同时具备下界和上界的范围模式必须括在圆括号中，如 `(a..)`，以"
"明确它意在匹配单个切片元素。像 `a..=b` 这样同时具有下界和上界的范围模式不需要"
"括在圆括号中。"

#: src/patterns.md:2862
msgid "Path patterns"
msgstr "路径模式"

#: src/patterns.md:2870
msgid ""
"**<sup>Syntax</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-PathPattern\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[PathPattern]"
"(patterns.md#railroad-PathPattern)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"text\">[PathExpression](expressions/path-expr.md#grammar-PathExpression)</"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"**<sup>语法</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-PathPattern\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[PathPattern]"
"(patterns.md#railroad-PathPattern)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"text\">[PathExpression](expressions/path-expr.md#grammar-PathExpression)</"
"span>"

#: src/patterns.md:2908
msgid ""
"_Path patterns_ are patterns that refer either to constant values or to "
"structs or enum variants that have no fields."
msgstr "_路径模式_是指向常量值，或者指向没有字段的 struct 或 enum 变体的模式。"

#: src/patterns.md:2914
msgid "Unqualified path patterns can refer to:"
msgstr "非限定路径模式可以指向："

#: src/patterns.md:2916
msgid "enum variants"
msgstr "enum 变体"

#: src/patterns.md:2917
msgid "structs"
msgstr "struct"

#: src/patterns.md:2918
msgid "constants"
msgstr "常量"

#: src/patterns.md:2919
msgid "associated constants"
msgstr "关联常量"

#: src/patterns.md:2925
msgid "Qualified path patterns can only refer to associated constants."
msgstr "限定路径模式只能指向关联常量。"

#: src/patterns.md:2931
msgid ""
"Path patterns are irrefutable when they refer to structs or an enum variant "
"when the enum has only one variant or a constant whose type is irrefutable. "
"They are refutable when they refer to refutable constants or enum variants "
"for enums with multiple variants."
msgstr ""
"当路径模式指向 struct、仅有一个变体的 enum 的某个 enum 变体，或类型不可反驳的"
"常量时，它们是不可反驳的。当它们指向可反驳常量，或具有多个变体的 enum 的 "
"enum 变体时，它们是可反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:2937
msgid "Constant patterns"
msgstr "常量模式"

#: src/patterns.md:2943
msgid ""
"When a constant `C` of type `T` is used as a pattern, we first check that "
"`T: PartialEq`."
msgstr "当类型为 `T` 的常量 `C` 被用作模式时，我们首先检查 `T: PartialEq`。"

#: src/patterns.md:2949
msgid ""
"Furthermore we require that the value of `C` _has (recursive) structural "
"equality_, which is defined recursively as follows:"
msgstr "此外，我们要求 `C` 的值_具有（递归的）结构相等性_，其递归定义如下："

#: src/patterns.md:2955
msgid ""
"Integers as well as `str`, `bool` and `char` values always have structural "
"equality."
msgstr "整数以及 `str`、`bool` 和 `char` 值始终具有结构相等性。"

#: src/patterns.md:2961
msgid ""
"Tuples, arrays, and slices have structural equality if all their fields/"
"elements have structural equality. (In particular, `()` and `[]` always have "
"structural equality.)"
msgstr ""
"如果元组、数组和切片的所有字段/元素都具有结构相等性，则它们具有结构相等性。"
"（特别是，`()` 和 `[]` 始终具有结构相等性。）"

#: src/patterns.md:2967
msgid ""
"References have structural equality if the value they point to has "
"structural equality."
msgstr "如果引用所指向的值具有结构相等性，则该引用具有结构相等性。"

#: src/patterns.md:2973
msgid ""
"A value of `struct` or `enum` type has structural equality if its "
"`PartialEq` instance is derived via `#[derive(PartialEq)]`, and all fields "
"(for enums: of the active variant) have structural equality."
msgstr ""
"如果 `struct` 或 `enum` 类型的值的 `PartialEq` 实例是通过 "
"`#[derive(PartialEq)]` 派生的，并且所有字段（对于 enum：活动变体的所有字段）"
"都具有结构相等性，则该值具有结构相等性。"

#: src/patterns.md:2979
msgid ""
"A raw pointer has structural equality if it was defined as a constant "
"integer (and then cast/transmuted)."
msgstr ""
"如果原始指针被定义为常量整数（然后被强制转换/transmute），则它具有结构相等"
"性。"

#: src/patterns.md:2985
msgid "A float value has structural equality if it is not a `NaN`."
msgstr "如果浮点数值不是 `NaN`，则它具有结构相等性。"

#: src/patterns.md:2991
msgid "Nothing else has structural equality."
msgstr "其他任何东西都不具有结构相等性。"

#: src/patterns.md:2997
msgid ""
"In particular, the value of `C` must be known at pattern-building time "
"(which is pre-monomorphization). This means that associated consts that "
"involve generic parameters cannot be used as patterns."
msgstr ""
"特别是，`C` 的值必须在模式构建时已知（即单态化前，pre-monomorphization）。这"
"意味着涉及泛型参数的关联 const 不能用作模式。"

#: src/patterns.md:3003
msgid ""
"The value of `C` must not contain any references to mutable statics (`static "
"mut` items or interior mutable `static` items) or `extern` statics."
msgstr ""
"`C` 的值不得包含任何指向可变静态项（`static mut` 项或内部可变的 `static` 项）"
"或 `extern` 静态项的引用。"

#: src/patterns.md:3009
msgid ""
"After ensuring all conditions are met, the constant value is translated into "
"a pattern, and now behaves exactly as-if that pattern had been written "
"directly. In particular, it fully participates in exhaustiveness checking. "
"(For raw pointers, constants are the only way to write such patterns. Only "
"`_` is ever considered exhaustive for these types.)"
msgstr ""
"在确保所有条件都满足之后，该常量值会被转换为一个模式，并且现在的行为完全如同"
"直接写出了该模式一样。特别是，它会完整参与穷尽性检查。（对于原始指针，常量是"
"书写这类模式的唯一方式。对于这些类型，只有 `_` 会被认为是穷尽的。）"

#: src/patterns.md:3015
msgid "Or-patterns"
msgstr "Or-patterns（或模式）"

#: src/patterns.md:3017
msgid ""
"_Or-patterns_ are patterns that match on one of two or more sub-patterns "
"(for example `A | B | C`). They can nest arbitrarily. Syntactically, or-"
"patterns are allowed in any of the places where other patterns are allowed "
"(represented by the [Pattern](patterns.md#grammar-Pattern) production), with "
"the exceptions of `let`\\-bindings and function and closure parameters "
"(represented by the [PatternNoTopAlt](patterns.md#grammar-PatternNoTopAlt) "
"production)."
msgstr ""
"_Or-patterns（或模式）_是匹配两个或多个子模式之一的模式（例如 `A | B | C`）。"
"它们可以任意嵌套。在语法上，or-patterns 可以出现在允许其他模式出现的任何位置"
"（由 [Pattern](patterns.md#grammar-Pattern) 产生式表示），但 `let`\\-绑定以及"
"函数和闭包参数例外（由 [PatternNoTopAlt](patterns.md#grammar-"
"PatternNoTopAlt) 产生式表示）。"

#: src/patterns.md:3023
msgid "Static semantics"
msgstr "静态语义"

#: src/patterns.md:3029
msgid ""
"Given a pattern `p | q` at some depth for some arbitrary patterns `p` and "
"`q`, the pattern is considered ill-formed if:"
msgstr ""
"给定某个深度处的模式 `p | q`，其中 `p` 和 `q` 是任意模式；如果满足以下情况，"
"则该模式被认为是形式不良的："

#: src/patterns.md:3031
msgid ""
"the type inferred for `p` does not unify with the type inferred for `q`, or"
msgstr "为 `p` 推断出的类型不能与为 `q` 推断出的类型合一，或"

#: src/patterns.md:3032
msgid "the same set of bindings are not introduced in `p` and `q`, or"
msgstr "`p` 和 `q` 中引入的不是同一组绑定，或"

#: src/patterns.md:3033
msgid ""
"the type of any two bindings with the same name in `p` and `q` do not unify "
"with respect to types or binding modes."
msgstr "`p` 和 `q` 中任何两个同名绑定的类型在类型或绑定模式方面不能合一。"

#: src/patterns.md:3035
msgid ""
"Unification of types is in all instances aforementioned exact and implicit "
"[type coercions](type-coercions.md) do not apply."
msgstr ""
"上述所有情况下，类型合一都是精确的，隐式[类型强制转换](type-coercions.md)不适"
"用。"

#: src/patterns.md:3041
msgid ""
"When type checking an expression `match e_s { a_1 => e_1, ... a_n => e_n }`, "
"for each match arm `a_i` which contains a pattern of form `p_i | q_i`, the "
"pattern `p_i | q_i` is considered ill formed if, at the depth `d` where it "
"exists the fragment of `e_s` at depth `d`, the type of the expression "
"fragment does not unify with `p_i | q_i`."
msgstr ""
"对表达式 `match e_s { a_1 => e_1, ... a_n => e_n }` 进行类型检查时，对于每个"
"包含 `p_i | q_i` 形式模式的 match 分支 `a_i`，如果在它所在的深度 `d` 处，"
"`e_s` 在深度 `d` 的表达式片段的类型不能与 `p_i | q_i` 合一，则模式 `p_i | "
"q_i` 被认为是形式不良的。"

#: src/patterns.md:3047
msgid ""
"With respect to exhaustiveness checking, a pattern `p | q` is considered to "
"cover `p` as well as `q`. For some constructor `c(x, ..)` the distributive "
"law applies such that `c(p | q, ..rest)` covers the same set of value as "
"`c(p, ..rest) | c(q, ..rest)` does. This can be applied recursively until "
"there are no more nested patterns of form `p | q` other than those that "
"exist at the top level."
msgstr ""
"就穷尽性检查而言，模式 `p | q` 被认为既覆盖 `p`，也覆盖 `q`。对于某个构造器 "
"`c(x, ..)`，分配律适用，使得 `c(p | q, ..rest)` 覆盖与 `c(p, ..rest) | "
"c(q, ..rest)` 相同的值集合。这可以递归应用，直到除了位于顶层的 `p | q` 形式模"
"式之外，不再存在嵌套的这类模式。"

#: src/patterns.md:3049
msgid ""
"Note that by _\"constructor\"_ we do not refer to tuple struct patterns, but "
"rather we refer to a pattern for any product type. This includes enum "
"variants, tuple structs, structs with named fields, arrays, tuples, and "
"slices."
msgstr ""
"注意，所谓 _\"构造器\"_ 并不是指元组结构体模式，而是指任何积类型的模式。这包"
"括 enum 变体、元组结构体、带命名字段的 struct、数组、元组和切片。"

#: src/patterns.md:3055
msgid "Dynamic semantics"
msgstr "动态语义"

#: src/patterns.md:3061
msgid ""
"The dynamic semantics of pattern matching a scrutinee expression `e_s` "
"against a pattern `c(p | q, ..rest)` at depth `d` where `c` is some "
"constructor, `p` and `q` are arbitrary patterns, and `rest` is optionally "
"any remaining potential factors in `c`, is defined as being the same as that "
"of `c(p, ..rest) | c(q, ..rest)`."
msgstr ""
"在深度 `d` 处，将被匹配值表达式 `e_s` 与模式 `c(p | q, ..rest)` 进行模式匹配"
"的动态语义，被定义为与 `c(p, ..rest) | c(q, ..rest)` 的动态语义相同；其中 "
"`c` 是某个构造器，`p` 和 `q` 是任意模式，`rest` 可选地表示 `c` 中任何剩余的潜"
"在因子。"

#: src/patterns.md:3067
msgid "Precedence with other undelimited patterns"
msgstr "与其他无定界模式的优先级"

#: src/patterns.md:3069
msgid ""
"As shown elsewhere in this chapter, there are several types of patterns that "
"are syntactically undelimited, including identifier patterns, reference "
"patterns, and or-patterns. Or-patterns always have the lowest-precedence. "
"This allows us to reserve syntactic space for a possible future type "
"ascription feature and also to reduce ambiguity. For example, `x @ A(..) | "
"B(..)` will result in an error that `x` is not bound in all patterns. `&A(x) "
"| B(x)` will result in a type mismatch between `x` in the different "
"subpatterns."
msgstr ""
"如本章其他地方所示，有几类模式在语法上是无定界的，包括标识符模式、引用模式和 "
"or-patterns（或模式）。Or-patterns 始终具有最低优先级。这使我们能够为未来可能"
"的类型标注特性保留语法空间，也能减少歧义。例如，`x @ A(..) | B(..)` 会导致错"
"误，因为 `x` 并未在所有模式中绑定。`&A(x) | B(x)` 会导致不同子模式中的 `x` 之"
"间出现类型不匹配。"

#: src/types.md:11
msgid ""
"Every variable, item, and value in a Rust program has a type. The _type_ of "
"a _value_ defines the interpretation of the memory holding it and the "
"operations that may be performed on the value."
msgstr ""
"Rust 程序中的每个变量、项和值都有类型。_值_ 的 _类型_ 定义了如何解释保存该值"
"的内存，以及可以对该值执行哪些操作。"

#: src/types.md:17
msgid ""
"Built-in types are tightly integrated into the language, in nontrivial ways "
"that are not possible to emulate in user-defined types."
msgstr ""
