#: src/types/numeric.md:45
msgid "Floating-point types"
msgstr "浮点类型"

#: src/types/numeric.md:47
msgid ""
"The IEEE 754-2008 \"binary32\" and \"binary64\" floating-point types are "
"`f32` and `f64`, respectively."
msgstr ""
"IEEE 754-2008 的 \"binary32\" 和 \"binary64\" 浮点类型分别是 `f32` 和 `f64`。"

#: src/types/numeric.md:53
msgid "Machine-dependent integer types"
msgstr "机器相关整数类型"

#: src/types/numeric.md:59
msgid ""
"The `usize` type is an unsigned integer type with the same number of bits as "
"the platform's pointer type. It can represent every memory address in the "
"process."
msgstr ""
"`usize` 类型是一种无符号整数类型，其位数与平台的指针类型相同。它可以表示进程"
"中的每个内存地址。"

#: src/types/numeric.md:65
msgid ""
"While a `usize` can represent every _address_, converting a _pointer_ to a "
"`usize` is not necessarily a reversible operation. For more information, see "
"the documentation for [type cast expressions](../expressions/operator-"
"expr.md#type-cast-expressions), [`std::ptr`](../../core/ptr/index.html), and "
"[provenance](../../core/ptr/index.html#provenance) in particular."
msgstr ""
"虽然 `usize` 可以表示每个 _地址_，但将 _指针_ 转换为 `usize` 不一定是可逆操"
"作。更多信息请参见[类型转换表达式](../expressions/operator-expr.md#type-cast-"
"expressions)、[`std::ptr`](../../core/ptr/index.html)，尤其是 [provenance]"
"(../../core/ptr/index.html#provenance) 的文档。"

#: src/types/numeric.md:74
msgid ""
"The `isize` type is a signed two's complement integer type with the same "
"number of bits as the platform's pointer type. The theoretical upper bound "
"on object and array size is the maximum `isize` value. This ensures that "
"`isize` can be used to calculate differences between pointers into an object "
"or array and can address every byte within an object along with one byte "
"past the end."
msgstr ""
"`isize` 类型是一种有符号二进制补码整数类型，其位数与平台的指针类型相同。对象"
"和数组大小的理论上限是 `isize` 的最大值。这确保 `isize` 可用于计算指向对象或"
"数组内部的指针之间的差值，并且能够寻址对象内的每个字节以及末尾之后一个字节。"

#: src/types/numeric.md:80
msgid "`usize` and `isize` are at least 16-bits wide."
msgstr "`usize` 和 `isize` 至少为 16 位宽。"

#: src/types/numeric.md:86
msgid ""
"Many pieces of Rust code may assume that pointers, `usize`, and `isize` are "
"either 32-bit or 64-bit. As a consequence, 16-bit pointer support is limited "
"and may require explicit care and acknowledgment from a library to support."
msgstr ""
"许多 Rust 代码可能假定指针、`usize` 和 `isize` 要么是 32 位，要么是 64 位。因"
"此，对 16 位指针的支持是有限的，并且可能需要库显式谨慎处理并确认支持。"

#: src/types/numeric.md:97
msgid ""
"For every numeric type, `T`, the bit validity of `T` is equivalent to the "
"bit validity of `[u8; size_of::<T>()]`. An uninitialized byte is not a valid "
"`u8`."
msgstr ""
"对于每种数值类型 `T`，`T` 的位有效性等价于 `[u8; size_of::<T>()]` 的位有效"
"性。未初始化字节不是有效的 `u8`。"

#: src/types/char.md:11
msgid ""
"The `char` type represents a single [Unicode scalar value](http://"
"www.unicode.org/glossary/#unicode_scalar_value) (i.e., a code point that is "
"not a surrogate)."
msgstr ""
"`char` 类型表示单个 [Unicode 标量值](http://www.unicode.org/glossary/"
"#unicode_scalar_value)（即不是代理项的码点）。"

#: src/types/char.md:19
msgid "'😀'"
msgstr "'😀'"

#: src/types/char.md:20
msgid "'\\u{1F600}'"
msgstr "'\\u{1F600}'"

#: src/types/char.md:30
msgid ""
"See [the standard library docs](../../std/primitive.char.html) for "
"information on the impls of the `char` type."
msgstr ""
"有关 `char` 类型的 impl 信息，请参见 [标准库文档](../../std/"
"primitive.char.html)。"

#: src/types/char.md:39
msgid ""
"A value of type `char` is represented as a 32-bit unsigned word in the "
"0x0000 to 0xD7FF or 0xE000 to 0x10FFFF range. It is immediate [undefined "
"behavior](../behavior-considered-undefined.md) to create a `char` that falls "
"outside this range."
msgstr ""
"`char` 类型的值表示为一个 32 位无符号字，位于 0x0000 到 0xD7FF 或 0xE000 到 "
"0x10FFFF 范围内。创建落在此范围之外的 `char` 会立即导致 [未定义行为](../"
"behavior-considered-undefined.md)。"

#: src/types/char.md:45
msgid ""
"`char` is guaranteed to have the same size and alignment as `u32` on all "
"platforms."
msgstr "保证 `char` 在所有平台上都具有与 `u32` 相同的大小和对齐。"

#: src/types/char.md:51
msgid ""
"Every byte of a `char` is guaranteed to be initialized. In other words, "
"`transmute::<char, [u8; size_of::<char>()]>(...)` is always sound -- but "
"since some bit patterns are invalid `char`s, the inverse is not always sound."
msgstr ""
"保证 `char` 的每个字节都已初始化。换言之，`transmute::<char, [u8; size_of::"
"<char>()]>(...)` 始终是健全的，但由于某些位模式是无效的 `char`，其逆向转换并"
"不总是健全的。"

#: src/types/str.md:11
msgid "The string slice (`str`) type represents a sequence of characters."
msgstr "字符串切片（`str`）类型表示一个字符序列。"

#: src/types/str.md:15
msgid "\"你好，世界\""
msgstr "\"你好，世界\""

#: src/types/str.md:22
msgid ""
"See [the standard library docs](../../std/primitive.str.html) for "
"information on the impls of the `str` type."
msgstr ""
"有关 `str` 类型的 impl 信息，请参见 [标准库文档](../../std/"
"primitive.str.html)。"

#: src/types/str.md:31
msgid ""
"A value of type `str` is represented in the same way as `[u8]`, a slice of 8-"
"bit unsigned bytes."
msgstr ""
"`str` 类型的值以与 `[u8]` 相同的方式表示，即一个 8 位无符号字节的切片。"

#: src/types/str.md:37
msgid ""
"The standard library makes extra assumptions about `str`: methods working on "
"`str` assume and ensure that the data it contains is valid UTF-8. Calling a "
"`str` method with a non-UTF-8 buffer can cause [undefined behavior](../"
"behavior-considered-undefined.md) now or in the future."
msgstr ""
"标准库对 `str` 作出额外假设：作用于 `str` 的方法会假设并确保它包含的数据是有"
"效的 UTF-8。现在或将来，使用非 UTF-8 缓冲区调用 `str` 方法都可能导致 [未定义"
"行为](../behavior-considered-undefined.md)。"

#: src/types/str.md:46
msgid ""
"A `str` is a [dynamically sized type](../dynamically-sized-types.md). It can "
"only be instantiated through a pointer type, such as `&str`. The layout of "
"`&str` is the same as the layout of `&[u8]`."
msgstr ""
"`str` 是一种 [动态大小类型](../dynamically-sized-types.md)。它只能通过指针类"
"型来实例化，例如 `&str`。`&str` 的布局与 `&[u8]` 的布局相同。"

#: src/types/never.md:13
msgid ""
"**<sup>Syntax</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-NeverType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[NeverType]"
"(never.md#railroad-NeverType)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-literal\">!</"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"**<sup>语法</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-NeverType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[NeverType]"
"(never.md#railroad-NeverType)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-literal\">!</"
"span>"

#: src/types/never.md:49
msgid ""
"The never type `!` is a type with no values, representing the result of "
"computations that never complete."
msgstr "never 类型 `!` 是一种没有值的类型，表示永不完成的计算的结果。"

#: src/types/never.md:55
msgid "Expressions of type `!` can be coerced into any other type."
msgstr "类型为 `!` 的表达式可以被强制转换为任何其他类型。"

#: src/types/never.md:61
msgid ""
"The `!` type can **only** appear in function return types presently, "
"indicating it is a diverging function that never returns."
msgstr ""
"目前，`!` 类型**只能**出现在函数返回类型中，表示该函数是一个永不返回的发散函"
"数。"

#: src/types/never.md:65
msgid "\"This call never returns.\""
msgstr "\"This call never returns.\""

#: src/types/tuple.md:13
msgid ""
"**<sup>Syntax</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-TupleType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[TupleType]"
"(tuple.md#railroad-TupleType)</span> →   \n"
"      <span class=\"grammar-literal\">(</span> <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">)</span>   \n"
"    \\| <span class=\"grammar-literal\">(</span> ( <span class=\"grammar-"
"text\">[Type](../types.md#grammar-Type)</span> <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">,</span> )<sup>+</sup> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[Type](../"
"types.md#grammar-Type)</span><sup>?</sup> <span class=\"grammar-literal\">)</"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"**<sup>语法</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-TupleType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[TupleType]"
"(tuple.md#railroad-TupleType)</span> →   \n"
"      <span class=\"grammar-literal\">(</span> <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">)</span>   \n"
"    \\| <span class=\"grammar-literal\">(</span> ( <span class=\"grammar-"
"text\">[Type](../types.md#grammar-Type)</span> <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">,</span> )<sup>+</sup> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[Type](../"
"types.md#grammar-Type)</span><sup>?</sup> <span class=\"grammar-literal\">)</"
"span>"

#: src/types/tuple.md:108
msgid ""
"_Tuple types_ are a family of structural types[^1] for heterogeneous lists "
"of other types."
msgstr "_元组类型_ 是一族结构类型[^1]，用于由其他类型组成的异构列表。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:110
msgid ""
"The syntax for a tuple type is a parenthesized, comma-separated list of "
"types."
msgstr "元组类型的语法是一个用括号括起、以逗号分隔的类型列表。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:116
msgid ""
"1-ary tuples require a comma after their element type to be disambiguated "
"with a [parenthesized type](../types.md#parenthesized-types)."
msgstr ""
"1-ary 元组要求在其元素类型后带有逗号，以便与 [带括号类型](../"
"types.md#parenthesized-types) 区分开。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:122
msgid ""
"A tuple type has a number of fields equal to the length of the list of "
"types. This number of fields determines the _arity_ of the tuple. A tuple "
"with `n` fields is called an _n-ary tuple_. For example, a tuple with 2 "
"fields is a 2-ary tuple."
msgstr ""
"元组类型的字段数等于类型列表的长度。该字段数决定元组的 _arity_（元数）。具有 "
"`n` 个字段的元组称为 _n-ary tuple_（n 元元组）。例如，具有 2 个字段的元组是 "
"2-ary 元组。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:128
msgid ""
"Fields of tuples are named using increasing numeric names matching their "
"position in the list of types. The first field is `0`. The second field is "
"`1`. And so on. The type of each field is the type of the same position in "
"the tuple's list of types."
msgstr ""
"元组的字段使用与它们在类型列表中位置相匹配的递增数字名称来命名。第一个字段是 "
"`0`。第二个字段是 `1`。以此类推。每个字段的类型是元组类型列表中相同位置的类"
"型。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:134
msgid ""
"For convenience and historical reasons, the tuple type with no fields (`()`) "
"is often called _unit_ or _the unit type_. Its one value is also called "
"_unit_ or _the unit value_."
msgstr ""
"出于便利和历史原因，没有字段的元组类型（`()`）通常称为 _unit_ 或 _the unit "
"type_（单元类型）。它的唯一值也称为 _unit_ 或 _the unit value_（单元值）。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:136
msgid "Some examples of tuple types:"
msgstr "元组类型的一些示例："

#: src/types/tuple.md:139
msgid "`(i32,)` (1-ary tuple)"
msgstr "`(i32,)`（1-ary 元组）"

#: src/types/tuple.md:141
msgid "`(String, i32)`"
msgstr "`(String, i32)`"

#: src/types/tuple.md:142
msgid "`(i32, String)` (different type from the previous example)"
msgstr "`(i32, String)`（与前一个示例是不同的类型）"

#: src/types/tuple.md:143
msgid "`(i32, f64, Vec<String>, Option<bool>)`"
msgstr "`(i32, f64, Vec<String>, Option<bool>)`"

#: src/types/tuple.md:149
msgid ""
"Values of this type are constructed using a [tuple expression](../"
"expressions/tuple-expr.md#tuple-expressions). Furthermore, various "
"expressions will produce the unit value if there is no other meaningful "
"value for it to evaluate to."
msgstr ""
"此类型的值使用 [元组表达式](../expressions/tuple-expr.md#tuple-expressions) "
"构造。此外，当没有其他有意义的求值结果时，各种表达式会产生单元值。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:155
msgid ""
"Tuple fields can be accessed by either a [tuple index expression](../"
"expressions/tuple-expr.md#tuple-indexing-expressions) or [pattern matching]"
"(../patterns.md#tuple-patterns)."
msgstr ""
"元组字段可以通过 [元组索引表达式](../expressions/tuple-expr.md#tuple-"
"indexing-expressions) 或 [模式匹配](../patterns.md#tuple-patterns) 访问。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:157
msgid ""
"Structural types are always equivalent if their internal types are "
"equivalent. For a nominal version of tuples, see [tuple structs](./"
"struct.md)."
msgstr ""
"如果结构类型的内部类型等价，那么它们总是等价的。关于元组的名义版本，请参见 "
"[元组结构体](./struct.md)。"

#: src/types/array.md:13
msgid ""
"**<sup>Syntax</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-ArrayType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[ArrayType]"
"(array.md#railroad-ArrayType)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-literal\">\\[</"
"span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[Type](../types.md#grammar-Type)</span> "
"<span class=\"grammar-literal\">;</span> <span class=\"grammar-"
"text\">[Expression](../expressions.md#grammar-Expression)</span> <span "
"class=\"grammar-literal\">\\]</span>"
msgstr ""
"**<sup>语法</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-ArrayType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[ArrayType]"
"(array.md#railroad-ArrayType)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-literal\">\\[</"
"span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[Type](../types.md#grammar-Type)</span> "
"<span class=\"grammar-literal\">;</span> <span class=\"grammar-"
"text\">[Expression](../expressions.md#grammar-Expression)</span> <span "
"class=\"grammar-literal\">\\]</span>"

#: src/types/array.md:79
msgid ""
"An array is a fixed-size sequence of `N` elements of type `T`. The array "
"type is written as `[T; N]`."
msgstr ""
"数组是由 `N` 个 `T` 类型元素组成的固定大小序列。数组类型写作 `[T; N]`。"

#: src/types/array.md:85
msgid ""
"The size is a [constant expression](../const_eval.md#constant-expressions) "
"that evaluates to a [`usize`](numeric.md#machine-dependent-integer-types)."
msgstr ""
"大小是一个 [常量表达式](../const_eval.md#constant-expressions)，其求值结果为 "
"[`usize`](numeric.md#machine-dependent-integer-types)。"

#: src/types/array.md:90
msgid "// A stack-allocated array\n"
msgstr "// A stack-allocated array\n"

#: src/types/array.md:92 src/types/slice.md:80
msgid "// A heap-allocated array, coerced to a slice\n"
msgstr "// A heap-allocated array, coerced to a slice\n"

#: src/types/array.md:101
msgid ""
"All elements of arrays are always initialized, and access to an array is "
"always bounds-checked in safe methods and operators."
msgstr ""
"数组的所有元素始终已初始化，并且在安全方法和运算符中访问数组始终会进行边界检"
"查。"

#: src/types/array.md:107
msgid ""
"The [`Vec<T>`](../../alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html) standard library type "
"provides a heap-allocated resizable array type."
msgstr ""
"标准库类型 [`Vec<T>`](../../alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html) 提供了一种堆分配的可调"
"整大小数组类型。"

#: src/types/slice.md:13
msgid ""
"**<sup>Syntax</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-SliceType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[SliceType]"
"(slice.md#railroad-SliceType)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-literal\">\\[</"
"span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[Type](../types.md#grammar-Type)</span> "
"<span class=\"grammar-literal\">\\]</span>"
msgstr ""
"**<sup>语法</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-SliceType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[SliceType]"
"(slice.md#railroad-SliceType)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-literal\">\\[</"
"span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[Type](../types.md#grammar-Type)</span> "
"<span class=\"grammar-literal\">\\]</span>"

#: src/types/slice.md:65
msgid ""
"A slice is a [dynamically sized type](../dynamically-sized-types.md) "
"representing a 'view' into a sequence of elements of type `T`. The slice "
"type is written as `[T]`."
msgstr ""
"切片是一种 [动态大小类型](../dynamically-sized-types.md)，表示对 `T` 类型元素"
"序列的一个“视图”。切片类型写作 `[T]`。"

#: src/types/slice.md:71
msgid "Slice types are generally used through pointer types. For example:"
msgstr "切片类型通常通过指针类型使用。例如："

#: src/types/slice.md:73
msgid ""
"`&[T]`: a 'shared slice', often just called a 'slice'. It doesn't own the "
"data it points to; it borrows it."
msgstr ""
"`&[T]`：一个“共享切片”，通常简称为“切片”。它不拥有其所指向的数据；它借用了这"
"些数据。"

#: src/types/slice.md:74
msgid ""
"`&mut [T]`: a 'mutable slice'. It mutably borrows the data it points to."
msgstr "`&mut [T]`：一个“可变切片”。它可变地借用其所指向的数据。"

#: src/types/slice.md:75
msgid "`Box<[T]>`: a 'boxed slice'"
msgstr "`Box<[T]>`：一个“装箱切片”"

#: src/types/slice.md:82
msgid "// A (shared) slice into an array\n"
msgstr "// A (shared) slice into an array\n"

#: src/types/slice.md:91
msgid ""
"All elements of slices are always initialized, and access to a slice is "
"always bounds-checked in safe methods and operators."
msgstr ""
"切片的所有元素始终已初始化，并且在安全方法和运算符中访问切片始终会进行边界检"
"查。"

#: src/types/struct.md:11
msgid ""
"A `struct` _type_ is a heterogeneous product of other types, called the "
"_fields_ of the type.[^structtype]"
msgstr ""
"`struct` _类型_ 是其他类型的异构积，这些其他类型称为该类型的 _字段_。"
"[^structtype]"

#: src/types/struct.md:17
msgid ""
"New instances of a `struct` can be constructed with a [struct expression](../"
"expressions/struct-expr.md)."
msgstr ""
"可以使用 [结构体表达式](../expressions/struct-expr.md) 构造 `struct` 的新实"
"例。"

#: src/types/struct.md:23
msgid ""
"The memory layout of a `struct` is undefined by default to allow for "
"compiler optimizations like field reordering, but it can be fixed with the "
"[`repr` attribute](../type-layout.md#representations). In either case, "
"fields may be given in any order in a corresponding struct _expression_; the "
"resulting `struct` value will always have the same memory layout."
msgstr ""
"`struct` 的内存布局默认未定义，以允许字段重排等编译器优化，但可以通过 "
"[`repr` 属性](../type-layout.md#representations) 固定其布局。在任一情况下，都"
"可以在相应的结构体 _表达式_ 中以任意顺序给出字段；生成的 `struct` 值始终具有"
"相同的内存布局。"

#: src/types/struct.md:29
msgid ""
"The fields of a `struct` may be qualified by [visibility modifiers](../"
"visibility-and-privacy.md), to allow access to data in a struct outside a "
"module."
msgstr ""
"`struct` 的字段可以由 [可见性修饰符](../visibility-and-privacy.md) 限定，以允"
"许在模块外部访问结构体中的数据。"

#: src/types/struct.md:35
msgid ""
"A _tuple struct_ type is just like a struct type, except that the fields are "
"anonymous."
msgstr "_元组结构体_ 类型与结构体类型类似，只是字段是匿名的。"

#: src/types/struct.md:41
msgid ""
"A _unit-like struct_ type is like a struct type, except that it has no "
"fields. The one value constructed by the associated [struct expression](../"
"expressions/struct-expr.md) is the only value that inhabits such a type."
msgstr ""
"_类单元结构体_ 类型与结构体类型类似，只是它没有字段。由关联的 [结构体表达式]"
"(../expressions/struct-expr.md) 构造的那一个值，是这种类型唯一拥有的值。"

#: src/types/struct.md:43
msgid ""
"`struct` types are analogous to `struct` types in C, the _record_ types of "
"the ML family, or the _struct_ types of the Lisp family."
msgstr ""
"`struct` 类型类似于 C 中的 `struct` 类型、ML 家族中的 _record_ 类型，或 Lisp "
"家族中的 _struct_ 类型。"

#: src/types/enum.md:11
msgid ""
"An _enumerated type_ is a nominal, heterogeneous disjoint union type, "
"denoted by the name of an [`enum` item](../items/enumerations.md). "
"[^enumtype]"
msgstr ""
"_枚举类型_ 是一种名义的异构不交联合类型，由 [`enum` 项](../items/"
"enumerations.md) 的名称表示。[^enumtype]"

#: src/types/enum.md:17
msgid ""
"An [`enum` item](../items/enumerations.md) declares both the type and a "
"number of _variants_, each of which is independently named and has the "
"syntax of a struct, tuple struct or unit-like struct."
msgstr ""
"一个 [`enum` 项](../items/enumerations.md) 同时声明类型和若干 _变体_，每个变"
"体都有独立名称，并具有结构体、元组结构体或类单元结构体的语法。"

#: src/types/enum.md:23
msgid ""
"New instances of an `enum` can be constructed with a [struct expression](../"
"expressions/struct-expr.md)."
msgstr ""
"可以使用 [结构体表达式](../expressions/struct-expr.md) 构造 `enum` 的新实例。"

#: src/types/enum.md:29
msgid ""
"Any `enum` value consumes as much memory as the largest variant for its "
"corresponding `enum` type, as well as the size needed to store a "
"discriminant."
msgstr ""
"任何 `enum` 值消耗的内存都等于其对应 `enum` 类型中最大变体所需的内存，再加上"
"存储判别值所需的大小。"

#: src/types/enum.md:35
msgid ""
"Enum types cannot be denoted _structurally_ as types, but must be denoted by "
"named reference to an [`enum` item](../items/enumerations.md)."
msgstr ""
"枚举类型不能作为类型被 _结构性地_ 表示，而必须通过对 [`enum` 项](../items/"
"enumerations.md) 的具名引用来表示。"

#: src/types/enum.md:37
msgid ""
"The `enum` type is analogous to a `data` constructor declaration in Haskell, "
"or a _pick ADT_ in Limbo."
msgstr ""
"`enum` 类型类似于 Haskell 中的 `data` 构造器声明，或 Limbo 中的 _pick ADT_。"

#: src/types/union.md:11
msgid ""
"A _union type_ is a nominal, heterogeneous C-like union, denoted by the name "
"of a [`union` item](../items/unions.md)."
msgstr ""
"_联合体类型_ 是一种名义的异构类 C 联合体，由 [`union` 项](../items/"
"unions.md) 的名称表示。"

#: src/types/union.md:17
msgid ""
"Unions have no notion of an \"active field\". Instead, every union access "
"transmutes parts of the content of the union to the type of the accessed "
"field."
msgstr ""
"联合体没有“活动字段”的概念。相反，每次访问联合体时，都会将联合体内容的一部分"
"转换为被访问字段的类型。"

#: src/types/union.md:23
msgid ""
"Since transmutes can cause unexpected or undefined behaviour, `unsafe` is "
"required to read from a union field."
msgstr "由于转换可能导致意外行为或未定义行为，从联合体字段读取需要 `unsafe`。"

#: src/types/union.md:29
msgid ""
"Union field types are also restricted to a subset of types which ensures "
"that they never need dropping. See the [item](../items/unions.md) "
"documentation for further details."
msgstr ""
"联合体字段类型也被限制为类型的一个子集，以确保它们永远不需要析构。更多细节请"
"参见 [项](../items/unions.md) 的文档。"

#: src/types/union.md:35
msgid ""
"The memory layout of a `union` is undefined by default (in particular, "
"fields do _not_ have to be at offset 0), but the `#[repr(...)]` attribute "
"can be used to fix a layout."
msgstr ""
"`union` 的内存布局默认未定义（特别是，字段_不_必须位于偏移量 0），但可以使用 "
"`#[repr(...)]` 属性来固定布局。"

#: src/types/function-item.md:11
msgid ""
"When referred to, a function item, or the constructor of a tuple-like struct "
"or enum variant, yields a [zero-sized](../glossary.md#r-glossary.zst) value "
"of its _function item type_."
msgstr ""
"在被引用时，函数项，或者类元组结构体或枚举变体的构造器，会产生一个其_函数项类"
"型_的[零大小](../glossary.md#r-glossary.zst)值。"

#: src/types/function-item.md:17
msgid ""
"That type explicitly identifies the function - its name, its type arguments, "
"and its early-bound lifetime arguments (but not its late-bound lifetime "
"arguments, which are only assigned when the function is called) - so the "
"value does not need to contain an actual function pointer, and no "
"indirection is needed when the function is called."
msgstr ""
"该类型会显式标识该函数，即它的名称、类型实参以及早期绑定的生命周期实参（但不"
"包括后期绑定的生命周期实参，后者只有在调用函数时才会被赋值），因此该值不需要"
"包含实际的函数指针，并且调用函数时也不需要间接访问。"

#: src/types/function-item.md:23
msgid ""
"There is no syntax that directly refers to a function item type, but the "
"compiler will display the type as something like `fn(u32) -> i32 {fn_name}` "
"in error messages."
msgstr ""
"没有语法可以直接引用函数项类型，但编译器会在错误消息中将该类型显示为类似 "
"`fn(u32) -> i32 {fn_name}` 的形式。"

#: src/types/function-item.md:25
msgid ""
"Because the function item type explicitly identifies the function, the item "
"types of different functions - different items, or the same item with "
"different generics - are distinct, and mixing them will create a type error:"
msgstr ""
"由于函数项类型会显式标识该函数，不同函数的项类型，即不同项，或同一项带有不同"
"泛型的情况，彼此是不同的；混用它们会产生类型错误："

#: src/types/function-item.md:30
msgid "//~ ERROR mismatched types\n"
msgstr "//~ ERROR mismatched types\n"

#: src/types/function-item.md:37
msgid ""
"However, there is a [coercion](../type-coercions.md) from function items to "
"[function pointers](function-pointer.md) with the same signature, which is "
"triggered not only when a function item is used when a function pointer is "
"directly expected, but also when different function item types with the same "
"signature meet in different arms of the same `if` or `match`:"
msgstr ""
"不过，函数项可以[强制转换](../type-coercions.md)为具有相同签名的[函数指针]"
"(function-pointer.md)。这种转换不仅会在直接期望函数指针却使用函数项时触发，也"
"会在具有相同签名的不同函数项类型出现在同一个 `if` 或 `match` 的不同分支中时触"
"发："

#: src/types/function-item.md:42
msgid "// `foo_ptr_1` has function pointer type `fn()` here\n"
msgstr "// `foo_ptr_1` has function pointer type `fn()` here\n"

#: src/types/function-item.md:45
msgid "// ... and so does `foo_ptr_2` - this type-checks.\n"
msgstr "// ... and so does `foo_ptr_2` - this type-checks.\n"

#: src/types/function-item.md:58
msgid ""
"All function items implement [`Copy`](../special-types-and-traits.md#copy), "
"[`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone), [`Send`](../special-types-"
"and-traits.md#send), and [`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync)."
msgstr ""
"所有函数项都实现 [`Copy`](../special-types-and-traits.md#copy)、[`Clone`](../"
"special-types-and-traits.md#clone)、[`Send`](../special-types-and-"
"traits.md#send) 和 [`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync)。"

#: src/types/function-item.md:60
msgid ""
"[`Fn`](../../core/ops/function/trait.Fn.html), [`FnMut`](../../core/ops/"
"function/trait.FnMut.html), and [`FnOnce`](../../core/ops/function/"
"trait.FnOnce.html) are implemented unless the function has any of the "
"following:"
msgstr ""
"除非函数具有以下任一项，否则它会实现 [`Fn`](../../core/ops/function/"
"trait.Fn.html)、[`FnMut`](../../core/ops/function/trait.FnMut.html) 和 "
"[`FnOnce`](../../core/ops/function/trait.FnOnce.html)："

#: src/types/function-item.md:62
msgid "an [`unsafe`](../unsafe-keyword.md#r-unsafe.fn) qualifier"
msgstr "一个 [`unsafe`](../unsafe-keyword.md#r-unsafe.fn) 限定符"

#: src/types/function-item.md:63
msgid ""
"a [`target_feature` attribute](../attributes/codegen.md#r-"
"attributes.codegen.target_feature)"
msgstr ""
"一个 [`target_feature` 属性](../attributes/codegen.md#r-"
"attributes.codegen.target_feature)"

#: src/types/function-item.md:64
msgid "an [ABI](../items/functions.md#r-items.fn.extern) other than `\"Rust\"`"
msgstr "一个不是 `\"Rust\"` 的 [ABI](../items/functions.md#r-items.fn.extern)"

#: src/types/closure.md:11
msgid ""
"A [closure expression](../expressions/closure-expr.md) produces a closure "
"value with a unique, anonymous type that cannot be written out. A closure "
"type is approximately equivalent to a struct which contains the captured "
"values. For instance, the following closure:"
msgstr ""
"[闭包表达式](../expressions/closure-expr.md)会产生一个闭包值，其类型唯一、匿"
"名且无法写出。闭包类型大致等价于一个包含被捕获值的 struct。例如，以下闭包："

#: src/types/closure.md:32
msgid "// Prints \"Point { x: 2, y: 1 }\".\n"
msgstr "// 打印 \"Point { x: 2, y: 1 }\"。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:35
msgid "generates a closure type roughly like the following:"
msgstr "会生成大致如下的闭包类型："

#: src/types/closure.md:39
msgid ""
"// Note: This is not exactly how it is translated, this is only for\n"
"// illustration.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 注意：实际转换并非完全如此，这里仅用于\n"
"// 演示。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:49 src/types/closure.md:956
msgid "\"rust-call\""
msgstr "\"rust-call\""

#: src/types/closure.md:57
msgid "so that the call to `f` works as if it were:"
msgstr "因此，对 `f` 的调用会像下面这样工作："

#: src/types/closure.md:74
msgid ""
"A _capture mode_ determines how a [place expression](../expressions.md#place-"
"expressions-and-value-expressions) from the environment is borrowed or moved "
"into the closure. The capture modes are:"
msgstr ""
"_捕获模式_决定环境中的[位置表达式](../expressions.md#place-expressions-and-"
"value-expressions)如何被借用或移动进闭包。捕获模式包括："

#: src/types/closure.md:76
msgid ""
"Immutable borrow (`ImmBorrow`) --- The place expression is captured as a "
"[shared reference](pointer.md#references--and-mut)."
msgstr ""
"不可变借用（`ImmBorrow`）--- 位置表达式会作为[共享引用]"
"(pointer.md#references--and-mut)被捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:77
msgid ""
"Unique immutable borrow (`UniqueImmBorrow`) --- This is similar to an "
"immutable borrow, but must be unique as described [below](#unique-immutable-"
"borrows-in-captures)."
msgstr ""
"唯一不可变借用（`UniqueImmBorrow`）--- 这类似于不可变借用，但必须如[下文]"
"(#unique-immutable-borrows-in-captures)所述保持唯一。"

#: src/types/closure.md:78
msgid ""
"Mutable borrow (`MutBorrow`) --- The place expression is captured as a "
"[mutable reference](pointer.md#mutable-references-mut)."
msgstr ""
"可变借用（`MutBorrow`）--- 位置表达式会作为[可变引用](pointer.md#mutable-"
"references-mut)被捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:79
msgid ""
"Move (`ByValue`) --- The place expression is captured by [moving the value]"
"(../expressions.md#moved-and-copied-types) into the closure."
msgstr ""
"移动（`ByValue`）--- 位置表达式通过将[值移动](../expressions.md#moved-and-"
"copied-types)进闭包来捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:85
msgid ""
"Place expressions from the environment are captured from the first mode that "
"is compatible with how the captured value is used inside the closure body. "
"The mode is not affected by the code surrounding the closure, such as the "
"lifetimes of involved variables or fields, or of the closure itself."
msgstr ""
"来自环境的位置表达式会按第一个与被捕获值在闭包体内使用方式兼容的模式被捕获。"
"该模式不受闭包周围代码影响，例如相关变量、字段或闭包自身的生命周期。"

#: src/types/closure.md:96
msgid "`Copy` values"
msgstr "`Copy` 值"

#: src/types/closure.md:98
msgid ""
"Values that implement [`Copy`](../special-types-and-traits.md#copy) that are "
"moved into the closure are captured with the `ImmBorrow` mode."
msgstr ""
"被移动进闭包且实现 [`Copy`](../special-types-and-traits.md#copy) 的值，会以 "
"`ImmBorrow` 模式捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:103
msgid "// x captured by ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// x 以 ImmBorrow 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:111
msgid "Async input capture"
msgstr "async 输入捕获"

#: src/types/closure.md:113
msgid ""
"Async closures always capture all input arguments, regardless of whether or "
"not they are used within the body."
msgstr "async 闭包总是捕获所有输入实参，无论它们是否在闭包体内使用。"

#: src/types/closure.md:115
msgid "Capture precision"
msgstr "捕获精度"

#: src/types/closure.md:121
msgid ""
"A _capture path_ is a sequence starting with a variable from the environment "
"followed by zero or more place projections from that variable."
msgstr ""
"_捕获路径_是一个序列，它以环境中的变量开头，后接从该变量出发的零个或多个位置"
"投影。"

#: src/types/closure.md:127
msgid ""
"A _place projection_ is a [field access](../expressions/field-expr.md), "
"[tuple index](../expressions/tuple-expr.md#tuple-indexing-expressions), "
"[dereference](../expressions/operator-expr.md#the-dereference-operator) (and "
"automatic dereferences), [array or slice index](../expressions/array-"
"expr.md#array-and-slice-indexing-expressions) expression, or [pattern "
"destructuring](../patterns.md#r-patterns.destructure) applied to a variable."
msgstr ""
"_位置投影_是应用于变量的[字段访问](../expressions/field-expr.md)、[元组索引]"
"(../expressions/tuple-expr.md#tuple-indexing-expressions)、[解引用](../"
"expressions/operator-expr.md#the-dereference-operator)（以及自动解引用）、[数"
"组或切片索引](../expressions/array-expr.md#array-and-slice-indexing-"
"expressions)表达式，或[模式解构](../patterns.md#r-patterns.destructure)。"

#: src/types/closure.md:133
msgid ""
"In `rustc`, pattern destructuring desugars into a series of dereferences and "
"field or element accesses."
msgstr "在 `rustc` 中，模式解构会脱糖为一系列解引用以及字段或元素访问。"

#: src/types/closure.md:142
msgid ""
"The closure borrows or moves the capture path, which may be truncated based "
"on the rules described below."
msgstr "闭包会借用或移动捕获路径，而该路径可能会根据下文描述的规则被截断。"

#: src/types/closure.md:153
msgid "// s.f1.1 captured by ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// s.f1.1 以 ImmBorrow 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:158
msgid ""
"Here the capture path is the local variable `s`, followed by a field access "
"`.f1`, and then a tuple index `.1`. This closure captures an immutable "
"borrow of `s.f1.1`."
msgstr ""
"这里的捕获路径是局部变量 `s`，后接字段访问 `.f1`，再后接元组索引 `.1`。此闭包"
"捕获的是对 `s.f1.1` 的不可变借用。"

#: src/types/closure.md:170
msgid "Shared prefix"
msgstr "共享前缀"

#: src/types/closure.md:172
msgid ""
"In the case where a capture path and one of the ancestors of that path are "
"both captured by a closure, the ancestor path is captured with the highest "
"capture mode among the two captures, `CaptureMode = max(AncestorCaptureMode, "
"DescendantCaptureMode)`, using the strict weak ordering:"
msgstr ""
"当一个捕获路径及该路径的某个祖先路径都被同一闭包捕获时，祖先路径会使用两次捕"
"获中较高的捕获模式来捕获，即 `CaptureMode = max(AncestorCaptureMode, "
"DescendantCaptureMode)`，其中采用以下严格弱序："

#: src/types/closure.md:174
msgid "`ImmBorrow < UniqueImmBorrow < MutBorrow < ByValue`"
msgstr "`ImmBorrow < UniqueImmBorrow < MutBorrow < ByValue`"

#: src/types/closure.md:176
msgid "Note that this might need to be applied recursively."
msgstr "注意，这可能需要递归应用。"

#: src/types/closure.md:179
msgid ""
"// In this example, there are three different capture paths with a shared "
"ancestor:\n"
msgstr "// 在此示例中，有三条不同的捕获路径拥有一个共享祖先：\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:181 src/paths.md:1051
msgid "\"S\""
msgstr "\"S\""

#: src/types/closure.md:182
msgid "\"T\""
msgstr "\"T\""

#: src/types/closure.md:183
msgid "\"U\""
msgstr "\"U\""

#: src/types/closure.md:186
msgid "// u captured by ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// u 以 ImmBorrow 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:187
msgid "// u.1 captured by MutBorrow\n"
msgstr "// u.1 以 MutBorrow 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:188
msgid "// u.0.0 captured by ByValue\n"
msgstr "// u.0.0 以 ByValue 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:193
msgid "Overall this closure will capture `u` by `ByValue`."
msgstr "总体而言，此闭包会以 `ByValue` 捕获 `u`。"

#: src/types/closure.md:199
msgid "Rightmost shared reference truncation"
msgstr "最右共享引用截断"

#: src/types/closure.md:201
msgid ""
"The capture path is truncated at the rightmost dereference in the capture "
"path if the dereference is applied to a shared reference."
msgstr ""
"如果捕获路径中的解引用应用于共享引用，则捕获路径会在其中最右侧的此类解引用处"
"截断。"

#: src/types/closure.md:203
msgid ""
"This truncation is allowed because fields that are read through a shared "
"reference will always be read via a shared reference or a copy. This helps "
"reduce the size of the capture when the extra precision does not yield any "
"benefit from a borrow checking perspective."
msgstr ""
"允许这种截断，是因为通过共享引用读取的字段始终会经由共享引用或副本来读取。当"
"额外的精度从借用检查角度看并无收益时，这有助于减小捕获的大小。"

#: src/types/closure.md:205
msgid ""
"The reason it is the _rightmost_ dereference is to help avoid a shorter "
"lifetime than is necessary. Consider the following example:"
msgstr ""
"之所以选择_最右侧_解引用，是为了帮助避免生命周期短于必要范围。考虑以下示例："

#: src/types/closure.md:222
msgid ""
"If this were to capture `m`, then the closure would no longer outlive "
"`'static`, since `m` is constrained to `'a`. Instead, it captures "
"`(*(*m).a)` by `ImmBorrow`."
msgstr ""
"如果这里捕获 `m`，则该闭包将不再比 `'static` 活得更久，因为 `m` 受限于 `'a`。"
"相反，它会以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获 `(*(*m).a)`。"

#: src/types/closure.md:228
msgid "Wildcard pattern bindings"
msgstr "通配符模式绑定"

#: src/types/closure.md:234
msgid ""
"Closures only capture data that needs to be read. Binding a value with a "
"[wildcard pattern](../patterns.md#wildcard-pattern) does not read the value, "
"so the place is not captured."
msgstr ""
"闭包只捕获需要读取的数据。使用[通配符模式](../patterns.md#wildcard-pattern)绑"
"定某个值并不会读取该值，因此该位置不会被捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:237 src/types/closure.md:265 src/types/closure.md:310
#: src/types/closure.md:327 src/types/closure.md:369 src/types/closure.md:386
msgid "// A non-`Copy` type.\n"
msgstr "// 一个非 `Copy` 类型。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:240 src/types/closure.md:243 src/types/closure.md:270
#: src/types/closure.md:278 src/types/closure.md:287 src/types/closure.md:297
#: src/types/closure.md:408 src/types/closure.md:536
msgid "// Does not capture `x`.\n"
msgstr "// 不捕获 `x`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:245 src/types/closure.md:272 src/types/closure.md:280
#: src/types/closure.md:289 src/types/closure.md:299 src/types/closure.md:410
#: src/types/closure.md:539
msgid "// OK: `x` can be moved here.\n"
msgstr "// OK：`x` 可以在这里被移动。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:253
msgid ""
"Destructuring tuples, structs, and single-variant enums does not, by itself, "
"cause a read or the place to be captured."
msgstr ""
"解构元组、struct 和单变体 enum，本身不会导致读取，也不会导致该位置被捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:259
msgid ""
"Enums marked with [`#[non_exhaustive]`](../attributes/type_system.md#r-"
"attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive) are always treated as having multiple "
"variants. See _[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.non_exhaustive]"
"(closure.md#r-type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.non_exhaustive)_."
msgstr ""
"带有 [`#[non_exhaustive]`](../attributes/type_system.md#r-attributes.type-"
"system.non_exhaustive) 标记的 enum 总是被视为具有多个变体。参见 "
"_[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.non_exhaustive](closure.md#r-"
"type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.non_exhaustive)_。"

#: src/types/closure.md:266
msgid "// Destructuring tuples does not cause a read or capture.\n"
msgstr "// 解构元组不会导致读取或捕获。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:274
msgid "// Destructuring unit structs does not cause a read or capture.\n"
msgstr "// 解构单元 struct 不会导致读取或捕获。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:282
msgid "// Destructuring structs does not cause a read or capture.\n"
msgstr "// 解构 struct 不会导致读取或捕获。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:291
msgid ""
"// Destructuring single-variant enums does not cause a read\n"
"// or capture.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 解构单变体 enum 不会导致读取\n"
"// 或捕获。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:307
msgid ""
"Fields matched against [RestPattern](../patterns.md#grammar-RestPattern) "
"(`..`) or [StructPatternEtCetera](../patterns.md#grammar-"
"StructPatternEtCetera) (also `..`) are not read, and those fields are not "
"captured."
msgstr ""
"由 [RestPattern](../patterns.md#grammar-RestPattern)（`..`）或 "
"[StructPatternEtCetera](../patterns.md#grammar-StructPatternEtCetera)（同样"
"是 `..`）匹配的字段不会被读取，且这些字段不会被捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:313
msgid "// Captures `x.0` by `ByValue`.\n"
msgstr "// 以 `ByValue` 捕获 `x.0`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:314
msgid "// Only the first tuple field was captured by the closure.\n"
msgstr "// 闭包只捕获了第一个元组字段。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:316 src/types/closure.md:394
msgid "// OK: `x.1` can be moved here.\n"
msgstr "// OK：`x.1` 可以在这里被移动。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:324
msgid ""
"Partial captures of arrays and slices are not supported; the entire slice or "
"array is always captured even if used with wildcard pattern matching, "
"indexing, or sub-slicing."
msgstr ""
"不支持对数组和切片进行部分捕获；即使使用通配符模式匹配、索引或子切片，也总是"
"捕获整个切片或数组。"

#: src/types/closure.md:330
msgid "// Captures all of `x` by `ByValue`.\n"
msgstr "// 以 `ByValue` 捕获整个 `x`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:332
msgid "// ERROR: Borrow of moved value.\n"
msgstr "// ERROR：借用了已移动的值。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:339
msgid "Values that are matched with wildcards must still be initialized."
msgstr "与通配符匹配的值仍然必须已初始化。"

#: src/types/closure.md:344
msgid "// ERROR: Binding `x` isn't initialized.\n"
msgstr "// ERROR：绑定 `x` 未初始化。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:354
msgid "Capturing for discriminant reads"
msgstr "针对判别值读取的捕获"

#: src/types/closure.md:360
msgid ""
"If pattern matching reads a discriminant, the place containing that "
"discriminant is captured by `ImmBorrow`."
msgstr "如果模式匹配会读取判别值，则包含该判别值的位置会以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:366
msgid ""
"Matching against a variant of an enum that has more than one variant reads "
"the discriminant, capturing the place by `ImmBorrow`."
msgstr ""
"匹配具有多个变体的 enum 的某个变体会读取判别值，并以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获该位置。"

#: src/types/closure.md:372
msgid ""
"//   ^^^^\n"
"// This pattern requires reading the discriminant, which\n"
"// causes `x.0` to be captured by `ImmBorrow`.\n"
msgstr ""
"//   ^^^^\n"
"// 此模式需要读取判别值，这会\n"
"// 导致 `x.0` 以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:378
msgid ""
"// ERROR: Cannot borrow `x.0` as mutable.\n"
"//           ^^^\n"
"// The closure is still live, so `x.0` is still immutably\n"
"// borrowed here.\n"
msgstr ""
"// ERROR：不能将 `x.0` 作为可变对象借用。\n"
"//           ^^^\n"
"// 闭包仍然存活，因此 `x.0` 在这里仍然被\n"
"// 不可变借用。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:388
msgid "// Captures `x.0` by `ImmBorrow`.\n"
msgstr "// 以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获 `x.0`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:391
msgid ""
"// Though `x.0` is captured due to the discriminant read,\n"
"// `x.1` is not captured.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 虽然 `x.0` 因判别值读取而被捕获，\n"
"// 但 `x.1` 不会被捕获。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:402
msgid ""
"Matching against the only variant of a single-variant enum does not read the "
"discriminant and does not capture the place."
msgstr "匹配单变体 enum 的唯一变体不会读取判别值，也不会捕获该位置。"

#: src/types/closure.md:405
msgid "// A single-variant enum.\n"
msgstr "// 一个单变体 enum。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:418
msgid ""
"If [`#[non_exhaustive]`](../attributes/type_system.md#r-attributes.type-"
"system.non_exhaustive) is applied to an enum, the enum is treated as having "
"multiple variants for the purpose of deciding whether a read occurs, even if "
"it actually has only one variant."
msgstr ""
"如果对 enum 应用了 [`#[non_exhaustive]`](../attributes/type_system.md#r-"
"attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive)，则在判定是否发生读取时，该 enum 会被"
"视为具有多个变体，即使它实际上只有一个变体。"

#: src/types/closure.md:424
msgid ""
"Even if all variants but the one being matched against are uninhabited, "
"making the pattern [irrefutable](../patterns.md#r-patterns.refutable), the "
"discriminant is still read if it otherwise would be."
msgstr ""
"即使除被匹配的变体之外所有变体都不可能有值，从而使该模式[不可反驳](../"
"patterns.md#r-patterns.refutable)，只要在其他情况下会读取判别值，这里仍然会读"
"取判别值。"

#: src/types/closure.md:430 src/types/closure.md:452
msgid "// Captures `x` by `ImmBorrow`.\n"
msgstr "// 以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获 `x`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:432 src/types/closure.md:454
msgid "// ERROR: Cannot borrow `x` as mutable.\n"
msgstr "// ERROR：不能将 `x` 作为可变对象借用。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:441
msgid "Capturing and range patterns"
msgstr "捕获与范围模式"

#: src/types/closure.md:447
msgid ""
"Matching against a [range pattern](../patterns.md#r-patterns.range) reads "
"the place being matched, even if the range includes all possible values of "
"the type, and captures the place by `ImmBorrow`."
msgstr ""
"匹配[范围模式](../patterns.md#r-patterns.range)会读取被匹配的位置，即使该范围"
"包含该类型的所有可能值，并且会以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获该位置。"

#: src/types/closure.md:462
msgid "Capturing and slice patterns"
msgstr "捕获与切片模式"

#: src/types/closure.md:468
msgid ""
"Matching a slice against a [slice pattern](../patterns.md#r-patterns.slice) "
"other than one with only a single [rest pattern](../patterns.md#r-"
"patterns.rest) (i.e. `[..]`) is treated as a read of the length from the "
"slice and captures the slice by `ImmBorrow`."
msgstr ""
"用[切片模式](../patterns.md#r-patterns.slice)匹配切片时，除只含单个[剩余模式]"
"(../patterns.md#r-patterns.rest)的模式（即 `[..]`）之外，都会被视为从该切片读"
"取长度，并以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获该切片。"

#: src/types/closure.md:472
msgid "// Captures `*x` by `ImmBorrow`.\n"
msgstr "// 以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获 `*x`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:473
msgid ""
"//       ^^\n"
"// This matches a slice of exactly zero elements. To know whether the\n"
"// scrutinee matches, the length must be read, causing the slice to\n"
"// be captured.\n"
msgstr ""
"//       ^^\n"
"// 这会匹配恰好有零个元素的切片。要知道\n"
"// 被匹配值是否匹配，必须读取长度，从而导致\n"
"// 该切片被捕获。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:480
msgid "// ERROR: Cannot borrow `*x` as mutable.\n"
msgstr "// ERROR：不能将 `*x` 作为可变对象借用。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:486
msgid "// Does not capture `*x`.\n"
msgstr "// 不捕获 `*x`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:487
msgid "//   ^^ Rest pattern.\n"
msgstr "//   ^^ 剩余模式。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:490
msgid "// OK: `*x` can be borrow here.\n"
msgstr "// OK：可以在这里借用 `*x`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:498
msgid ""
"Perhaps surprisingly, even though the length is contained in the (wide) "
"_pointer_ to the slice, it is the place of the _pointee_ (the slice) that is "
"treated as read and is captured."
msgstr ""
"也许令人意外的是，虽然长度包含在指向切片的（宽）_指针_中，但被视为读取并被捕"
"获的是_被指向对象_（切片）的位置。"

#: src/types/closure.md:502
msgid "// The closure outlives `'l` because it captures `**x`. If\n"
msgstr "// 该闭包比 `'l` 活得更久，因为它捕获 `**x`。如果\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:503
msgid "// instead it captured `*x`, it would not live long enough\n"
msgstr "// 它转而捕获 `*x`，则它就不会活得足够久，\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:504
msgid "// to satisfy the `impl Fn() + 'l` bound.\n"
msgstr "// 无法满足 `impl Fn() + 'l` 约束。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:505 src/types/closure.md:516
msgid "// Captures `**x` by `ImmBorrow`.\n"
msgstr "// 以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获 `**x`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:512
msgid ""
"In this way, the behavior is consistent with dereferencing to the slice in "
"the scrutinee."
msgstr "这样一来，其行为就与在被匹配值中解引用到切片一致。"

#: src/types/closure.md:523
msgid ""
"For details, see [Rust PR #138961](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/"
"138961)."
msgstr ""
"详情请参见 [Rust PR #138961](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/138961)。"

#: src/types/closure.md:532
msgid ""
"As the length of an array is fixed by its type, matching an array against a "
"slice pattern does not by itself capture the place."
msgstr "由于数组长度由其类型固定，用切片模式匹配数组本身不会捕获该位置。"

#: src/types/closure.md:537
msgid "// Length is fixed.\n"
msgstr "// 长度是固定的。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:547
msgid "Capturing references in move contexts"
msgstr "在 move 上下文中捕获引用"

#: src/types/closure.md:549
msgid ""
"Because it is not allowed to move fields out of a reference, `move` closures "
"will only capture the prefix of a capture path that runs up to, but not "
"including, the first dereference of a reference. The reference itself will "
"be moved into the closure."
msgstr ""
"由于不允许从引用中移出字段，`move` 闭包只会捕获捕获路径的前缀，直到但不包括对"
"引用的第一次解引用。该引用本身会被移动进闭包。"

#: src/types/closure.md:557
msgid "// captures `t_mut_ref` ByValue\n"
msgstr "// 以 ByValue 捕获 `t_mut_ref`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:566
msgid "Raw pointer dereference"
msgstr "裸指针解引用"

#: src/types/closure.md:568
msgid ""
"Because it is `unsafe` to dereference a raw pointer, closures will only "
"capture the prefix of a capture path that runs up to, but not including, the "
"first dereference of a raw pointer."
msgstr ""
"由于解引用裸指针是 `unsafe` 的，闭包只会捕获捕获路径的前缀，直到但不包括对裸"
"指针的第一次解引用。"

#: src/types/closure.md:577
msgid "// captures `t_ptr` by ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// 以 ImmBorrow 捕获 `t_ptr`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:586
msgid "Union fields"
msgstr "union 字段"

#: src/types/closure.md:588
msgid ""
"Because it is `unsafe` to access a union field, closures will only capture "
"the prefix of a capture path that runs up to the union itself."
msgstr ""
"由于访问 union 字段是 `unsafe` 的，闭包只会捕获捕获路径中直到 union 本身为止"
"的前缀。"

#: src/types/closure.md:598
msgid "// captures `u` ByValue\n"
msgstr "// 以 ByValue 捕获 `u`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:601
msgid "// This also includes writing to fields.\n"
msgstr "// 这也包括写入字段。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:606
msgid "// captures `u` with MutBorrow\n"
msgstr "// 以 MutBorrow 捕获 `u`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:615
msgid "Reference into unaligned `struct`s"
msgstr "指向未对齐 `struct` 的引用"

#: src/types/closure.md:617
msgid ""
"Because it is [undefined behavior](../behavior-considered-undefined.md) to "
"create references to unaligned fields in a structure, closures will only "
"capture the prefix of the capture path that runs up to, but not including, "
"the first field access into a structure that uses [the `packed` "
"representation](../type-layout.md#the-alignment-modifiers). This includes "
"all fields, even those that are aligned, to protect against compatibility "
"concerns should any of the fields in the structure change in the future."
msgstr ""
"由于为结构中未对齐的字段创建引用是[未定义行为](../behavior-considered-"
"undefined.md)，闭包只会捕获捕获路径的前缀，直到但不包括对使用 [`packed` 表示]"
"(../type-layout.md#the-alignment-modifiers)的结构进行的第一次字段访问。这包括"
"所有字段，即使是已对齐的字段也包括在内，以防结构中的任何字段将来发生变化时引"
"发兼容性问题。"

#: src/types/closure.md:625 src/types/closure.md:640
msgid "// captures `t` with ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// 以 ImmBorrow 捕获 `t`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:626
msgid "// Copies out of `t` are ok.\n"
msgstr "// 可以从 `t` 中复制出值。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:632
msgid ""
"Similarly, taking the address of an unaligned field also captures the entire "
"struct:"
msgstr "类似地，取得未对齐字段的地址也会捕获整个 struct："

#: src/types/closure.md:642
msgid "// ERROR: cannot move out of `t.0` because it is borrowed\n"
msgstr "// ERROR：不能移出 `t.0`，因为它已被借用\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:646
msgid ""
"but the above works if it is not packed since it captures the field "
"precisely:"
msgstr "但如果它不是 packed 的，上述代码就可以工作，因为它会精确捕获该字段："

#: src/types/closure.md:653
msgid "// captures `t.1` with ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// 以 ImmBorrow 捕获 `t.1`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:654
msgid "// The move here is allowed.\n"
msgstr "// 这里的移动是允许的。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:667
msgid "`Box` vs other `Deref` implementations"
msgstr "`Box` 与其他 `Deref` 实现"

#: src/types/closure.md:669
msgid ""
"The implementation of the [`Deref`](../special-types-and-traits.md#deref-and-"
"derefmut) trait for [`Box`](../special-types-and-traits.md#boxt) is treated "
"differently from other `Deref` implementations, as it is considered a "
"special entity."
msgstr ""
"[`Box`](../special-types-and-traits.md#boxt) 的 [`Deref`](../special-types-"
"and-traits.md#deref-and-derefmut) trait 实现会被区别于其他 `Deref` 实现来处"
"理，因为它被认为是一个特殊实体。"

#: src/types/closure.md:671
msgid ""
"For example, let us look at examples involving `Rc` and `Box`. The `*rc` is "
"desugared to a call to the trait method `deref` defined on `Rc`, but since "
"`*box` is treated differently, it is possible to do a precise capture of the "
"contents of the `Box`."
msgstr ""
"例如，来看涉及 `Rc` 和 `Box` 的示例。`*rc` 会脱糖为对 `Rc` 上定义的 trait 方"
"法 `deref` 的调用，但由于 `*box` 会被区别处理，因此可以精确捕获 `Box` 的内"
"容。"

#: src/types/closure.md:680
msgid "`Box` with non-`move` closure"
msgstr "非 `move` 闭包中的 `Box`"

#: src/types/closure.md:682
msgid ""
"In a non-`move` closure, if the contents of the `Box` are not moved into the "
"closure body, the contents of the `Box` are precisely captured."
msgstr ""
"在非 `move` 闭包中，如果 `Box` 的内容没有被移动进闭包体，则 `Box` 的内容会被"
"精确捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:689
msgid "// captures `(*b).0` by ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// 以 ImmBorrow 捕获 `(*b).0`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:692
msgid "// Contrast `Box` with another type that implements Deref:\n"
msgstr "// 将 `Box` 与另一种实现 Deref 的类型进行对比：\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:696
msgid "// captures `r` by ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// 以 ImmBorrow 捕获 `r`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:705
msgid ""
"However, if the contents of the `Box` are moved into the closure, then the "
"box is entirely captured. This is done so the amount of data that needs to "
"be moved into the closure is minimized."
msgstr ""
"然而，如果 `Box` 的内容被移动进闭包，则整个 box 都会被捕获。这样做是为了最小"
"化需要移动进闭包的数据量。"

#: src/types/closure.md:708
msgid ""
"// This is the same as the example above except the closure\n"
"// moves the value instead of taking a reference to it.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这与上面的示例相同，只是闭包会移动该值，\n"
"// 而不是取得对它的引用。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:715 src/types/closure.md:733
msgid "// captures `b` with ByValue\n"
msgstr "// 以 ByValue 捕获 `b`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:724
msgid "`Box` with move closure"
msgstr "move 闭包中的 `Box`"

#: src/types/closure.md:726
msgid ""
"Similarly to moving contents of a `Box` in a non-`move` closure, reading the "
"contents of a `Box` in a `move` closure will capture the `Box` entirely."
msgstr ""
"与在非 `move` 闭包中移动 `Box` 的内容类似，在 `move` 闭包中读取 `Box` 的内容"
"会捕获整个 `Box`。"

#: src/types/closure.md:741
msgid "Unique immutable borrows in captures"
msgstr "捕获中的唯一不可变借用"

#: src/types/closure.md:743
msgid ""
"Captures can occur by a special kind of borrow called a _unique immutable "
"borrow_, which cannot be used anywhere else in the language and cannot be "
"written out explicitly. It occurs when modifying the referent of a mutable "
"reference, as in the following example:"
msgstr ""
"捕获可以通过一种称为_唯一不可变借用_的特殊借用发生，这种借用不能在语言的其他"
"任何地方使用，也不能显式写出。它会在修改可变引用的被引用对象时发生，如以下示"
"例所示："

#: src/types/closure.md:749
msgid "// An ImmBorrow and a MutBorrow of `x`.\n"
msgstr "// 对 `x` 的一个 ImmBorrow 和一个 MutBorrow。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:751
msgid "// `x` captured by UniqueImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// `x` 以 UniqueImmBorrow 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:752
msgid ""
"// The following line is an error:\n"
"// let y = &x;\n"
msgstr ""
"// 下面这一行会出错：\n"
"// let y = &x;\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:755
msgid "// However, the following is OK.\n"
msgstr "// 然而，下面这样是 OK 的。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:760
msgid ""
"In this case, borrowing `x` mutably is not possible, because `x` is not "
"`mut`. But at the same time, borrowing `x` immutably would make the "
"assignment illegal, because a `& &mut` reference might not be unique, so it "
"cannot safely be used to modify a value. So a unique immutable borrow is "
"used: it borrows `x` immutably, but like a mutable borrow, it must be unique."
msgstr ""
"在此情况下，不可能可变借用 `x`，因为 `x` 不是 `mut`。但与此同时，不可变借用 "
"`x` 又会使赋值非法，因为 `& &mut` 引用可能不是唯一的，所以不能安全地用于修改"
"值。因此会使用唯一不可变借用：它以不可变方式借用 `x`，但像可变借用一样，它必"
"须是唯一的。"

#: src/types/closure.md:762
msgid ""
"In the above example, uncommenting the declaration of `y` will produce an "
"error because it would violate the uniqueness of the closure's borrow of "
"`x`; the declaration of z is valid because the closure's lifetime has "
"expired at the end of the block, releasing the borrow."
msgstr ""
"在上面的示例中，如果取消 `y` 的声明的注释，将会产生错误，因为这会违反闭包对 "
"`x` 的借用的唯一性；`z` 的声明是有效的，因为闭包的生命周期已在块的末尾结束，"
"从而释放了该借用。"

#: src/types/closure.md:768
msgid "Call traits and coercions"
msgstr "调用 trait 与强制转换"

#: src/types/closure.md:774
msgid ""
"Closure types all implement [`FnOnce`](../../core/ops/function/"
"trait.FnOnce.html), indicating that they can be called once by consuming "
"ownership of the closure. Additionally, some closures implement more "
"specific call traits:"
msgstr ""
"所有闭包类型都实现 [`FnOnce`](../../core/ops/function/trait.FnOnce.html)，表"
"示它们可以通过消耗闭包的所有权来调用一次。此外，某些闭包会实现更具体的调用 "
"trait："

#: src/types/closure.md:780
msgid ""
"A closure which does not move out of any captured variables implements "
"[`FnMut`](../../core/ops/function/trait.FnMut.html), indicating that it can "
"be called by mutable reference."
msgstr ""
"不会移出任何被捕获变量的闭包实现 [`FnMut`](../../core/ops/function/"
"trait.FnMut.html)，表示它可以通过可变引用调用。"

#: src/types/closure.md:786
msgid ""
"A closure which does not mutate or move out of any captured variables "
"implements [`Fn`](../../core/ops/function/trait.Fn.html), indicating that it "
"can be called by shared reference."
msgstr ""
"不会修改或移出任何被捕获变量的闭包实现 [`Fn`](../../core/ops/function/"
"trait.Fn.html)，表示它可以通过共享引用调用。"

#: src/types/closure.md:792
msgid ""
"`move` closures may still implement [`Fn`](../../core/ops/function/"
"trait.Fn.html) or [`FnMut`](../../core/ops/function/trait.FnMut.html), even "
"though they capture variables by move. This is because the traits "
"implemented by a closure type are determined by what the closure does with "
"captured values, not how it captures them."
msgstr ""
"`move` 闭包仍然可以实现 [`Fn`](../../core/ops/function/trait.Fn.html) 或 "
"[`FnMut`](../../core/ops/function/trait.FnMut.html)，即使它们通过移动来捕获变"
"量。这是因为闭包类型实现哪些 trait 取决于闭包如何处理被捕获值，而不是它如何捕"
"获这些值。"

#: src/types/closure.md:801
msgid ""
"_Non-capturing closures_ are closures that don't capture anything from their "
"environment. Non-async, non-capturing closures can be coerced to function "
"pointers (e.g., `fn()`) with the matching signature."
msgstr ""
"_非捕获闭包_是不从其环境捕获任何内容的闭包。非 async 的非捕获闭包可以被强制转"
"换为具有匹配签名的函数指针（例如 `fn()`）。"

#: src/types/closure.md:817
msgid "Async closure traits"
msgstr "async 闭包 trait"

#: src/types/closure.md:823
msgid ""
"Async closures have a further restriction of whether or not they implement "
"[`FnMut`](../../core/ops/function/trait.FnMut.html) or [`Fn`](../../core/ops/"
"function/trait.Fn.html)."
msgstr ""
"async 闭包对于是否实现 [`FnMut`](../../core/ops/function/trait.FnMut.html) "
"或 [`Fn`](../../core/ops/function/trait.Fn.html) 还有进一步限制。"

#: src/types/closure.md:825
msgid ""
"The [`Future`](../../core/future/future/trait.Future.html) returned by the "
"async closure has similar capturing characteristics as a closure. It "
"captures place expressions from the async closure based on how they are "
"used. The async closure is said to be _lending_ to its [`Future`](../../core/"
"future/future/trait.Future.html) if it has either of the following "
"properties:"
msgstr ""
"async 闭包返回的 [`Future`](../../core/future/future/trait.Future.html) 具有"
"与闭包类似的捕获特性。它会根据使用方式从 async 闭包中捕获位置表达式。如果 "
"async 闭包具有以下任一性质，则称它向其 [`Future`](../../core/future/future/"
"trait.Future.html) _借出_："

#: src/types/closure.md:827
msgid "The `Future` includes a mutable capture."
msgstr "`Future` 包含可变捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:828
msgid ""
"The async closure captures by value, except when the value is accessed with "
"a dereference projection."
msgstr "async 闭包按值捕获，但通过解引用投影访问该值时除外。"

#: src/types/closure.md:830
msgid ""
"If the async closure is lending to its `Future`, then [`FnMut`](../../core/"
"ops/function/trait.FnMut.html) and [`Fn`](../../core/ops/function/"
"trait.Fn.html) are _not_ implemented. [`FnOnce`](../../core/ops/function/"
"trait.FnOnce.html) is always implemented."
msgstr ""
"如果 async 闭包向其 `Future` 借出，则_不会_实现 [`FnMut`](../../core/ops/"
"function/trait.FnMut.html) 和 [`Fn`](../../core/ops/function/trait.Fn.html)。"
"[`FnOnce`](../../core/ops/function/trait.FnOnce.html) 总是会实现。"

#: src/types/closure.md:832
msgid ""
"**Example**: The first clause for a mutable capture can be illustrated with "
"the following:"
msgstr "**示例**：关于可变捕获的第一项条件可以用下面的代码说明："

#: src/types/closure.md:840
msgid "// x captured with MutBorrow\n"
msgstr "// x 以 MutBorrow 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:842
msgid "// ERROR: async closure does not implement `FnMut`\n"
msgstr "// ERROR：async 闭包未实现 `FnMut`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:846
msgid ""
"The second clause for a regular value capture can be illustrated with the "
"following:"
msgstr "关于常规值捕获的第二项条件可以用下面的代码说明："

#: src/types/closure.md:854
msgid "// x captured ByValue\n"
msgstr "// x 以 ByValue 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:856
msgid "// ERROR: async closure does not implement `Fn`\n"
msgstr "// ERROR：async 闭包未实现 `Fn`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:860
msgid ""
"The exception of the the second clause can be illustrated by using a "
"dereference, which does allow `Fn` and `FnMut` to be implemented:"
msgstr ""
"第二项条件的例外可以通过使用解引用来说明，这种方式确实允许实现 `Fn` 和 "
"`FnMut`："

#: src/types/closure.md:870
msgid "// OK: implements `Fn`\n"
msgstr "// OK：实现 `Fn`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:878
msgid ""
"Async closures implement [`AsyncFn`](../../core/ops/async_function/"
"trait.AsyncFn.html), [`AsyncFnMut`](../../core/ops/async_function/"
"trait.AsyncFnMut.html), and [`AsyncFnOnce`](../../core/ops/async_function/"
"trait.AsyncFnOnce.html) in an analogous way as regular closures implement "
"[`Fn`](../../core/ops/function/trait.Fn.html), [`FnMut`](../../core/ops/"
"function/trait.FnMut.html), and [`FnOnce`](../../core/ops/function/"
"trait.FnOnce.html); that is, depending on the use of the captured variables "
"in its body."
msgstr ""
"async 闭包实现 [`AsyncFn`](../../core/ops/async_function/"
"trait.AsyncFn.html)、[`AsyncFnMut`](../../core/ops/async_function/"
"trait.AsyncFnMut.html) 和 [`AsyncFnOnce`](../../core/ops/async_function/"
"trait.AsyncFnOnce.html) 的方式，类似于常规闭包实现 [`Fn`](../../core/ops/"
"function/trait.Fn.html)、[`FnMut`](../../core/ops/function/trait.FnMut.html) "
"和 [`FnOnce`](../../core/ops/function/trait.FnOnce.html) 的方式；也就是说，取"
"决于其闭包体内如何使用被捕获变量。"

#: src/types/closure.md:884
msgid "Other traits"
msgstr "其他 trait"

#: src/types/closure.md:890
msgid ""
"All closure types implement [`Sized`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sized). "
"Additionally, closure types implement the following traits if allowed to do "
"so by the types of the captures it stores:"
msgstr ""
"所有闭包类型都实现 [`Sized`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sized)。此外，如"
"果其存储的捕获项的类型允许，闭包类型还会实现以下 trait："

#: src/types/closure.md:892
msgid "[`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone)"
msgstr "[`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone)"

#: src/types/closure.md:893
msgid "[`Copy`](../special-types-and-traits.md#copy)"
msgstr "[`Copy`](../special-types-and-traits.md#copy)"

#: src/types/closure.md:894
msgid "[`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync)"
msgstr "[`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync)"

#: src/types/closure.md:895
msgid "[`Send`](../special-types-and-traits.md#send)"
msgstr "[`Send`](../special-types-and-traits.md#send)"

#: src/types/closure.md:901
msgid ""
"The rules for [`Send`](../special-types-and-traits.md#send) and [`Sync`](../"
"special-types-and-traits.md#sync) match those for normal struct types, while "
"[`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone) and [`Copy`](../special-"
"types-and-traits.md#copy) behave as if [derived](../attributes/derive.md). "
"For [`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone), the order of cloning of "
"the captured values is left unspecified."
msgstr ""
"[`Send`](../special-types-and-traits.md#send) 和 [`Sync`](../special-types-"
"and-traits.md#sync) 的规则与普通 struct 类型的规则一致，而 [`Clone`](../"
"special-types-and-traits.md#clone) 和 [`Copy`](../special-types-and-"
"traits.md#copy) 的行为就像是[派生](../attributes/derive.md)得到的一样。对于 "
"[`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone)，被捕获值的克隆顺序是未指定"
"的。"

#: src/types/closure.md:903
msgid ""
"Because captures are often by reference, the following general rules arise:"
msgstr "由于捕获通常通过引用进行，因此会得到以下一般规则："

#: src/types/closure.md:905
msgid ""
"A closure is [`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync) if all captured "
"values are [`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync)."
msgstr ""
"如果所有被捕获值都是 [`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync)，则闭包是 "
"[`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync)。"

#: src/types/closure.md:906
msgid ""
"A closure is [`Send`](../special-types-and-traits.md#send) if all values "
"captured by non-unique immutable reference are [`Sync`](../special-types-and-"
"traits.md#sync), and all values captured by unique immutable or mutable "
"reference, copy, or move are [`Send`](../special-types-and-traits.md#send)."
msgstr ""
"如果所有通过非唯一不可变引用捕获的值都是 [`Sync`](../special-types-and-"
"traits.md#sync)，且所有通过唯一不可变引用、可变引用、复制或移动捕获的值都是 "
"[`Send`](../special-types-and-traits.md#send)，则闭包是 [`Send`](../special-"
"types-and-traits.md#send)。"

#: src/types/closure.md:907
msgid ""
"A closure is [`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone) or [`Copy`](../"
"special-types-and-traits.md#copy) if it does not capture any values by "
"unique immutable or mutable reference, and if all values it captures by copy "
"or move are [`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone) or [`Copy`](../"
"special-types-and-traits.md#copy), respectively."
msgstr ""
"如果闭包没有通过唯一不可变引用或可变引用捕获任何值，并且它通过复制或移动捕获"
"的所有值分别都是 [`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone) 或 [`Copy`]"
"(../special-types-and-traits.md#copy)，则该闭包是 [`Clone`](../special-types-"
"and-traits.md#clone) 或 [`Copy`](../special-types-and-traits.md#copy)。"

#: src/types/closure.md:921
msgid "Drop order"
msgstr "丢弃顺序"

#: src/types/closure.md:923
msgid ""
"If a closure captures a field of a composite types such as structs, tuples, "
"and enums by value, the field's lifetime would now be tied to the closure. "
"As a result, it is possible for disjoint fields of a composite types to be "
"dropped at different times."
msgstr ""
"如果闭包按值捕获复合类型（例如 struct、元组和 enum）的某个字段，则该字段的生"
"命周期现在会与闭包绑定。因此，复合类型中互不重叠的字段可能会在不同时间被丢"
"弃。"

#: src/types/closure.md:928
msgid "// --+\n"
msgstr "// --+\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:929
msgid "//                                               |\n"
msgstr "//                                               |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:930
msgid ""
"// ----------------------------+  |\n"
"            // tuple.0 is captured into the closure |  |\n"
msgstr ""
"// ----------------------------+  |\n"
"            // tuple.0 is captured into the closure |  |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:932
msgid "//                       |  |\n"
msgstr "//                       |  |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:933
msgid "//                                       |  |\n"
msgstr "//                                       |  |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:934
msgid "// 'c' and 'tuple.0' dropped here ------------+  |\n"
msgstr "// 'c' and 'tuple.0' dropped here ------------+  |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:935
msgid "// tuple.1 dropped here -----------------------------+\n"
msgstr "// tuple.1 dropped here -----------------------------+\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:942
msgid "Edition 2018 and before"
msgstr "2018 edition 及以前版本"

#: src/types/closure.md:944
msgid "Closure types difference"
msgstr "闭包类型差异"

#: src/types/closure.md:946
msgid ""
"In Edition 2018 and before, closures always capture a variable in its "
"entirety, without its precise capture path. This means that for the example "
"used in the [Closure types](#closure-types) section, the generated closure "
"type would instead look something like this:"
msgstr ""
"在 2018 edition 及以前版本中，闭包总是整体捕获变量，而不会使用其精确捕获路"
"径。这意味着对于[闭包类型](#closure-types)一节中的示例，生成的闭包类型会改为"
"大致如下："

#: src/types/closure.md:964
msgid "and the call to `f` would work as follows:"
msgstr "而对 `f` 的调用会按如下方式工作："

#: src/types/closure.md:975
msgid "Capture precision difference"
msgstr "捕获精度差异"

#: src/types/closure.md:977
msgid ""
"Composite types such as structs, tuples, and enums are always captured in "
"its entirety, not by individual fields. As a result, it may be necessary to "
"borrow into a local variable in order to capture a single field:"
msgstr ""
"复合类型（例如 struct、元组和 enum）总是被整体捕获，而不是按单个字段捕获。因"
"此，为了捕获单个字段，可能需要先借用到局部变量中："

#: src/types/closure.md:997
msgid ""
"If, instead, the closure were to use `self.vec` directly, then it would "
"attempt to capture `self` by mutable reference. But since `self.set` is "
"already borrowed to iterate over, the code would not compile."
msgstr ""
"如果该闭包改为直接使用 `self.vec`，则它会尝试通过可变引用捕获 `self`。但由于 "
"`self.set` 已经被借用来进行迭代，这段代码将无法编译。"

#: src/types/closure.md:1003
msgid ""
"If the `move` keyword is used, then all captures are by move or, for `Copy` "
"types, by copy, regardless of whether a borrow would work. The `move` "
"keyword is usually used to allow the closure to outlive the captured values, "
"such as if the closure is being returned or used to spawn a new thread."
msgstr ""
"如果使用 `move` 关键字，则所有捕获都会通过移动进行；对于 `Copy` 类型，则通过"
"复制进行，而不考虑借用是否可行。`move` 关键字通常用于让闭包比被捕获值活得更"
"久，例如闭包被返回或用于生成新线程时。"

#: src/types/closure.md:1009
msgid ""
"Regardless of if the data will be read by the closure, i.e. in case of wild "
"card patterns, if a variable defined outside the closure is mentioned within "
"the closure the variable will be captured in its entirety."
msgstr ""
"无论闭包是否会读取数据，例如在通配符模式的情况下，只要闭包内提到在闭包外定义"
"的变量，该变量就会被整体捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:1015
msgid "Drop order difference"
msgstr "丢弃顺序差异"

#: src/types/closure.md:1017
msgid ""
"As composite types are captured in their entirety, a closure which captures "
"one of those composite types by value would drop the entire captured "
"variable at the same time as the closure gets dropped."
msgstr ""
"由于复合类型会被整体捕获，按值捕获其中某个复合类型的闭包，会在闭包被丢弃的同"
"时丢弃整个被捕获变量。"

#: src/types/closure.md:1024
msgid ""
"// --------------------------+\n"
"            // tuple is captured into the closure |\n"
msgstr ""
"// --------------------------+\n"
"            // tuple is captured into the closure |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:1026
msgid "//                     |\n"
msgstr "//                     |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:1027
msgid "//                                     |\n"
msgstr "//                                     |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:1028
msgid "// 'c' and 'tuple' dropped here ------------+\n"
msgstr "// 'c' and 'tuple' dropped here ------------+\n"

#: src/types/pointer.md:11
msgid ""
"All pointers are explicit first-class values. They can be moved or copied, "
"stored into data structs, and returned from functions."
msgstr ""
"所有指针都是显式的一等值。它们可以被移动或复制，可以存储到数据结构中，也可以"
"从函数返回。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:17
msgid "References (`&` and `&mut`)"
msgstr "引用（`&` 和 `&mut`）"

#: src/types/pointer.md:25
msgid ""
"**<sup>Syntax</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-ReferenceType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[ReferenceType]"
"(pointer.md#railroad-ReferenceType)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">&</span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[Lifetime](../trait-"
"bounds.md#grammar-Lifetime)</span><sup>?</sup> <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">mut</span><sup>?</sup> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[TypeNoBounds]"
"(../types.md#grammar-TypeNoBounds)</span>"
msgstr ""
"**<sup>语法</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-ReferenceType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[ReferenceType]"
"(pointer.md#railroad-ReferenceType)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">&</span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[Lifetime](../trait-"
"bounds.md#grammar-Lifetime)</span><sup>?</sup> <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">mut</span><sup>?</sup> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[TypeNoBounds]"
"(../types.md#grammar-TypeNoBounds)</span>"

#: src/types/pointer.md:91
msgid "Shared references (`&`)"
msgstr "共享引用（`&`）"

#: src/types/pointer.md:97
msgid "Shared references point to memory which is owned by some other value."
msgstr "共享引用指向由某个其他值拥有的内存。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:103
msgid ""
"When a shared reference to a value is created, it prevents direct mutation "
"of the value. [Interior mutability](../interior-mutability.md) provides an "
"exception for this in certain circumstances. As the name suggests, any "
"number of shared references to a value may exist. A shared reference type is "
"written `&type`, or `&'a type` when you need to specify an explicit lifetime."
msgstr ""
"创建指向某个值的共享引用后，它会阻止对该值的直接变更。[内部可变性](../"
"interior-mutability.md)在某些情况下为此提供例外。顾名思义，可以存在任意数量的"
"指向同一个值的共享引用。共享引用类型写作 `&type`，在需要指定显式生命周期时写"
"作 `&'a type`。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:109
msgid ""
"Copying a reference is a \"shallow\" operation: it involves only copying the "
"pointer itself, that is, pointers are `Copy`. Releasing a reference has no "
"effect on the value it points to, but referencing of a [temporary value](../"
"expressions.md#temporaries) will keep it alive during the scope of the "
"reference itself."
msgstr ""
"复制引用是一种“浅”操作：它只涉及复制指针本身，也就是说，指针是 `Copy` 的。释"
"放一个引用不会影响它所指向的值，但对[临时值](../expressions.md#temporaries)的"
"引用会让该临时值在引用本身的作用域期间保持存活。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:115
msgid "Mutable references (`&mut`)"
msgstr "可变引用（`&mut`）"

#: src/types/pointer.md:121
msgid ""
"Mutable references point to memory which is owned by some other value. A "
"mutable reference type is written `&mut type` or `&'a mut type`."
msgstr ""
"可变引用指向由某个其他值拥有的内存。可变引用类型写作 `&mut type` 或 `&'a mut "
"type`。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:127
msgid ""
"A mutable reference (that hasn't been borrowed) is the only way to access "
"the value it points to, so is not `Copy`."
msgstr ""
"一个（尚未被借用的）可变引用是访问其所指向值的唯一方式，因此它不是 `Copy` "
"的。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:133
msgid "Raw pointers (`*const` and `*mut`)"
msgstr "裸指针（`*const` 和 `*mut`）"

#: src/types/pointer.md:141
msgid ""
"**<sup>Syntax</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-RawPointerType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[RawPointerType]"
"(pointer.md#railroad-RawPointerType)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">\\*</span> ( <span class=\"grammar-literal\">mut</span> | <span "
"class=\"grammar-literal\">const</span> ) <span class=\"grammar-"
"text\">[TypeNoBounds](../types.md#grammar-TypeNoBounds)</span>"
msgstr ""
"**<sup>语法</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-RawPointerType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[RawPointerType]"
"(pointer.md#railroad-RawPointerType)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">\\*</span> ( <span class=\"grammar-literal\">mut</span> | <span "
"class=\"grammar-literal\">const</span> ) <span class=\"grammar-"
"text\">[TypeNoBounds](../types.md#grammar-TypeNoBounds)</span>"

#: src/types/pointer.md:203
msgid ""
"Raw pointers are pointers without safety or liveness guarantees. Raw "
"pointers are written as `*const T` or `*mut T`. For example `*const i32` "
"means a raw pointer to a 32-bit integer."
msgstr ""
"裸指针是没有安全性或存活性保证的指针。裸指针写作 `*const T` 或 `*mut T`。例"
"如，`*const i32` 表示指向 32 位整数的裸指针。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:209
msgid ""
"Copying or dropping a raw pointer has no effect on the lifecycle of any "
"other value."
msgstr "复制或丢弃裸指针不会影响任何其他值的生命周期。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:215
msgid "Dereferencing a raw pointer is an [`unsafe` operation](../unsafety.md)."
msgstr "解引用裸指针是一种 [`unsafe` 操作](../unsafety.md)。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:217
msgid ""
"This can also be used to convert a raw pointer to a reference by reborrowing "
"it (`&*` or `&mut *`). Raw pointers are generally discouraged; they exist to "
"support interoperability with foreign code, and writing performance-critical "
"or low-level functions."
msgstr ""
"这也可以通过重新借用裸指针（`&*` 或 `&mut *`）来将它转换为引用。通常不鼓励使"
"用裸指针；它们的存在是为了支持与外部代码的互操作，以及编写性能关键或低层级函"
"数。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:223
msgid ""
"When comparing raw pointers they are compared by their address, rather than "
"by what they point to. When comparing raw pointers to [dynamically sized "
"types](../dynamically-sized-types.md) they also have their additional data "
"compared."
msgstr ""
"比较裸指针时，比较的是它们的地址，而不是它们所指向的内容。比较指向[动态大小类"
"型](../dynamically-sized-types.md)的裸指针时，还会比较它们的附加数据。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:229
msgid ""
"Raw pointers can be created directly using `&raw const` for `*const` "
"pointers and `&raw mut` for `*mut` pointers."
msgstr ""
"可以直接使用 `&raw const` 创建 `*const` 指针，使用 `&raw mut` 创建 `*mut` 指"
"针。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:235
msgid "Smart pointers"
msgstr "智能指针"

#: src/types/pointer.md:237
msgid ""
"The standard library contains additional 'smart pointer' types beyond "
"references and raw pointers."
msgstr "除了引用和裸指针之外，标准库还包含额外的“智能指针”类型。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:249
msgid ""
"Despite pointers and references being similar to `usize`s in the machine "
"code emitted on most platforms, the semantics of transmuting a reference or "
"pointer type to a non-pointer type is currently undecided. Thus, it may not "
"be valid to transmute a pointer or reference type, `P`, to a `[u8; size_of::"
"<P>()]`."
msgstr ""
"尽管在大多数平台生成的机器码中，指针和引用与 `usize` 类似，但将引用或指针类型"
"转换为非指针类型的语义目前尚未确定。因此，将指针或引用类型 `P` 转换为 `[u8; "
"size_of::<P>()]` 可能不是有效的。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:255
msgid ""
"For thin raw pointers (i.e., for `P = *const T` or `P = *mut T` for `T: "
"Sized`), the inverse direction (transmuting from an integer or array of "
"integers to `P`) is always valid. However, the pointer produced via such a "
"transmutation may not be dereferenced (not even if `T` has [size zero](../"
"glossary.md#r-glossary.zst))."
msgstr ""
"对于薄裸指针（即当 `T: Sized` 时，`P = *const T` 或 `P = *mut T`），反方向"
"（从整数或整数数组转换为 `P`）始终是有效的。不过，通过这种转换生成的指针不得"
"被解引用（即使 `T` 具有[零大小](../glossary.md#r-glossary.zst)也不行）。"

