#: src/types/trait-object.md:98
msgid ""
"A _trait object_ is an opaque value of another type that implements a set of "
"traits. The set of traits is made up of a [dyn compatible](../items/"
"traits.md#dyn-compatibility) _base trait_ plus any number of [auto traits]"
"(../special-types-and-traits.md#auto-traits)."
msgstr ""
"_trait 对象_ 是实现一组 trait 的某个其他类型的不透明值。这组 trait 由一个 "
"[dyn 兼容](../items/traits.md#dyn-compatibility)的 _基 trait_ 加任意数量的 "
"[auto trait](../special-types-and-traits.md#auto-traits)组成。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:104
msgid ""
"Trait objects implement the base trait, its auto traits, and any "
"[supertraits](../items/traits.md#supertraits) of the base trait."
msgstr ""
"trait 对象会实现基 trait、它的 auto trait，以及基 trait 的任何 [supertrait]"
"(../items/traits.md#supertraits)。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:110
msgid ""
"Trait objects are written as the keyword `dyn` followed by a set of trait "
"bounds, but with the following restrictions on the trait bounds."
msgstr ""
"trait 对象写作关键字 `dyn` 后跟一组 trait 约束，但这些 trait 约束有以下限制。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:116
msgid ""
"There may not be more than one non-auto trait, no more than one lifetime, "
"and opt-out bounds (e.g. `?Sized`) are not allowed. Furthermore, paths to "
"traits may be parenthesized."
msgstr ""
"非 auto trait 不得超过一个，生命周期不得超过一个，并且不允许使用选择退出的约"
"束（例如 `?Sized`）。此外，指向 trait 的路径可以加括号。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:118
msgid ""
"For example, given a trait `Trait`, the following are all trait objects:"
msgstr "例如，给定一个 trait `Trait`，以下都是 trait 对象："

#: src/types/trait-object.md:120 src/syntax-index.md:240
msgid "`dyn Trait`"
msgstr "`dyn Trait`"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:121
msgid "`dyn Trait + Send`"
msgstr "`dyn Trait + Send`"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:122
msgid "`dyn Trait + Send + Sync`"
msgstr "`dyn Trait + Send + Sync`"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:123
msgid "`dyn Trait + 'static`"
msgstr "`dyn Trait + 'static`"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:124
msgid "`dyn Trait + Send + 'static`"
msgstr "`dyn Trait + Send + 'static`"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:125
msgid "`dyn Trait +`"
msgstr "`dyn Trait +`"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:126
msgid "`dyn 'static + Trait`."
msgstr "`dyn 'static + Trait`."

#: src/types/trait-object.md:127
msgid "`dyn (Trait)`"
msgstr "`dyn (Trait)`"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:137
msgid "Before the 2021 edition, the `dyn` keyword may be omitted."
msgstr "在 2021 edition 之前，`dyn` 关键字可以省略。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:150
msgid ""
"In the 2015 edition, if the first bound of the trait object is a path that "
"starts with `::`, then the `dyn` will be treated as a part of the path. The "
"first path can be put in parenthesis to get around this. As such, if you "
"want a trait object with the trait `::your_module::Trait`, you should write "
"it as `dyn (::your_module::Trait)`."
msgstr ""
"在 2015 edition 中，如果 trait 对象的第一个约束是以 `::` 开头的路径，那么 "
"`dyn` 会被视为该路径的一部分。可以将第一个路径放入括号中来绕过这一点。因此，"
"如果你想要一个带有 trait `::your_module::Trait` 的 trait 对象，应写作 `dyn "
"(::your_module::Trait)`。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:152
msgid ""
"Beginning in the 2018 edition, `dyn` is a true keyword and is not allowed in "
"paths, so the parentheses are not necessary."
msgstr ""
"自 2018 edition 起，`dyn` 是真正的关键字，且不允许出现在路径中，因此括号不再"
"必要。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:161
msgid ""
"Two trait object types alias each other if the base traits alias each other "
"and if the sets of auto traits are the same and the lifetime bounds are the "
"same. For example, `dyn Trait + Send + UnwindSafe` is the same as `dyn Trait "
"+ UnwindSafe + Send`."
msgstr ""
"如果基 trait 互为别名，auto trait 的集合相同，并且生命周期约束相同，则两个 "
"trait 对象类型互为别名。例如，`dyn Trait + Send + UnwindSafe` 与 `dyn Trait "
"+ UnwindSafe + Send` 相同。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:167
msgid ""
"Due to the opaqueness of which concrete type the value is of, trait objects "
"are [dynamically sized types](../dynamically-sized-types.md). Like all <abbr "
"title=\"dynamically sized types\">DSTs</abbr>, trait objects are used behind "
"some type of pointer; for example `&dyn SomeTrait` or `Box<dyn SomeTrait>`. "
"Each instance of a pointer to a trait object includes:"
msgstr ""
"由于该值属于哪个具体类型是不透明的，trait 对象是[动态大小类型](../"
"dynamically-sized-types.md)。与所有 <abbr title=\"dynamically sized "
"types\">DST</abbr> 一样，trait 对象通过某种指针间接使用；例如 `&dyn "
"SomeTrait` 或 `Box<dyn SomeTrait>`。指向 trait 对象的指针的每个实例都包含："

#: src/types/trait-object.md:169
msgid "a pointer to an instance of a type `T` that implements `SomeTrait`"
msgstr "一个指向类型 `T` 的实例的指针，该类型实现了 `SomeTrait`"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:170
msgid ""
"a _virtual method table_, often just called a _vtable_, which contains, for "
"each method of `SomeTrait` and its [supertraits](../items/"
"traits.md#supertraits) that `T` implements, a pointer to `T`'s "
"implementation (i.e. a function pointer)."
msgstr ""
"一个_虚方法表_，通常直接称为 _vtable_，它针对 `T` 所实现的 `SomeTrait` 及其 "
"[supertrait](../items/traits.md#supertraits) 的每个方法，包含一个指向 `T` 的"
"实现的指针（即函数指针）。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:172
msgid ""
"The purpose of trait objects is to permit \"late binding\" of methods. "
"Calling a method on a trait object results in virtual dispatch at runtime: "
"that is, a function pointer is loaded from the trait object vtable and "
"invoked indirectly. The actual implementation for each vtable entry can vary "
"on an object-by-object basis."
msgstr ""
"trait 对象的目的是允许方法的“后期绑定”。在 trait 对象上调用方法会在运行时产生"
"虚分派：也就是说，从 trait 对象的 vtable 中加载一个函数指针，并间接调用它。每"
"个 vtable 条目的实际实现可以因对象而异。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:174
msgid "An example of a trait object:"
msgstr "trait 对象的示例："

#: src/types/trait-object.md:194
msgid ""
"In this example, the trait `Printable` occurs as a trait object in both the "
"type signature of `print`, and the cast expression in `main`."
msgstr ""
"在此示例中，trait `Printable` 在 `print` 的类型签名和 `main` 中的转换表达式里"
"都作为 trait 对象出现。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:200
msgid "Trait object lifetime bounds"
msgstr "trait 对象生命周期约束"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:202
msgid ""
"Since a trait object can contain references, the lifetimes of those "
"references need to be expressed as part of the trait object. This lifetime "
"is written as `Trait + 'a`. There are [defaults](../lifetime-"
"elision.md#default-trait-object-lifetimes) that allow this lifetime to "
"usually be inferred with a sensible choice."
msgstr ""
"由于 trait 对象可以包含引用，这些引用的生命周期需要作为 trait 对象的一部分表"
"达出来。这个生命周期写作 `Trait + 'a`。存在一些[默认值](../lifetime-"
"elision.md#default-trait-object-lifetimes)，使得该生命周期通常可以被推断为一"
"个合理的选择。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:5
msgid "Impl trait"
msgstr "impl Trait"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:13
msgid ""
"**<sup>Syntax</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-ImplTraitType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[ImplTraitType]"
"(impl-trait.md#railroad-ImplTraitType)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">impl</span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[Bounds](../trait-"
"bounds.md#grammar-Bounds)</span>"
msgstr ""
"**<sup>语法</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-ImplTraitType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[ImplTraitType]"
"(impl-trait.md#railroad-ImplTraitType)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">impl</span> <span class=\"grammar-text\">[Bounds](../trait-"
"bounds.md#grammar-Bounds)</span>"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:17
msgid ""
"<span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" id=\"grammar-"
"ImplTraitTypeOneBound\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[ImplTraitTypeOneBound]"
"(impl-trait.md#railroad-ImplTraitTypeOneBound)</span> → <span "
"class=\"grammar-literal\">impl</span> <span class=\"grammar-"
"text\">[TraitBound](../trait-bounds.md#grammar-TraitBound)</span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" id=\"grammar-"
"ImplTraitTypeOneBound\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[ImplTraitTypeOneBound]"
"(impl-trait.md#railroad-ImplTraitTypeOneBound)</span> → <span "
"class=\"grammar-literal\">impl</span> <span class=\"grammar-"
"text\">[TraitBound](../trait-bounds.md#grammar-TraitBound)</span>"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:92
msgid ""
"`impl Trait` provides ways to specify unnamed but concrete types that "
"implement a specific trait. It can appear in two sorts of places: argument "
"position (where it can act as an anonymous type parameter to functions), and "
"return position (where it can act as an abstract return type)."
msgstr ""
"`impl Trait` 提供了指定未命名但具体、且实现某个特定 trait 的类型的方式。它可"
"以出现在两类位置：实参位置（此时它可以充当函数的匿名类型形参）和返回位置（此"
"时它可以充当抽象返回类型）。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:97
msgid "// argument position: anonymous type parameter\n"
msgstr "// 实参位置：匿名类型形参\n"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:101
msgid "// return position: abstract return type\n"
msgstr "// 返回位置：抽象返回类型\n"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:110
msgid "Anonymous type parameters"
msgstr "匿名类型形参"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:116
msgid ""
"This is often called \"impl Trait in argument position\". (The term "
"\"parameter\" is more correct here, but \"impl Trait in argument position\" "
"is the phrasing used during the development of this feature, and it remains "
"in parts of the implementation.)"
msgstr ""
"这通常称为“实参位置中的 impl Trait”。（这里使用“形参”这个术语更准确，但“实参"
"位置中的 impl Trait”是此特性开发期间使用的表述，并且仍保留在部分实现中。）"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:125
msgid ""
"Functions can use `impl` followed by a set of trait bounds to declare a "
"parameter as having an anonymous type. The caller must provide a type that "
"satisfies the bounds declared by the anonymous type parameter, and the "
"function can only use the methods available through the trait bounds of the "
"anonymous type parameter."
msgstr ""
"函数可以使用 `impl` 后跟一组 trait 约束，将一个形参声明为具有匿名类型。调用者"
"必须提供满足该匿名类型形参所声明约束的类型，而函数只能使用通过该匿名类型形参"
"的 trait 约束可用的方法。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:127
msgid "For example, these two forms are almost equivalent:"
msgstr "例如，这两种形式几乎等价："

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:131
msgid "// generic type parameter\n"
msgstr "// 泛型类型形参\n"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:135
msgid "// impl Trait in argument position\n"
msgstr "// 实参位置中的 impl Trait\n"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:145
msgid ""
"That is, `impl Trait` in argument position is syntactic sugar for a generic "
"type parameter like `<T: Trait>`, except that the type is anonymous and "
"doesn't appear in the [GenericParams](../items/generics.md#grammar-"
"GenericParams) list."
msgstr ""
"也就是说，实参位置中的 `impl Trait` 是类似 `<T: Trait>` 的泛型类型形参的语法"
"糖，只不过该类型是匿名的，并且不会出现在 [GenericParams](../items/"
"generics.md#grammar-GenericParams) 列表中。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:151
msgid ""
"For function parameters, generic type parameters and `impl Trait` are not "
"exactly equivalent. With a generic parameter such as `<T: Trait>`, the "
"caller has the option to explicitly specify the generic argument for `T` at "
"the call site using [GenericArgs](../paths.md#grammar-GenericArgs), for "
"example, `foo::<usize>(1)`. Changing a parameter from either one to the "
"other can constitute a breaking change for the callers of a function, since "
"this changes the number of generic arguments."
msgstr ""
"对于函数形参，泛型类型形参和 `impl Trait` 并不完全等价。对于像 `<T: Trait>` "
"这样的泛型形参，调用者可以选择在调用点使用 [GenericArgs](../paths.md#grammar-"
"GenericArgs) 显式指定 `T` 的泛型实参，例如 `foo::<usize>(1)`。将一个形参从其"
"中一种形式改为另一种形式，可能构成对函数调用者的破坏性变更，因为这会改变泛型"
"实参的数量。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:160
msgid "Abstract return types"
msgstr "抽象返回类型"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:166
msgid "This is often called \"impl Trait in return position\"."
msgstr "这通常称为“返回位置中的 impl Trait”。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:175
msgid ""
"Functions can use `impl Trait` to return an abstract return type. These "
"types stand in for another concrete type where the caller may only use the "
"methods declared by the specified `Trait`."
msgstr ""
"函数可以使用 `impl Trait` 来返回抽象返回类型。这些类型代表另一个具体类型，而"
"调用者只能使用由指定 `Trait` 声明的方法。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:181
msgid ""
"Each possible return value from the function must resolve to the same "
"concrete type."
msgstr "函数中每一个可能的返回值都必须解析为同一个具体类型。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:183
msgid ""
"`impl Trait` in return position allows a function to return an unboxed "
"abstract type. This is particularly useful with [closures](closure.md) and "
"iterators. For example, closures have a unique, un-writable type. "
"Previously, the only way to return a closure from a function was to use a "
"[trait object](trait-object.md):"
msgstr ""
"返回位置中的 `impl Trait` 允许函数返回未装箱的抽象类型。这对[闭包]"
"(closure.md)和迭代器特别有用。例如，闭包具有唯一且无法写出的类型。以前，从函"
"数返回闭包的唯一方式是使用 [trait 对象](trait-object.md)："

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:191
msgid ""
"This could incur performance penalties from heap allocation and dynamic "
"dispatch. It wasn't possible to fully specify the type of the closure, only "
"to use the `Fn` trait. That means that the trait object is necessary. "
"However, with `impl Trait`, it is possible to write this more simply:"
msgstr ""
"这可能因堆分配和动态分派而带来性能损耗。以前无法完整指定闭包的类型，只能使用 "
"`Fn` trait。这意味着 trait 对象是必要的。然而，使用 `impl Trait` 可以更简单地"
"写成："

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:199
msgid "which also avoids the drawbacks of using a boxed trait object."
msgstr "这也避免了使用装箱 trait 对象的缺点。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:201
msgid ""
"Similarly, the concrete types of iterators could become very complex, "
"incorporating the types of all previous iterators in a chain. Returning "
"`impl Iterator` means that a function only exposes the `Iterator` trait as a "
"bound on its return type, instead of explicitly specifying all of the other "
"iterator types involved."
msgstr ""
"类似地，迭代器的具体类型可能变得非常复杂，包含链中所有先前迭代器的类型。返回 "
"`impl Iterator` 意味着函数只在其返回类型上暴露 `Iterator` trait 作为约束，而"
"不是显式指定所涉及的所有其他迭代器类型。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:207
msgid "Return-position `impl Trait` in traits and trait implementations"
msgstr "trait 和 trait 实现中的返回位置 `impl Trait`"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:213
msgid ""
"Functions in traits may also use `impl Trait` as a syntax for an anonymous "
"associated type."
msgstr "trait 中的函数也可以使用 `impl Trait` 作为匿名关联类型的语法。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:219
msgid ""
"Every `impl Trait` in the return type of an associated function in a trait "
"is desugared to an anonymous associated type. The return type that appears "
"in the implementation's function signature is used to determine the value of "
"the associated type."
msgstr ""
"trait 中关联函数的返回类型里的每个 `impl Trait` 都会被脱糖为一个匿名关联类"
"型。实现的函数签名中出现的返回类型用于确定该关联类型的值。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:225
msgid "Capturing"
msgstr "捕获"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:227
msgid ""
"Behind each return-position `impl Trait` abstract type is some hidden "
"concrete type.  For this concrete type to use a generic parameter, that "
"generic parameter must be _captured_ by the abstract type."
msgstr ""
"每个返回位置 `impl Trait` 抽象类型背后都有某个隐藏的具体类型。要让这个具体类"
"型使用某个泛型形参，该泛型形参必须被该抽象类型_捕获_。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:233
msgid "Automatic capturing"
msgstr "自动捕获"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:239
msgid ""
"Return-position `impl Trait` abstract types automatically capture all in-"
"scope generic parameters, including generic type, const, and lifetime "
"parameters (including higher-ranked ones)."
msgstr ""
"返回位置 `impl Trait` 抽象类型会自动捕获所有作用域内泛型形参，包括泛型类型、"
"const 和生命周期形参（包括高阶生命周期形参）。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:249
msgid ""
"Before the 2024 edition, on free functions and on associated functions and "
"methods of inherent impls, generic lifetime parameters that do not appear in "
"the bounds of the abstract return type are not automatically captured."
msgstr ""
"在 2024 edition 之前，对于自由函数以及固有 impl 的关联函数和方法，未出现在抽"
"象返回类型约束中的泛型生命周期形参不会被自动捕获。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:258
msgid "Precise capturing"
msgstr "精确捕获"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:264
msgid ""
"The set of generic parameters captured by a return-position `impl Trait` "
"abstract type may be explicitly controlled with a [`use<..>` bound](../trait-"
"bounds.md#use-bounds).  If present, only the generic parameters listed in "
"the `use<..>` bound will be captured.  E.g.:"
msgstr ""
"返回位置 `impl Trait` 抽象类型所捕获的泛型形参集合，可以通过 [`use<..>` 约束]"
"(../trait-bounds.md#use-bounds)显式控制。如果存在该约束，则只有列在 "
"`use<..>` 约束中的泛型形参会被捕获。例如："

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:268
msgid ""
"//                                      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n"
"  //                                     Captures `'a` and `T` only.\n"
msgstr ""
"//                                      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n"
"  //                                     只捕获 `'a` 和 `T`。\n"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:278
msgid ""
"Currently, only one `use<..>` bound may be present in a bounds list, all in-"
"scope type and const generic parameters must be included, and all lifetime "
"parameters that appear in other bounds of the abstract type must be included."
msgstr ""
"目前，一个约束列表中最多只能出现一个 `use<..>` 约束，必须包含所有作用域内类型"
"和 const 泛型形参，并且必须包含所有出现在该抽象类型其他约束中的生命周期形参。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:284
msgid ""
"Within the `use<..>` bound, any lifetime parameters present must appear "
"before all type and const generic parameters, and the elided lifetime (`'_`) "
"may be present if it is otherwise allowed to appear within the `impl Trait` "
"return type."
msgstr ""
"在 `use<..>` 约束内，任何出现的生命周期形参都必须位于所有类型和 const 泛型形"
"参之前；如果省略生命周期 (`'_`) 原本允许出现在 `impl Trait` 返回类型内，那么"
"它可以出现。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:290
msgid ""
"Because all in-scope type parameters must be included by name, a `use<..>` "
"bound may not be used in the signature of items that use argument-position "
"`impl Trait`, as those items have anonymous type parameters in scope."
msgstr ""
"由于所有作用域内类型形参都必须按名称包含，`use<..>` 约束不得用于使用实参位置 "
"`impl Trait` 的项的签名中，因为这些项的作用域内有匿名类型形参。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:296
msgid ""
"Any `use<..>` bound that is present in an associated function in a trait "
"definition must include all generic parameters of the trait, including the "
"implicit `Self` generic type parameter of the trait."
msgstr ""
"trait 定义中的关联函数里出现的任何 `use<..>` 约束，都必须包含该 trait 的所有"
"泛型形参，包括该 trait 隐式的 `Self` 泛型类型形参。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:298
msgid "Differences between generics and `impl Trait` in return position"
msgstr "返回位置中泛型与 `impl Trait` 的差异"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:300
msgid ""
"In argument position, `impl Trait` is very similar in semantics to a generic "
"type parameter. However, there are significant differences between the two "
"in return position. With `impl Trait`, unlike with a generic type parameter, "
"the function chooses the return type, and the caller cannot choose the "
"return type."
msgstr ""
"在实参位置，`impl Trait` 在语义上非常类似于泛型类型形参。然而，二者在返回位置"
"中存在显著差异。使用 `impl Trait` 时，与使用泛型类型形参不同，函数会选择返回"
"类型，而调用者不能选择返回类型。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:302 src/types/impl-trait.md:314
msgid "The function:"
msgstr "函数："

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:312
msgid ""
"allows the caller to determine the return type, `T`, and the function "
"returns that type."
msgstr "允许调用者确定返回类型 `T`，并且该函数返回该类型。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:324
msgid ""
"doesn't allow the caller to determine the return type. Instead, the function "
"chooses the return type, but only promises that it will implement `Trait`."
msgstr ""
"不允许调用者确定返回类型。相反，该函数会选择返回类型，但只承诺它会实现 "
"`Trait`。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:332
msgid ""
"`impl Trait` can only appear as a parameter or return type of a non-`extern` "
"function. It cannot be the type of a `let` binding, field type, or appear "
"inside a type alias."
msgstr ""
"`impl Trait` 只能作为非 `extern` 函数的形参或返回类型出现。它不能作为 `let` "
"绑定的类型、字段类型，也不能出现在类型别名内部。"

#: src/types/parameters.md:7
msgid ""
"Within the body of an item that has type parameter declarations, the names "
"of its type parameters are types:"
msgstr "在具有类型参数声明的项的主体内，其类型参数的名称就是类型："

#: src/types/parameters.md:21
msgid ""
"Here, `first` has type `A`, referring to `to_vec`'s `A` type parameter; and "
"`rest` has type `Vec<A>`, a vector with element type `A`."
msgstr ""
"这里，`first` 的类型为 `A`，指代 `to_vec` 的 `A` 类型参数；而 `rest` 的类型"
"为 `Vec<A>`，即元素类型为 `A` 的 vector。"

#: src/types/inferred.md:13
msgid ""
"**<sup>Syntax</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-InferredType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[InferredType]"
"(inferred.md#railroad-InferredType)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">\\_</span>"
msgstr ""
"**<sup>语法</sup>** <br> <span class=\"grammar-text grammar-production\" "
"id=\"grammar-InferredType\" onclick=\"show_railroad()\">[InferredType]"
"(inferred.md#railroad-InferredType)</span> → <span class=\"grammar-"
"literal\">\\_</span>"

#: src/types/inferred.md:49
msgid ""
"The inferred type asks the compiler to infer the type if possible based on "
"the surrounding information available."
msgstr "推断类型要求编译器在可能时基于周围可用的信息推断类型。"

#: src/types/inferred.md:55
msgid "The inferred type is often used in generic arguments:"
msgstr "推断类型常用于泛型实参："

#: src/types/inferred.md:68
msgid "The inferred type cannot be used in item signatures."
msgstr "推断类型不能用于项签名。"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:11
msgid ""
"Most types have a fixed size that is known at compile time and implement the "
"trait [`Sized`](special-types-and-traits.md#sized). A type with a size that "
"is known only at run-time is called a _dynamically sized type_ (_DST_) or, "
"informally, an unsized type.  [Slices](types/slice.md), [trait objects]"
"(types/trait-object.md), and [str](types/str.md) are examples of <abbr "
"title=\"dynamically sized types\">DSTs</abbr>."
msgstr ""
"大多数类型都有在编译时已知的固定大小，并实现 trait [`Sized`](special-types-"
"and-traits.md#sized)。大小只有在运行时才知道的类型称为_动态大小类型_"
"（_DST_），非正式地也称为 unsized 类型。[切片](types/slice.md)、[trait 对象]"
"(types/trait-object.md) 和 [str](types/str.md) 是 <abbr title=\"dynamically "
"sized types\">DSTs</abbr> 的例子。"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:17
msgid "Such types can only be used in certain cases:"
msgstr "这类类型只能在某些情况下使用："

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:23
msgid ""
"[Pointer types](types/pointer.md) to <abbr title=\"dynamically sized "
"types\">DSTs</abbr> are sized but have twice the size of pointers to sized "
"types"
msgstr ""
"指向 <abbr title=\"dynamically sized types\">DSTs</abbr> 的[指针类型](types/"
"pointer.md) 是有大小的，但其大小是指向有大小类型的指针的两倍"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:24
msgid "Pointers to slices and `str` also store the number of elements."
msgstr "指向切片和 `str` 的指针还会存储元素数量。"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:25
msgid "Pointers to trait objects also store a pointer to a vtable."
msgstr "指向 trait 对象的指针还会存储一个指向 vtable 的指针。"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:31
msgid ""
"<abbr title=\"dynamically sized types\">DSTs</abbr> can be provided as type "
"arguments to generic type parameters having the special `?Sized` bound. They "
"can also be used for associated type definitions when the corresponding "
"associated type declaration has a `?Sized` bound. By default, any type "
"parameter or associated type has a `Sized` bound, unless it is relaxed using "
"`?Sized`."
msgstr ""
"<abbr title=\"dynamically sized types\">DSTs</abbr> 可以作为类型实参提供给具"
"有特殊 `?Sized` 边界的泛型类型形参。当对应的关联类型声明具有 `?Sized` 边界"
"时，它们也可以用于关联类型定义。默认情况下，任何类型形参或关联类型都有 "
"`Sized` 边界，除非使用 `?Sized` 将其放宽。"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:37
msgid ""
"Traits may be implemented for <abbr title=\"dynamically sized\n"
"types\">DSTs</abbr>. Unlike with generic type parameters, `Self: ?Sized` is "
"the default in trait definitions."
msgstr ""
"可以为 <abbr title=\"dynamically sized\n"
"types\">DSTs</abbr> 实现 trait。与泛型类型形参不同，在 trait 定义中 `Self: ?"
"Sized` 是默认情况。"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:44
msgid ""
"Structs may contain a <abbr title=\"dynamically sized type\">DST</abbr> as "
"the last field; this makes the struct itself a <abbr title=\"dynamically "
"sized type\">DST</abbr>."
msgstr ""
"结构体可以包含一个 <abbr title=\"dynamically sized type\">DST</abbr> 作为最后"
"一个字段；这会使该结构体本身成为一个 <abbr title=\"dynamically sized "
"type\">DST</abbr>。"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:50
msgid ""
"[Variables](variables.md), function parameters, [const](items/constant-"
"items.md) items, and [static](items/static-items.md) items must be `Sized`."
msgstr ""
"[变量](variables.md)、函数形参、[const](items/constant-items.md) 项和 "
"[static](items/static-items.md) 项必须是 `Sized`。"

#: src/type-layout.md:11
msgid ""
"The layout of a type is its size, alignment, and the relative offsets of its "
"fields. For enums, how the discriminant is laid out and interpreted is also "
"part of type layout."
msgstr ""
"类型的布局包括它的大小、对齐以及其字段的相对偏移量。对于 enum，判别值如何布局"
"和解释也属于类型布局的一部分。"

#: src/type-layout.md:17
msgid ""
"Type layout can be changed with each compilation. Instead of trying to "
"document exactly what is done, we only document what is guaranteed today."
msgstr ""
"类型布局可能随每次编译而改变。我们不试图记录实际具体做了什么，而只记录目前保"
"证的内容。"

#: src/type-layout.md:19
msgid ""
"Note that even types with the same layout can still differ in how they are "
"passed across function boundaries. For function call ABI compatibility of "
"types, see [here](../core/primitive.fn.md#abi-compatibility)."
msgstr ""
"注意，即使两个类型具有相同布局，它们跨函数边界传递的方式仍可能不同。关于类型"
"的函数调用 ABI 兼容性，见[这里](../core/primitive.fn.md#abi-compatibility)。"

#: src/type-layout.md:25
msgid "Size and alignment"
msgstr "大小和对齐"

#: src/type-layout.md:27
msgid "All values have an alignment and size."
msgstr "所有值都有对齐和大小。"

#: src/type-layout.md:33
msgid ""
"The _alignment_ of a value specifies what addresses are valid to store the "
"value at. A value of alignment `n` must only be stored at an address that is "
"a multiple of n. For example, a value with an alignment of 2 must be stored "
"at an even address, while a value with an alignment of 1 can be stored at "
"any address. Alignment is measured in bytes, and must be at least 1, and "
"always a power of 2. The alignment of a value can be checked with the "
"[`align_of_val`](../core/mem/fn.align_of_val.html) function."
msgstr ""
"值的 _对齐_ 指定了哪些地址可用于存储该值。对齐为 `n` 的值只能存储在地址值为 "
"n 的倍数的地址处。例如，对齐为 2 的值必须存储在偶数地址，而对齐为 1 的值可以"
"存储在任意地址。对齐以字节为单位，必须至少为 1，并且始终是 2 的幂。可以使用 "
"[`align_of_val`](../core/mem/fn.align_of_val.html) 函数检查值的对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:39
msgid ""
"The _size_ of a value is the offset in bytes between successive elements in "
"an array with that item type including alignment padding. The size of a "
"value is always a multiple of its alignment. Note that some types are [zero-"
"sized](glossary.md#r-glossary.zst); 0 is considered a multiple of any "
"alignment (for example, on some platforms, the type `[u16; 0]` has size 0 "
"and alignment 2). The size of a value can be checked with the [`size_of_val`]"
"(../core/mem/fn.size_of_val.html) function."
msgstr ""
"值的 _大小_ 是具有该元素类型的数组中相邻元素之间的字节偏移量，包括对齐填充。"
"值的大小始终是其对齐的倍数。注意，某些类型是[零大小](glossary.md#r-"
"glossary.zst)；0 被视为任何对齐的倍数（例如，在某些平台上，类型 `[u16; 0]` 的"
"大小为 0、对齐为 2）。可以使用 [`size_of_val`](../core/mem/"
"fn.size_of_val.html) 函数检查值的大小。"

#: src/type-layout.md:45
msgid ""
"Types where all values have the same size and alignment, and both are known "
"at compile time, implement the [`Sized`](../core/marker/trait.Sized.html) "
"trait and can be checked with the [`size_of`](../core/mem/fn.size_of.html) "
"and [`align_of`](../core/mem/fn.align_of.html) functions. Types that are not "
"[`Sized`](../core/marker/trait.Sized.html) are known as [dynamically sized "
"types](dynamically-sized-types.md). Since all values of a `Sized` type share "
"the same size and alignment, we refer to those shared values as the size of "
"the type and the alignment of the type respectively."
msgstr ""
"所有值都具有相同大小和对齐，且二者在编译时已知的类型，实现 [`Sized`](../core/"
"marker/trait.Sized.html) trait，并可用 [`size_of`](../core/mem/"
"fn.size_of.html) 和 [`align_of`](../core/mem/fn.align_of.html) 函数检查。不"
"是 [`Sized`](../core/marker/trait.Sized.html) 的类型称为[动态大小类型]"
"(dynamically-sized-types.md)。由于 `Sized` 类型的所有值共享相同的大小和对齐，"
"我们分别将这些共享的量称为该类型的大小和该类型的对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:51
msgid "Primitive data layout"
msgstr "原始数据布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:57
msgid "The size of most primitives is given in this table."
msgstr "大多数原始类型的大小见下表。"

#: src/type-layout.md:59
msgid "`size_of::<Type>()`"
msgstr "`size_of::<Type>()`"

#: src/type-layout.md:61 src/type-layout.md:62
msgid "1"
msgstr "1"

#: src/type-layout.md:62
msgid "`u8` / `i8`"
msgstr "`u8` / `i8`"

#: src/type-layout.md:63
msgid "`u16` / `i16`"
msgstr "`u16` / `i16`"

#: src/type-layout.md:63
msgid "2"
msgstr "2"

#: src/type-layout.md:64
msgid "`u32` / `i32`"
msgstr "`u32` / `i32`"

#: src/type-layout.md:64 src/type-layout.md:68 src/type-layout.md:70
msgid "4"
msgstr "4"

#: src/type-layout.md:65
msgid "`u64` / `i64`"
msgstr "`u64` / `i64`"

#: src/type-layout.md:65 src/type-layout.md:69
msgid "8"
msgstr "8"

#: src/type-layout.md:66
msgid "`u128` / `i128`"
msgstr "`u128` / `i128`"

#: src/type-layout.md:66
msgid "16"
msgstr "16"

#: src/type-layout.md:67
msgid "`usize` / `isize`"
msgstr "`usize` / `isize`"

#: src/type-layout.md:67
msgid "See below"
msgstr "见下文"

#: src/type-layout.md:68 src/inline-assembly.md:1765
#: src/inline-assembly.md:1770
msgid "`f32`"
msgstr "`f32`"

#: src/type-layout.md:69 src/inline-assembly.md:1766
#: src/inline-assembly.md:1771
msgid "`f64`"
msgstr "`f64`"

#: src/type-layout.md:76
msgid ""
"`usize` and `isize` have a size big enough to contain every address on the "
"target platform. For example, on a 32 bit target, this is 4 bytes, and on a "
"64 bit target, this is 8 bytes."
msgstr ""
"`usize` 和 `isize` 的大小足以容纳目标平台上的每个地址。例如，在 32 位目标上"
"为 4 字节，在 64 位目标上为 8 字节。"

#: src/type-layout.md:82
msgid "`usize` and `isize` have the same size and alignment."
msgstr "`usize` 和 `isize` 具有相同的大小和对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:88
msgid ""
"The alignment of primitives is platform-specific. In most cases, their "
"alignment is equal to their size, but it may be less. In particular, `i128` "
"and `u128` are often aligned to 4 or 8 bytes even though their size is 16, "
"and on many 32-bit platforms, `i64`, `u64`, and `f64` are only aligned to 4 "
"bytes, not 8."
msgstr ""
"原始类型的对齐是平台特定的。大多数情况下，它们的对齐等于其大小，但也可能更"
"小。特别是，`i128` 和 `u128` 虽然大小为 16，却通常按 4 或 8 字节对齐；在许多 "
"32 位平台上，`i64`、`u64` 和 `f64` 只按 4 字节而不是 8 字节对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:94
msgid ""
"Alignment is guaranteed to be the same for fixed-width signed and unsigned "
"integer variants of the same indicated size --- that is, for a given size "
"`N`, `align_of::<uN>() == align_of::<iN>()`."
msgstr ""
"保证同一指定位宽的定宽有符号和无符号整数变体具有相同对齐——也就是说，对于给定"
"大小 `N`，`align_of::<uN>() == align_of::<iN>()`。"

#: src/type-layout.md:100
msgid "Pointers and references layout"
msgstr "指针和引用布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:106
msgid ""
"Pointers and references have the same layout. Mutability of the pointer or "
"reference does not change the layout."
msgstr "指针和引用具有相同布局。指针或引用的可变性不会改变布局。"

#: src/type-layout.md:112
msgid "Pointers to sized types have the same size and alignment as `usize`."
msgstr "指向有大小类型的指针具有与 `usize` 相同的大小和对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:118
msgid ""
"Pointers to unsized types are sized. The size and alignment of a pointer to "
"an unsized type are each guaranteed to be greater than or equal to those of "
"a pointer to a sized type."
msgstr ""
"指向无大小类型的指针是有大小的。保证指向无大小类型的指针的大小和对齐分别大于"
"或等于指向有大小类型的指针的大小和对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:124
msgid ""
"Though you should not rely on this, all pointers to <abbr "
"title=\"Dynamically Sized Types\">DSTs</abbr> are currently twice the size "
"of the size of `usize` and have the same alignment."
msgstr ""
"尽管你不应依赖这一点，但目前所有指向 <abbr title=\"Dynamically Sized "
"Types\">DSTs</abbr> 的指针的大小都是 `usize` 大小的两倍，并具有相同的对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:133
msgid "Array layout"
msgstr "数组布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:135
msgid ""
"An array of `[T; N]` has a size of `size_of::<T>() * N` and the same "
"alignment of `T`. Arrays are laid out so that the zero-based `nth` element "
"of the array is offset from the start of the array by `n * size_of::<T>()` "
"bytes."
msgstr ""
"`[T; N]` 数组的大小为 `size_of::<T>() * N`，并具有与 `T` 相同的对齐。数组的布"
"局使得数组中从零开始计数的 `nth` 元素相对于数组开头的偏移量为 `n * size_of::"
"<T>()` 字节。"

#: src/type-layout.md:141
msgid "Slice layout"
msgstr "切片布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:143
msgid "Slices have the same layout as the section of the array they slice."
msgstr "切片与其切取的数组区段具有相同布局。"

#: src/type-layout.md:149
msgid ""
"This is about the raw `[T]` type, not pointers (`&[T]`, `Box<[T]>`, etc.) to "
"slices."
msgstr ""
"这里说的是原始 `[T]` 类型，而不是指向切片的指针（`&[T]`、`Box<[T]>` 等）。"

#: src/type-layout.md:158
msgid "`str` Layout"
msgstr "`str` 布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:160
msgid ""
"String slices are a UTF-8 representation of characters that have the same "
"layout as slices of type `[u8]`. A reference `&str` has the same layout as a "
"reference `&[u8]`."
msgstr ""
"字符串切片是字符的 UTF-8 表示，其布局与类型 `[u8]` 的切片相同。引用 `&str` 与"
"引用 `&[u8]` 具有相同布局。"

#: src/type-layout.md:166
msgid "Tuple layout"
msgstr "元组布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:172
msgid ""
"Tuples are laid out according to the [`Rust` representation](#the-rust-"
"representation)."
msgstr "元组按照 [`Rust` 表示](#the-rust-representation)进行布局。"

#: src/type-layout.md:178
msgid ""
"The exception to this is the unit tuple (`()`), which is guaranteed as a "
"[zero-sized type](glossary.md#r-glossary.zst) to have a size of 0 and an "
"alignment of 1."
msgstr ""
"例外是单元元组（`()`），保证它作为[零大小类型](glossary.md#r-glossary.zst)具"
"有大小 0 和对齐 1。"

#: src/type-layout.md:184
msgid "Trait object layout"
msgstr "trait 对象布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:186
msgid "Trait objects have the same layout as the value the trait object is of."
msgstr "trait 对象与其所表示的值具有相同布局。"

#: src/type-layout.md:192
msgid ""
"This is about the raw trait object types, not pointers (`&dyn Trait`, "
"`Box<dyn Trait>`, etc.) to trait objects."
msgstr ""
"这里说的是原始 trait 对象类型，而不是指向 trait 对象的指针（`&dyn Trait`、"
"`Box<dyn Trait>` 等）。"

#: src/type-layout.md:201
msgid "Closure layout"
msgstr "闭包布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:203
msgid "Closures have no layout guarantees."
msgstr "闭包没有布局保证。"

#: src/type-layout.md:209
msgid "Representations"
msgstr "表示"

#: src/type-layout.md:215
msgid ""
"All user-defined composite types (`struct`s, `enum`s, and `union`s) have a "
"_representation_ that specifies what the layout is for the type."
msgstr ""
"所有用户定义的复合类型（`struct`、`enum` 和 `union`）都有一个 _表示_，用于指"
"定该类型的布局。"

#: src/type-layout.md:221
msgid "The possible representations for a type are:"
msgstr "类型可能具有的表示有："

#: src/type-layout.md:223
msgid "[`Rust`](#the-rust-representation) (default)"
msgstr "[`Rust`](#the-rust-representation)（默认）"

#: src/type-layout.md:224
msgid "[`C`](#the-c-representation)"
msgstr "[`C`](#the-c-representation)"

#: src/type-layout.md:225
msgid "The [primitive representations](#primitive-representations)"
msgstr "[原始表示](#primitive-representations)"

#: src/type-layout.md:226
msgid "[`transparent`](#the-transparent-representation)"
msgstr "[`transparent`](#the-transparent-representation)"

#: src/type-layout.md:232
msgid ""
"The representation of a type can be changed by applying the `repr` attribute "
"to it. The following example shows a struct with a `C` representation."
msgstr ""
"可以通过对类型应用 `repr` 属性来改变类型的表示。下面的示例展示了一个具有 `C` "
"表示的 struct。"

#: src/type-layout.md:247
msgid ""
"The alignment may be raised or lowered with the `align` and `packed` "
"modifiers respectively. They alter the representation specified in the "
"attribute. If no representation is specified, the default one is altered."
msgstr ""
"可以分别使用 `align` 和 `packed` 修饰符提高或降低对齐。它们会更改属性中指定的"
"表示。如果未指定表示，则会更改默认表示。"

#: src/type-layout.md:250
msgid "// Default representation, alignment lowered to 2.\n"
msgstr "// 默认表示，对齐降低为 2。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:257
msgid "// C representation, alignment raised to 8\n"
msgstr "// C 表示，对齐提高为 8\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:271
msgid ""
"As a consequence of the representation being an attribute on the item, the "
"representation does not depend on generic parameters. Any two types with the "
"same name have the same representation. For example, `Foo<Bar>` and "
"`Foo<Baz>` both have the same representation."
msgstr ""
"由于表示是项上的属性，表示不依赖于泛型参数。任何两个具有相同名称的类型都有相"
"同表示。例如，`Foo<Bar>` 和 `Foo<Baz>` 都具有相同表示。"

#: src/type-layout.md:280
msgid ""
"The representation of a type can change the padding between fields, but does "
"not change the layout of the fields themselves. For example, a struct with a "
"`C` representation that contains a struct `Inner` with the `Rust` "
"representation will not change the layout of `Inner`."
msgstr ""
"类型的表示可以改变字段之间的填充，但不会改变字段本身的布局。例如，一个具有 "
"`C` 表示的 struct，如果包含一个具有 `Rust` 表示的 struct `Inner`，则不会改变 "
"`Inner` 的布局。"

#: src/type-layout.md:282
msgid "<a id=\"the-default-representation\"></a>"
msgstr "<a id=\"the-default-representation\"></a>"

#: src/type-layout.md:287
msgid "The `Rust` representation"
msgstr "`Rust` 表示"

#: src/type-layout.md:293
msgid ""
"The `Rust` representation is the default representation for nominal types "
"without a `repr` attribute. Using this representation explicitly through a "
"`repr` attribute is guaranteed to be the same as omitting the attribute "
"entirely."
msgstr ""
"`Rust` 表示是没有 `repr` 属性的名义类型的默认表示。通过 `repr` 属性显式使用此"
"表示，保证与完全省略该属性相同。"

#: src/type-layout.md:299
msgid ""
"The only data layout guarantees made by this representation are those "
"required for soundness. These are:"
msgstr "此表示作出的数据布局保证只有健全性所要求的那些。它们是："

#: src/type-layout.md:301
msgid "The offset of a field is divisible by that field's alignment."
msgstr "字段的偏移量可被该字段的对齐整除。"

#: src/type-layout.md:302
msgid ""
"The alignment of the type is at least the maximum alignment of its fields."
msgstr "类型的对齐至少是其字段的最大对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:308
msgid ""
"For [structs](items/structs.md), it is further guaranteed that the fields do "
"not overlap. That is, the fields can be ordered such that the offset plus "
"the size of any field is less than or equal to the offset of the next field "
"in the ordering. The ordering does not have to be the same as the order in "
"which the fields are specified in the declaration of the type."
msgstr ""
"对于 [struct](items/structs.md)，还进一步保证字段不重叠。也就是说，可以对字段"
"排序，使得任意字段的偏移量加上其大小小于或等于该排序中下一个字段的偏移量。该"
"排序不必与类型声明中指定字段的顺序相同。"

#: src/type-layout.md:310
msgid ""
"Be aware that this guarantee does not imply that the fields have distinct "
"addresses: [zero-sized types](glossary.md#r-glossary.zst) may have the same "
"address as other fields in the same struct."
msgstr ""
"注意，此保证并不意味着字段具有不同地址：[零大小类型](glossary.md#r-"
"glossary.zst) 可能与同一 struct 中的其他字段具有相同地址。"

#: src/type-layout.md:316
msgid ""
"There are no other guarantees of data layout made by this representation."
msgstr "此表示不作其他数据布局保证。"

#: src/type-layout.md:322
msgid "The `C` representation"
msgstr "`C` 表示"

#: src/type-layout.md:328
msgid ""
"The `C` representation is designed for dual purposes. One purpose is for "
"creating types that are interoperable with the C Language. The second "
"purpose is to create types that you can soundly perform operations on that "
"rely on data layout such as reinterpreting values as a different type."
msgstr ""
"`C` 表示有双重目的。一个目的是创建可与 C 语言互操作的类型。第二个目的是创建可"
"以健全地在其上执行依赖数据布局的操作（例如将值重新解释为不同类型）的类型。"

#: src/type-layout.md:330
msgid ""
"Because of this dual purpose, it is possible to create types that are not "
"useful for interfacing with the C programming language."
msgstr "由于这种双重目的，可以创建出不适合与 C 编程语言交互的类型。"

#: src/type-layout.md:336
msgid ""
"This representation can be applied to structs, unions, and enums. The "
"exception is [zero-variant enums](items/enumerations.md#zero-variant-enums) "
"for which the `C` representation is an error."
msgstr ""
"此表示可以应用于 struct、union 和 enum。例外是[零变体枚举](items/"
"enumerations.md#zero-variant-enums)，对它们使用 `C` 表示会出错。"

#: src/type-layout.md:342
msgid "`#[repr(C)]` Structs"
msgstr "`#[repr(C)]` struct"

#: src/type-layout.md:348
msgid ""
"The alignment of the struct is the alignment of the most-aligned field in "
"it, or one if there are no fields."
msgstr "struct 的对齐是其中对齐要求最高的字段的对齐；如果没有字段，则为 1。"

#: src/type-layout.md:354
msgid "The size and offset of fields is determined by the following algorithm."
msgstr "字段的大小和偏移量由以下算法确定。"

#: src/type-layout.md:356
msgid "Start with a current offset of 0 bytes."
msgstr "从当前偏移量 0 字节开始。"

#: src/type-layout.md:358
msgid ""
"For each field in declaration order in the struct, first determine the size "
"and alignment of the field. If the current offset is not a multiple of the "
"field's alignment, then add padding bytes to the current offset until it is "
"a multiple of the field's alignment. The offset for the field is what the "
"current offset is now. Then increase the current offset by the size of the "
"field."
msgstr ""
"对于 struct 中按声明顺序排列的每个字段，首先确定该字段的大小和对齐。如果当前"
"偏移量不是该字段对齐的倍数，则向当前偏移量添加填充字节，直到它成为该字段对齐"
"的倍数。该字段的偏移量就是此时的当前偏移量。然后将当前偏移量增加该字段的大"
"小。"

#: src/type-layout.md:360
msgid ""
"Finally, the size of the struct is the current offset rounded up to the "
"nearest multiple of the struct's alignment."
msgstr ""
"最后，struct 的大小是将当前偏移量向上取整到最接近的 struct 对齐倍数后的值。"

#: src/type-layout.md:362
msgid "Here is this algorithm described in pseudocode."
msgstr "下面用伪代码描述此算法。"

#: src/type-layout.md:366
msgid ""
"/// Returns the amount of padding needed after `offset` to ensure that the\n"
"/// following address will be aligned to `alignment`.\n"
msgstr ""
"/// 返回 `offset` 之后所需的填充量，以确保\n"
"/// 后续地址将按 `alignment` 对齐。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:371
msgid "// round up to next multiple of `alignment`\n"
msgstr "// 向上取整到下一个 `alignment` 的倍数\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:374
msgid "// already a multiple of `alignment`\n"
msgstr "// 已经是 `alignment` 的倍数\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:384
msgid ""
"// Increase the current offset so that it's a multiple of the alignment\n"
"    // of this field. For the first field, this will always be zero.\n"
"    // The skipped bytes are called padding bytes.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 增加当前偏移量，使其成为此字段对齐的倍数。\n"
"    // 对第一个字段，这始终为零。\n"
"    // 跳过的字节称为填充字节。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:401
msgid ""
"This pseudocode uses a naive algorithm that ignores overflow issues for the "
"sake of clarity. To perform memory layout computations in actual code, use "
"[`Layout`](../core/alloc/layout/struct.Layout.html)."
msgstr ""
"为了清晰起见，此伪代码使用忽略溢出问题的朴素算法。要在实际代码中执行内存布局"
"计算，请使用 [`Layout`](../core/alloc/layout/struct.Layout.html)。"

#: src/type-layout.md:410
msgid ""
"This algorithm can produce [zero-sized](glossary.md#r-glossary.zst) structs. "
"In C, an empty struct declaration like `struct Foo { }` is illegal. However, "
"both gcc and clang support options to enable such structs, and assign them "
"size zero. C++, in contrast, gives empty structs a size of 1, unless they "
"are inherited from or they are fields that have the `[[no_unique_address]]` "
"attribute, in which case they do not increase the overall size of the struct."
msgstr ""
"此算法可以产生[零大小](glossary.md#r-glossary.zst) struct。在 C 中，像 "
"`struct Foo { }` 这样的空 struct 声明是非法的。不过，gcc 和 clang 都支持启用"
"这类 struct 的选项，并赋予它们零大小。相比之下，C++ 会给空 struct 大小 1，除"
"非它们被继承，或者它们是具有 `[[no_unique_address]]` 属性的字段；在这些情况"
"下，它们不会增加 struct 的整体大小。"

#: src/type-layout.md:419
msgid "`#[repr(C)]` Unions"
msgstr "`#[repr(C)]` union"

#: src/type-layout.md:425
msgid ""
"A union declared with `#[repr(C)]` will have the same size and alignment as "
"an equivalent C union declaration in the C language for the target platform."
msgstr ""
"使用 `#[repr(C)]` 声明的 union 将具有与目标平台上 C 语言中等价的 C union 声明"
"相同的大小和对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:431
msgid ""
"The union will have a size of the maximum size of all of its fields rounded "
"to its alignment, and an alignment of the maximum alignment of all of its "
"fields. These maximums may come from different fields. Each field lives at "
"byte offset 0 from the beginning of the union."
msgstr ""
"union 的大小是其所有字段最大大小按其对齐向上取整后的值，对齐是其所有字段的最"
"大对齐。这两个最大值可能来自不同字段。每个字段都位于从 union 开头起的字节偏移"
"量 0 处。"

#: src/type-layout.md:440
msgid "// From f2\n"
msgstr "// 来自 f2\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:441
msgid "// From f1\n"
msgstr "// 来自 f1\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:452
msgid ""
"// Size of 6 from b,\n"
"                                                      // rounded up to 8 "
"from\n"
"                                                      // alignment of a.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 大小 6 来自 b，\n"
"                                                      // 根据 a 的对齐\n"
"                                                      // 向上取整到 8。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:455
msgid "// From a\n"
msgstr "// 来自 a\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:465
msgid "`#[repr(C)]` Field-less Enums"
msgstr "`#[repr(C)]` 无字段 enum"

#: src/type-layout.md:467
msgid ""
"For [field-less enums](items/enumerations.md#field-less-enum), the `C` "
"representation has the size and alignment of the default `enum` size and "
"alignment for the target platform's C ABI."
msgstr ""
"对于[无字段枚举](items/enumerations.md#field-less-enum)，`C` 表示的大小和对齐"
"等同于目标平台 C ABI 中默认的 `enum` 大小和对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:473
msgid ""
"The enum representation in C is implementation defined, so this is really a "
"\"best guess\". In particular, this may be incorrect when the C code of "
"interest is compiled with certain flags."
msgstr ""
"C 中的 enum 表示由实现定义，因此这实际上只是“最佳猜测”。特别是，当相关 C 代码"
"使用某些标志编译时，这可能不正确。"

#: src/type-layout.md:482
msgid ""
"There are crucial differences between an `enum` in the C language and Rust's "
"[field-less enums](items/enumerations.md#field-less-enum) with this "
"representation. An `enum` in C is mostly a `typedef` plus some named "
"constants; in other words, an object of an `enum` type can hold any integer "
"value. For example, this is often used for bitflags in `C`. In contrast, "
"Rust’s [field-less enums](items/enumerations.md#field-less-enum) can only "
"legally hold the discriminant values, everything else is [undefined behavior]"
"(behavior-considered-undefined.md). Therefore, using a field-less enum in "
"FFI to model a C `enum` is often wrong."
msgstr ""
"C 语言中的 `enum` 与 Rust 中使用此表示的[无字段枚举](items/"
"enumerations.md#field-less-enum)之间存在关键差异。C 中的 `enum` 大多是一个 "
"`typedef` 加上一些具名常量；换句话说，`enum` 类型的对象可以持有任何整数值。例"
"如，这在 `C` 中常用于 bitflags。相比之下，Rust 的[无字段枚举](items/"
"enumerations.md#field-less-enum)只能合法地持有判别值，其他一切都是[未定义行"
"为](behavior-considered-undefined.md)。因此，在 FFI 中使用无字段枚举来模拟 C "
"`enum` 往往是错误的。"

#: src/type-layout.md:491
msgid "`#[repr(C)]` Enums With Fields"
msgstr "`#[repr(C)]` 带字段 enum"

#: src/type-layout.md:497
msgid ""
"The representation of a `repr(C)` enum with fields is a `repr(C)` struct "
"with two fields, also called a \"tagged union\" in C:"
msgstr ""
"带字段的 `repr(C)` enum 的表示是一个有两个字段的 `repr(C)` struct，在 C 中也"
"称为“tagged union”："

#: src/type-layout.md:503
msgid "a `repr(C)` version of the enum with all fields removed (\"the tag\")"
msgstr "该 enum 移除所有字段后的 `repr(C)` 版本（“标签”）"

#: src/type-layout.md:509
msgid ""
"a `repr(C)` union of `repr(C)` structs for the fields of each variant that "
"had them (\"the payload\")"
msgstr ""
"由每个带字段变体的字段所对应的 `repr(C)` struct 构成的 `repr(C)` union（“载"
"荷”）"

#: src/type-layout.md:515
msgid ""
"Due to the representation of `repr(C)` structs and unions, if a variant has "
"a single field there is no difference between putting that field directly in "
"the union or wrapping it in a struct; any system which wishes to manipulate "
"such an `enum`'s representation may therefore use whichever form is more "
"convenient or consistent for them."
msgstr ""
"由于 `repr(C)` struct 和 union 的表示，如果某个变体只有一个字段，那么将该字段"
"直接放入 union 与将其包装在 struct 中没有区别；因此，任何希望操作这种 `enum` "
"表示的系统都可以使用对它们来说更方便或更一致的形式。"

#: src/type-layout.md:521
msgid "// This Enum has the same representation as ...\n"
msgstr "// 此 Enum 具有与以下内容相同的表示...\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:529
msgid "// ... this struct.\n"
msgstr "// ...这个 struct。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:536 src/type-layout.md:630
msgid "// This is the discriminant enum.\n"
msgstr "// 这是判别值 enum。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:540
msgid "// This is the variant union.\n"
msgstr "// 这是变体 union。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:561
msgid ""
"// This struct could be omitted (it is a zero-sized type), and it must be "
"in\n"
"// C/C++ headers.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此 struct 可以省略（它是零大小类型），且它必须位于\n"
"// C/C++ 头文件中。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:573
msgid "Primitive representations"
msgstr "原始表示"

#: src/type-layout.md:579
msgid ""
"The _primitive representations_ are the representations with the same names "
"as the primitive integer types. That is: `u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `u128`, "
"`usize`, `i8`, `i16`, `i32`, `i64`, `i128`, and `isize`."
msgstr ""
"_原始表示_ 是与原始整数类型同名的表示。也就是：`u8`、`u16`、`u32`、`u64`、"
"`u128`、`usize`、`i8`、`i16`、`i32`、`i64`、`i128` 和 `isize`。"

#: src/type-layout.md:585
msgid ""
"Primitive representations can only be applied to enumerations and have "
"different behavior whether the enum has fields or no fields. It is an error "
"for [zero-variant enums](items/enumerations.md#zero-variant-enums) to have a "
"primitive representation. Combining two primitive representations together "
"is an error."
msgstr ""
"原始表示只能应用于枚举，并且根据 enum 是否有字段而有不同的行为。对[零变体枚"
"举](items/enumerations.md#zero-variant-enums)使用原始表示是错误。将两个原始表"
"示组合在一起是错误。"

#: src/type-layout.md:591
msgid "Primitive representation of field-less enums"
msgstr "无字段枚举的原始表示"

#: src/type-layout.md:593
msgid ""
"For [field-less enums](items/enumerations.md#field-less-enum), primitive "
"representations set the size and alignment to be the same as the primitive "
"type of the same name. For example, a field-less enum with a `u8` "
"representation can only have discriminants between 0 and 255 inclusive."
msgstr ""
"对于[无字段枚举](items/enumerations.md#field-less-enum)，原始表示会将大小和对"
"齐设为与同名原始类型相同。例如，具有 `u8` 表示的无字段枚举只能具有 0 到 255"
"（含）之间的判别值。"

#: src/type-layout.md:599
msgid "Primitive representation of enums with fields"
msgstr "带字段枚举的原始表示"

#: src/type-layout.md:601
msgid ""
"The representation of a primitive representation enum is a `repr(C)` union "
"of `repr(C)` structs for each variant with a field. The first field of each "
"struct in the union is the primitive representation version of the enum with "
"all fields removed (\"the tag\") and the remaining fields are the fields of "
"that variant."
msgstr ""
"原始表示枚举的表示是一个 `repr(C)` union，其中包含每个带字段变体对应的 "
"`repr(C)` struct。union 中每个 struct 的第一个字段是该 enum 移除所有字段后的"
"原始表示版本（“标签”），其余字段是该变体的字段。"

#: src/type-layout.md:607
msgid ""
"This representation is unchanged if the tag is given its own member in the "
"union, should that make manipulation more clear for you (although to follow "
"the C++ standard the tag member should be wrapped in a `struct`)."
msgstr ""
"如果将标签作为自己的成员放在 union 中，此表示不变；如果这能让操作对你更清晰的"
"话可以这样做（不过，为了遵循 C++ 标准，标签成员应包装在 `struct` 中）。"

#: src/type-layout.md:613
msgid "// This enum has the same representation as ...\n"
msgstr "// 此 enum 具有与以下内容相同的表示...\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:621
msgid "// ... this union.\n"
msgstr "// ...这个 union。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:657
msgid ""
"Combining primitive representations of enums with fields and `#[repr(C)]`"
msgstr "组合带字段枚举的原始表示和 `#[repr(C)]`"

#: src/type-layout.md:659
msgid ""
"For enums with fields, it is also possible to combine `repr(C)` and a "
"primitive representation (e.g., `repr(C, u8)`). This modifies the [`repr(C)`]"
"(#reprc-enums-with-fields) by changing the representation of the "
"discriminant enum to the chosen primitive instead. So, if you chose the `u8` "
"representation, then the discriminant enum would have a size and alignment "
"of 1 byte."
msgstr ""
"对于带字段枚举，也可以组合 `repr(C)` 和原始表示（例如 `repr(C, u8)`）。这会修"
"改 [`repr(C)`](#reprc-enums-with-fields)，将判别值 enum 的表示改为所选原始类"
"型。因此，如果选择 `u8` 表示，判别值 enum 的大小和对齐将为 1 字节。"

#: src/type-layout.md:661
msgid ""
"The discriminant enum from the example [earlier](#reprc-enums-with-fields) "
"then becomes:"
msgstr "前面[示例](#reprc-enums-with-fields)中的判别值 enum 随后变为："

#: src/type-layout.md:664
msgid "// `u8` was added\n"
msgstr "// 添加了 `u8`\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:674
msgid "// So `u8` is used here instead of `C`\n"
msgstr "// 因此这里使用 `u8` 而不是 `C`\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:680
msgid ""
"For example, with a `repr(C, u8)` enum it is not possible to have 257 unique "
"discriminants (\"tags\") whereas the same enum with only a `repr(C)` "
"attribute will compile without any problems."
msgstr ""
"例如，对于 `repr(C, u8)` enum，不可能有 257 个唯一判别值（“标签”）；而同一个 "
"enum 如果只有 `repr(C)` 属性，则会顺利编译。"

#: src/type-layout.md:682
msgid ""
"Using a primitive representation in addition to `repr(C)` can change the "
"size of an enum from the `repr(C)` form:"
msgstr ""
"除了 `repr(C)` 之外再使用原始表示，可能会改变 enum 相对于 `repr(C)` 形式的大"
"小："

#: src/type-layout.md:702
msgid "// The size of the C representation is platform dependent\n"
msgstr "// C 表示的大小依赖平台\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:704
msgid ""
"// One byte for the discriminant and one byte for the value in "
"Enum8::Variant0\n"
msgstr "// 判别值一个字节，Enum8::Variant0 中的值一个字节\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:706
msgid ""
"// Two bytes for the discriminant and one byte for the value in "
"Enum16::Variant0\n"
"// plus one byte of padding.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 判别值两个字节，Enum16::Variant0 中的值一个字节，\n"
"// 再加一个字节的填充。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:718
msgid "The alignment modifiers"
msgstr "对齐修饰符"

#: src/type-layout.md:724
msgid ""
"The `align` and `packed` modifiers can be used to respectively raise or "
"lower the alignment of `struct`s and `union`s. `packed` may also alter the "
"padding between fields (although it will not alter the padding inside of any "
"field). On their own, `align` and `packed` do not provide guarantees about "
"the order of fields in the layout of a struct or the layout of an enum "
"variant, although they may be combined with representations (such as `C`) "
"which do provide such guarantees."
msgstr ""
"`align` 和 `packed` 修饰符可分别用于提高或降低 `struct` 和 `union` 的对齐。"
"`packed` 也可能改变字段之间的填充（不过它不会改变任何字段内部的填充）。"
"`align` 和 `packed` 本身不保证 struct 布局或 enum 变体布局中字段的顺序，不过"
"它们可以与确实提供此类保证的表示（如 `C`）组合使用。"

#: src/type-layout.md:730
msgid ""
"The alignment is specified as an integer parameter in the form of "
"`#[repr(align(x))]` or `#[repr(packed(x))]`. The alignment value must be a "
"power of two from 1 up to 2<sup>29</sup>. For `packed`, if no value is "
"given, as in `#[repr(packed)]`, then the value is 1."
msgstr ""
"对齐以 `#[repr(align(x))]` 或 `#[repr(packed(x))]` 形式的整数参数指定。对齐值"
"必须是从 1 到 2<sup>29</sup> 的 2 的幂。对于 `packed`，如果未给出值，如 "
"`#[repr(packed)]`，则该值为 1。"

#: src/type-layout.md:736
msgid ""
"For `align`, if the specified alignment is less than the alignment of the "
"type without the `align` modifier, then the alignment is unaffected."
msgstr ""
"对于 `align`，如果指定的对齐小于没有 `align` 修饰符时该类型的对齐，则对齐不受"
"影响。"

#: src/type-layout.md:742
msgid ""
"For `packed`, if the specified alignment is greater than the type's "
"alignment without the `packed` modifier, then the alignment and layout is "
"unaffected."
msgstr ""
"对于 `packed`，如果指定的对齐大于没有 `packed` 修饰符时该类型的对齐，则对齐和"
"布局不受影响。"

#: src/type-layout.md:748
msgid ""
"The alignments of each field, for the purpose of positioning fields, is the "
"smaller of the specified alignment and the alignment of the field's type."
msgstr ""
"为放置字段而使用的每个字段的对齐，是指定对齐和该字段类型对齐两者中的较小者。"

#: src/type-layout.md:754
msgid ""
"Inter-field padding is guaranteed to be the minimum required in order to "
"satisfy each field's (possibly altered) alignment (although note that, on "
"its own, `packed` does not provide any guarantee about field ordering). An "
"important consequence of these rules is that a type with "
"`#[repr(packed(1))]` (or `#[repr(packed)]`) will have no inter-field padding."
msgstr ""
"保证字段间填充是满足每个字段（可能已更改的）对齐所需的最小填充（不过请注意，"
"`packed` 本身不提供任何字段排序保证）。这些规则的一个重要后果是，具有 "
"`#[repr(packed(1))]`（或 `#[repr(packed)]`）的类型没有字段间填充。"

#: src/type-layout.md:760
msgid ""
"The `align` and `packed` modifiers cannot be applied on the same type and a "
"`packed` type cannot transitively contain another `align`ed type. `align` "
"and `packed` may only be applied to the [`Rust`](#the-rust-representation) "
"and [`C`](#the-c-representation) representations."
msgstr ""
"`align` 和 `packed` 修饰符不能应用于同一类型，且 `packed` 类型不能传递地包含"
"另一个已 `align` 的类型。`align` 和 `packed` 只能应用于 [`Rust`](#the-rust-"
"representation) 和 [`C`](#the-c-representation) 表示。"

#: src/type-layout.md:766
msgid ""
"The `align` modifier can also be applied on an `enum`. When it is, the "
"effect on the `enum`'s alignment is the same as if the `enum` was wrapped in "
"a newtype `struct` with the same `align` modifier."
msgstr ""
"`align` 修饰符也可以应用于 `enum`。这样做时，它对 `enum` 对齐的影响，就像将"
"该 `enum` 包装在具有相同 `align` 修饰符的 newtype `struct` 中一样。"

#: src/type-layout.md:772
msgid ""
"References to unaligned fields are not allowed because it is [undefined "
"behavior](behavior-considered-undefined.md). When fields are unaligned due "
"to an alignment modifier, consider the following options for using "
"references and dereferences:"
msgstr ""
"不允许引用未对齐字段，因为这是[未定义行为](behavior-considered-"
"undefined.md)。当字段因对齐修饰符而未对齐时，使用引用和解引用可考虑以下选项："

#: src/type-layout.md:781
msgid ""
"// Instead of creating a reference to a field, copy the value to a local "
"variable.\n"
msgstr "// 不要创建指向字段的引用，而是将值复制到局部变量。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:783
msgid ""
"// Or in situations like `println!` which creates a reference, use braces\n"
msgstr "// 或者在 `println!` 这类会创建引用的情形中，使用花括号\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:784
msgid "// to change it to a copy of the value.\n"
msgstr "// 将它改为值的副本。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:786
msgid ""
"// Or if you need a pointer, use the unaligned methods for reading and "
"writing\n"
msgstr "// 或者如果需要指针，使用用于读写的未对齐方法，\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:787
msgid "// instead of dereferencing the pointer directly.\n"
msgstr "// 而不是直接解引用指针。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:801
msgid "The `transparent` representation"
msgstr "`transparent` 表示"

#: src/type-layout.md:807
msgid ""
"The `transparent` representation can only be used on a [`struct`](items/"
"structs.md) or an [`enum`](items/enumerations.md) with a single variant that "
"has:"
msgstr ""
"`transparent` 表示只能用于 [`struct`](items/structs.md)，或用于具有单个变体"
"的 [`enum`](items/enumerations.md)，并且其具有："

#: src/type-layout.md:808
msgid ""
"any number of fields with size 0 and alignment 1 (e.g. [`PhantomData<T>`]"
"(special-types-and-traits.md#phantomdatat)), and"
msgstr ""
"任意数量大小为 0 且对齐为 1 的字段（例如 [`PhantomData<T>`](special-types-"
"and-traits.md#phantomdatat)），以及"

#: src/type-layout.md:809
msgid "at most one other field."
msgstr "至多一个其他字段。"

#: src/type-layout.md:815
msgid ""
"Structs and enums with this representation have the same layout and ABI as "
"the only non-size 0 non-alignment 1 field, if present, or unit otherwise."
msgstr ""
"具有此表示的 struct 和 enum，如果存在唯一一个不属于大小 0 且对齐 1 的字段，则"
"具有与该字段相同的布局和 ABI；否则具有与单元类型相同的布局和 ABI。"

#: src/type-layout.md:817
msgid ""
"This is different than the `C` representation because a struct with the `C` "
"representation will always have the ABI of a `C` `struct` while, for "
"example, a struct with the `transparent` representation with a primitive "
"field will have the ABI of the primitive field."
msgstr ""
"这不同于 `C` 表示，因为具有 `C` 表示的 struct 总是具有 `C` `struct` 的 ABI；"
"而例如，具有 `transparent` 表示且包含原始字段的 struct 将具有该原始字段的 "
"ABI。"

#: src/type-layout.md:823
msgid ""
"Because this representation delegates type layout to another type, it cannot "
"be used with any other representation."
msgstr "由于此表示将类型布局委托给另一个类型，因此不能与任何其他表示一起使用。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:11
msgid ""
"Sometimes a type needs to be mutated while having multiple aliases. In Rust "
"this is achieved using a pattern called _interior mutability_."
msgstr ""
"有时，一个类型需要在具有多个别名的同时被修改。在 Rust 中，这是通过一种称为_内"
"部可变性_的模式实现的。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:17
msgid ""
"A type has interior mutability if its internal state can be changed through "
"a [shared reference](types/pointer.md#shared-references-) to it."
msgstr ""
"如果一个类型的内部状态可以通过指向它的[共享引用](types/pointer.md#shared-"
"references-) 来改变，则该类型具有内部可变性。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:23
msgid ""
"This goes against the usual [requirement](behavior-considered-undefined.md) "
"that the value pointed to by a shared reference is not mutated."
msgstr ""
"这违背了通常的[要求](behavior-considered-undefined.md)：共享引用所指向的值不"
"会被修改。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:29
msgid ""
"[`std::cell::UnsafeCell<T>`](../core/cell/struct.UnsafeCell.html) type is "
"the only allowed way to disable this requirement. When `UnsafeCell<T>` is "
"immutably aliased, it is still safe to mutate, or obtain a mutable reference "
"to, the `T` it contains."
msgstr ""
"[`std::cell::UnsafeCell<T>`](../core/cell/struct.UnsafeCell.html) 类型是唯一"
"允许用来禁用此要求的方式。当 `UnsafeCell<T>` 被不可变地别名化时，修改其包含"
"的 `T`，或取得指向该 `T` 的可变引用，仍然是安全的。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:35
msgid ""
"As with all other types, it is undefined behavior to have multiple `&mut "
"UnsafeCell<T>` aliases."
msgstr "与所有其他类型一样，拥有多个 `&mut UnsafeCell<T>` 别名是未定义行为。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:41
msgid ""
"Other types with interior mutability can be created by using `UnsafeCell<T>` "
"as a field. The standard library provides a variety of types that provide "
"safe interior mutability APIs."
msgstr ""
"可以通过将 `UnsafeCell<T>` 用作字段来创建其他具有内部可变性的类型。标准库提供"
"了多种类型，它们提供安全的内部可变性 API。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:47
msgid ""
"For example, [`std::cell::RefCell<T>`](../core/cell/struct.RefCell.html) "
"uses run-time borrow checks to ensure the usual rules around multiple "
"references."
msgstr ""
"例如，[`std::cell::RefCell<T>`](../core/cell/struct.RefCell.html) 使用运行时"
"借用检查来确保关于多个引用的通常规则。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:53
msgid ""
"The [`std::sync::atomic`](../core/sync/atomic/index.html) module contains "
"types that wrap a value that is only accessed with atomic operations, "
"allowing the value to be shared and mutated across threads."
msgstr ""
"[`std::sync::atomic`](../core/sync/atomic/index.html) 模块包含一些类型，它们"
"包装只能通过原子操作访问的值，从而允许该值在线程之间共享和修改。"

#: src/subtyping.md:11
msgid ""
"Subtyping is implicit and can occur at any stage in type checking or "
"inference."
msgstr "子类型化是隐式的，可以发生在类型检查或推断的任何阶段。"

#: src/subtyping.md:17
msgid ""
"Subtyping is restricted to two cases: variance with respect to lifetimes and "
"between types with higher ranked lifetimes. If we were to erase lifetimes "
"from types, then the only subtyping would be due to type equality."
msgstr ""
"子类型化仅限于两种情况：关于生命周期的型变，以及具有高阶生命周期的类型之间的"
"子类型化。如果从类型中擦除生命周期，那么唯一的子类型化将来自类型相等。"

#: src/subtyping.md:19
msgid ""
"Consider the following example: string literals always have `'static` "
"lifetime. Nevertheless, we can assign `s` to `t`:"
msgstr ""
"考虑以下示例：字符串字面量始终具有 `'static` 生命周期。尽管如此，我们仍可以"
"将 `s` 赋给 `t`："

#: src/subtyping.md:23
msgid "\"hi\""
msgstr "\"hi\""

#: src/subtyping.md:28
msgid ""
"Since `'static` outlives the lifetime parameter `'a`, `&'static str` is a "
"subtype of `&'a str`."
msgstr ""
"由于 `'static` 比生命周期参数 `'a` 存活得更久，`&'static str` 是 `&'a str` 的"
"子类型。"

#: src/subtyping.md:34
msgid ""
"[Higher-ranked](../nomicon/hrtb.html) [function pointers](types/function-"
"pointer.md) and [trait objects](types/trait-object.md) have another subtype "
"relation. They are subtypes of types that are given by substitutions of the "
"higher-ranked lifetimes. Some examples:"
msgstr ""
"[高阶](../nomicon/hrtb.html)[函数指针](types/function-pointer.md)和 [trait 对"
"象](types/trait-object.md)具有另一种子类型关系。它们是由替换高阶生命周期所给"
"出的类型的子类型。一些示例："

#: src/subtyping.md:37
msgid "// Here 'a is substituted for 'static\n"
msgstr "// 这里用 'a 替换 'static\n"

#: src/subtyping.md:40
msgid "// This works similarly for trait objects\n"
msgstr "// 对 trait 对象也类似\n"

#: src/subtyping.md:44
msgid "// We can also substitute one higher-ranked lifetime for another\n"
msgstr "// 我们也可以用一个高阶生命周期替换另一个\n"

#: src/subtyping.md:54
msgid "Variance"
msgstr "型变"

#: src/subtyping.md:60
msgid ""
"Variance is a property that generic types have with respect to their "
"arguments. A generic type's _variance_ in a parameter is how the subtyping "
"of the parameter affects the subtyping of the type."
msgstr ""
"型变是泛型类型相对于其实参所具有的属性。泛型类型在某个参数上的 _型变_，表示该"
"参数的子类型化如何影响该类型的子类型化。"

#: src/subtyping.md:66
msgid ""
"`F<T>` is _covariant_ over `T` if `T` being a subtype of `U` implies that "
"`F<T>` is a subtype of `F<U>` (subtyping \"passes through\")"
msgstr ""
"如果 `T` 是 `U` 的子类型会推出 `F<T>` 是 `F<U>` 的子类型，则 `F<T>` 对 `T` 是"
"_协变_ 的（子类型化“传递通过”）"

#: src/subtyping.md:72
msgid ""
"`F<T>` is _contravariant_ over `T` if `T` being a subtype of `U` implies "
"that `F<U>` is a subtype of `F<T>`"
msgstr ""
"如果 `T` 是 `U` 的子类型会推出 `F<U>` 是 `F<T>` 的子类型，则 `F<T>` 对 `T` 是"
"_逆变_ 的"

#: src/subtyping.md:78
msgid ""
"`F<T>` is _invariant_ over `T` otherwise (no subtyping relation can be "
"derived)"
msgstr "否则，`F<T>` 对 `T` 是 _不变_ 的（无法导出子类型关系）"

#: src/subtyping.md:84
msgid "Variance of types is automatically determined as follows"
msgstr "类型的型变按如下方式自动确定"

#: src/subtyping.md:86
msgid "Variance in `'a`"
msgstr "在 `'a` 上的型变"

#: src/subtyping.md:86
msgid "Variance in `T`"
msgstr "在 `T` 上的型变"

#: src/subtyping.md:88
msgid "`&'a T`"
msgstr "`&'a T`"

#: src/subtyping.md:88 src/subtyping.md:89 src/subtyping.md:90
