#: src/paths.md:1199
msgid ""
"Type paths are used within type definitions, trait bounds, and qualified "
"paths."
msgstr "类型路径用于类型定义、trait 边界和限定路径。"

#: src/paths.md:1205
msgid ""
"Although the `::` token is allowed before the generics arguments, it is not "
"required because there is no ambiguity like there is in [PathInExpression]"
"(paths.md#grammar-PathInExpression)."
msgstr ""
"虽然允许在泛型实参前使用 `::` token，但这不是必需的，因为不存在像 "
"[PathInExpression](paths.md#grammar-PathInExpression) 中那样的歧义。"

#: src/paths.md:1214
msgid "/*...*/"
msgstr "/*...*/"

#: src/paths.md:1227
msgid "Path qualifiers"
msgstr "路径限定符"

#: src/paths.md:1229
msgid ""
"Paths can be denoted with various leading qualifiers to change the meaning "
"of how it is resolved."
msgstr "路径可以用各种前导限定符表示，以改变其被解析的含义。"

#: src/paths.md:1235
msgid ""
"[`use` declarations](items/use-declarations.md) have additional behaviors "
"and restrictions for `self`, `super`, `crate`, and `$crate`."
msgstr ""
"[`use` 声明](items/use-declarations.md) 对 `self`、`super`、`crate` 和 "
"`$crate` 有额外的行为和限制。"

#: src/paths.md:1244 src/syntax-index.md:109
msgid "`::`"
msgstr "`::`"

#: src/paths.md:1250
msgid ""
"Paths starting with `::` are considered to be _global paths_ where the "
"segments of the path start being resolved from a place which differs based "
"on edition. Each identifier in the path must resolve to an item."
msgstr ""
"以 `::` 开头的路径被视为_全局路径_，其中路径段开始解析的位置会因 edition 而"
"异。路径中的每个标识符都必须解析为一个项。"

#: src/paths.md:1260
msgid ""
"In the 2015 Edition, identifiers resolve from the \"crate root\" (`crate::` "
"in the 2018 edition), which contains a variety of different items, including "
"external crates, default crates such as `std` or `core`, and items in the "
"top level of the crate (including `use` imports)."
msgstr ""
"在 2015 edition 中，标识符从“crate 根”（2018 edition 中为 `crate::`）解析；"
"crate 根包含各种不同项，包括外部 crate、`std` 或 `core` 等默认 crate，以及 "
"crate 顶层中的项（包括 `use` 导入）。"

#: src/paths.md:1262
msgid ""
"Beginning with the 2018 Edition, paths starting with `::` resolve from "
"crates in the [extern prelude](names/preludes.md#extern-prelude). That is, "
"they must be followed by the name of a crate."
msgstr ""
"从 2018 edition 开始，以 `::` 开头的路径会从 [extern prelude](names/"
"preludes.md#extern-prelude) 中的 crate 解析。也就是说，它们后面必须跟随一个 "
"crate 的名称。"

#: src/paths.md:1269
msgid ""
"// In the 2018 edition, this accesses `std` via the extern prelude.\n"
"    // In the 2015 edition, this accesses `std` via the crate root.\n"
msgstr ""
"// In the 2018 edition, this accesses `std` via the extern prelude.\n"
"    // In the 2015 edition, this accesses `std` via the crate root.\n"

#: src/paths.md:1283
msgid ""
"// call `a`'s foo function\n"
"        // In Rust 2018, `::a` would be interpreted as the crate `a`.\n"
msgstr ""
"// call `a`'s foo function\n"
"        // In Rust 2018, `::a` would be interpreted as the crate `a`.\n"

#: src/paths.md:1300
msgid "`self` resolves the path relative to the current module."
msgstr "`self` 会相对于当前模块解析路径。"

#: src/paths.md:1306
msgid ""
"`self` may only be used as the first segment of a path (without a preceding "
"`::`) or as the last segment (preceded by `::`)."
msgstr ""
"`self` 只能作为路径的第一段（前面没有 `::`）使用，或者作为最后一段（前面有 "
"`::`）使用。"

#: src/paths.md:1312
msgid ""
"When `self` appears as the last segment of a path, it refers to the entity "
"named by the preceding segment. The preceding path must resolve to a [module]"
"(items/modules.md), [enumeration](items/enumerations.md), or [trait](items/"
"traits.md)."
msgstr ""
"当 `self` 作为路径的最后一段出现时，它指代由前一段命名的实体。前面的路径必须"
"解析为[模块](items/modules.md)、[枚举](items/enumerations.md)或 [trait]"
"(items/traits.md)。"

#: src/paths.md:1320
msgid "// OK: Enumerations can be parents of `self`.\n"
msgstr "// OK: Enumerations can be parents of `self`.\n"

#: src/paths.md:1335
msgid ""
"See [items.use.self](items/use-declarations.md#r-items.use.self) for "
"additional rules about `self` in `use` declarations."
msgstr ""
"有关 `use` 声明中 `self` 的额外规则，参见 [items.use.self](items/use-"
"declarations.md#r-items.use.self)。"

#: src/paths.md:1344
msgid ""
"In a method body, a path which consists of a single `self` segment resolves "
"to the method's self parameter."
msgstr "在方法体中，由单个 `self` 段组成的路径会解析为该方法的 self 参数。"

#: src/paths.md:1370
msgid ""
"`Self`, with a capital \"S\", is used to refer to the current type being "
"implemented or defined. It may be used in the following situations:"
msgstr ""
"首字母大写的 `Self` 用于指代当前正在实现或定义的类型。它可以在以下情况下使"
"用："

#: src/paths.md:1376
msgid ""
"In a [trait](items/traits.md) definition, it refers to the type implementing "
"the trait."
msgstr "在 [trait](items/traits.md) 定义中，它指代实现该 trait 的类型。"

#: src/paths.md:1382
msgid ""
"In an [implementation](items/implementations.md), it refers to the type "
"being implemented. When implementing a tuple or unit [struct](items/"
"structs.md), it also refers to the constructor in the [value namespace]"
"(names/namespaces.md)."
msgstr ""
"在[实现](items/implementations.md)中，它指代正在实现的类型。当实现元组[结构"
"体](items/structs.md)或单元[结构体](items/structs.md)时，它还指代[值命名空间]"
"(names/namespaces.md)中的构造器。"

#: src/paths.md:1388
msgid ""
"In the definition of a [struct](items/structs.md), [enumeration](items/"
"enumerations.md), or [union](items/unions.md), it refers to the type being "
"defined. The definition is not allowed to be infinitely recursive (there "
"must be an indirection)."
msgstr ""
"在[结构体](items/structs.md)、[枚举](items/enumerations.md)或[联合体](items/"
"unions.md)的定义中，它指代正在定义的类型。该定义不允许无限递归（必须有一层间"
"接性）。"

#: src/paths.md:1394
msgid ""
"The scope of `Self` behaves similarly to a generic parameter; see the "
"[`Self` scope](names/scopes.md#self-scope) section for more details."
msgstr ""
"`Self` 的作用域行为类似于泛型参数；更多细节见 [`Self` 作用域](names/"
"scopes.md#self-scope)章节。"

#: src/paths.md:1400
msgid "`Self` can only be used as the first segment, without a preceding `::`."
msgstr "`Self` 只能作为第一段使用，前面不能有 `::`。"

#: src/paths.md:1406
msgid "The `Self` path cannot include generic arguments (as in `Self::<i32>`)."
msgstr "`Self` 路径不能包含泛型实参（如 `Self::<i32>`）。"

#: src/paths.md:1412
msgid "// `Self` will be whatever type that implements `T`.\n"
msgstr "// `Self` will be whatever type that implements `T`.\n"

#: src/paths.md:1414
msgid "// `Self::Item` will be the type alias in the implementation.\n"
msgstr "// `Self::Item` will be the type alias in the implementation.\n"

#: src/paths.md:1421
msgid "// `Self` is the type `S`.\n"
msgstr "// `Self` is the type `S`.\n"

#: src/paths.md:1424
msgid "// `Self::Item` is the type `i32`.\n"
msgstr "// `Self::Item` is the type `i32`.\n"

#: src/paths.md:1425
msgid "// `Self::C` is the constant value `9`.\n"
msgstr "// `Self::C` is the constant value `9`.\n"

#: src/paths.md:1428
msgid ""
"// `Self` is in scope within the generics of a trait definition,\n"
"// to refer to the type being defined.\n"
msgstr ""
"// `Self` is in scope within the generics of a trait definition,\n"
"// to refer to the type being defined.\n"

#: src/paths.md:1433
msgid ""
"// `Self` can also reference associated items of the\n"
"    // type being implemented.\n"
msgstr ""
"// `Self` can also reference associated items of the\n"
"    // type being implemented.\n"

#: src/paths.md:1440
msgid ""
"// A struct can reference itself (as long as it is not\n"
"    // infinitely recursive).\n"
msgstr ""
"// A struct can reference itself (as long as it is not\n"
"    // infinitely recursive).\n"

#: src/paths.md:1456
msgid "`super` in a path resolves to the parent module."
msgstr "路径中的 `super` 解析为父模块。"

#: src/paths.md:1462
msgid ""
"It may only be used in leading segments of the path, possibly after an "
"initial `self` segment."
msgstr "它只能用于路径的前导段，可能跟在初始的 `self` 段之后。"

#: src/paths.md:1470 src/paths.md:1489 src/paths.md:1490
msgid "// call a's foo function\n"
msgstr "// call a's foo function\n"

#: src/paths.md:1480
msgid ""
"`super` may be repeated several times after the first `super` or `self` to "
"refer to ancestor modules."
msgstr ""
"在第一个 `super` 或 `self` 之后，可以重复使用 `super` 多次以指代祖先模块。"

#: src/paths.md:1508
msgid "`crate` resolves the path relative to the current crate."
msgstr "`crate` 会相对于当前 crate 解析路径。"

#: src/paths.md:1514
msgid ""
"`crate` can only be used as the first segment, without a preceding `::`."
msgstr "`crate` 只能作为第一段使用，前面不能有 `::`。"

#: src/paths.md:1530
msgid "`$crate`"
msgstr "`$crate`"

#: src/paths.md:1536
msgid ""
"[`$crate`](macros-by-example.md#r-macro.decl.hygiene.crate) is only used "
"within [macro transcribers](macros-by-example.md), and can only be used as "
"the first segment, without a preceding `::`."
msgstr ""
"[`$crate`](macros-by-example.md#r-macro.decl.hygiene.crate) 只在[宏转录器]"
"(macros-by-example.md)中使用，并且只能作为第一段使用，前面不能有 `::`。"

#: src/paths.md:1542
msgid ""
"[`$crate`](macros-by-example.md#r-macro.decl.hygiene.crate) will expand to a "
"path to access items from the top level of the crate where the macro is "
"defined, regardless of which crate the macro is invoked."
msgstr ""
"[`$crate`](macros-by-example.md#r-macro.decl.hygiene.crate) 会展开为一条路"
"径，用于访问定义该宏的 crate 顶层中的项，而不管该宏是在哪个 crate 中被调用"
"的。"

#: src/paths.md:1560
msgid "Canonical paths"
msgstr "规范路径"

#: src/paths.md:1566
msgid ""
"Each item defined in a module or implementation has a _canonical path_ that "
"corresponds to where within its crate it is defined."
msgstr ""
"模块或实现中定义的每个项都有一条_规范路径_，对应它在其 crate 内的定义位置。"

#: src/paths.md:1572
msgid "All other paths to these items are aliases."
msgstr "指向这些项的所有其他路径都是别名。"

#: src/paths.md:1578
msgid ""
"The canonical path is defined as a _path prefix_ appended by the path "
"segment the item itself defines."
msgstr "规范路径定义为：由_路径前缀_附加该项自身定义的路径段组成。"

#: src/paths.md:1584
msgid ""
"[Implementations](items/implementations.md) and [use declarations](items/use-"
"declarations.md) do not have canonical paths, although the items that "
"implementations define do have them. Items defined in block expressions do "
"not have canonical paths. Items defined in a module that does not have a "
"canonical path do not have a canonical path. Associated items defined in an "
"implementation that refers to an item without a canonical path, e.g. as the "
"implementing type, the trait being implemented, a type parameter or bound on "
"a type parameter, do not have canonical paths."
msgstr ""
"[实现](items/implementations.md)和 [use 声明](items/use-declarations.md)没有"
"规范路径，尽管实现所定义的项确实有规范路径。在块表达式中定义的项没有规范路"
"径。在没有规范路径的模块中定义的项也没有规范路径。在实现中定义的关联项，如果"
"该实现引用了一个没有规范路径的项，例如作为被实现类型、被实现的 trait、类型参"
"数或类型参数上的边界，则这些关联项没有规范路径。"

#: src/paths.md:1590
msgid "The path prefix for modules is the canonical path to that module."
msgstr "模块的路径前缀是指向该模块的规范路径。"

#: src/paths.md:1596
msgid ""
"For bare implementations, it is the canonical path of the item being "
"implemented surrounded by <span class=\"parenthetical\">angle (`<>`)</span> "
"brackets."
msgstr ""
"对于不带 trait 的实现，它是被实现项的规范路径，并用 <span "
"class=\"parenthetical\">尖括号（`<>`）</span> 括起来。"

#: src/paths.md:1602
msgid ""
"For [trait implementations](items/implementations.md#trait-implementations), "
"it is the canonical path of the item being implemented followed by `as` "
"followed by the canonical path to the trait all surrounded in <span "
"class=\"parenthetical\">angle (`<>`)</span> brackets."
msgstr ""
"对于 [trait 实现](items/implementations.md#trait-implementations)，它是被实现"
"项的规范路径，后接 `as`，再后接指向该 trait 的规范路径，整体用 <span "
"class=\"parenthetical\">尖括号（`<>`）</span> 括起来。"

#: src/paths.md:1608
msgid ""
"The canonical path is only meaningful within a given crate. There is no "
"global namespace across crates; an item's canonical path merely identifies "
"it within the crate."
msgstr ""
"规范路径只在给定 crate 内有意义。跨 crate 不存在全局命名空间；项的规范路径仅"
"在该 crate 内标识该项。"

#: src/paths.md:1611
msgid "// Comments show the canonical path of the item.\n"
msgstr "// Comments show the canonical path of the item.\n"

#: src/paths.md:1613
msgid "// crate::a\n"
msgstr "// crate::a\n"

#: src/paths.md:1614
msgid "// crate::a::Struct\n"
msgstr "// crate::a::Struct\n"

#: src/paths.md:1616
msgid "// crate::a::Trait\n"
msgstr "// crate::a::Trait\n"

#: src/paths.md:1617
msgid "// crate::a::Trait::f\n"
msgstr "// crate::a::Trait::f\n"

#: src/paths.md:1621
msgid "// <crate::a::Struct as crate::a::Trait>::f\n"
msgstr "// <crate::a::Struct as crate::a::Trait>::f\n"

#: src/paths.md:1625
msgid "// <crate::a::Struct>::g\n"
msgstr "// <crate::a::Struct>::g\n"

#: src/paths.md:1629
msgid "// crate::without\n"
msgstr "// crate::without\n"

#: src/paths.md:1630
msgid "// crate::without::canonicals\n"
msgstr "// crate::without::canonicals\n"

#: src/paths.md:1631 src/paths.md:1633 src/paths.md:1634 src/paths.md:1638
#: src/paths.md:1642 src/paths.md:1646
msgid "// None\n"
msgstr "// None\n"

#: src/names/name-resolution.md:11
msgid ""
"_Name resolution_ is the process of tying paths and other identifiers to the "
"declarations of those entities. Names are segregated into different "
"[namespaces](../names/namespaces.md), allowing entities in different "
"namespaces to share the same name without conflict. Each name is valid "
"within a [scope](../names/scopes.md), or a region of source text where that "
"name may be referenced. Access to a name may be restricted based on its "
"[visibility](../visibility-and-privacy.md)."
msgstr ""
"_名称解析_ 是将路径和其他标识符关联到这些实体的声明的过程。名称被分隔到不同的"
"[命名空间](../names/namespaces.md)中，使不同命名空间中的实体可以共享同一个名"
"称而不冲突。每个名称在某个[作用域](../names/scopes.md)内有效，也就是该名称可"
"以被引用的一段源文本区域。对名称的访问可能会基于其[可见性](../visibility-and-"
"privacy.md)受到限制。"

#: src/names/name-resolution.md:13
msgid ""
"Name resolution is split into three stages throughout the compilation "
"process. The first stage, _expansion-time resolution_, resolves all [`use` "
"declarations](../items/use-declarations.md) and [macro invocations](../"
"macros.md#macro-invocation). The second stage, _primary resolution_, "
"resolves all names that have not yet been resolved and that do not depend on "
"type information to resolve. The last stage, _type-relative resolution_, "
"resolves the remaining names once type information is available."
msgstr ""
"名称解析在整个编译过程中分为三个阶段。第一阶段，_展开时解析_，解析所有 "
"[`use` 声明](../items/use-declarations.md)和[宏调用](../macros.md#macro-"
"invocation)。第二阶段，_主解析_，解析所有尚未解析且其解析不依赖类型信息的名"
"称。最后阶段，_类型相对解析_，在类型信息可用后解析剩余名称。"

#: src/names/name-resolution.md:19
msgid ""
"Expansion-time resolution is also known as _early resolution_. Primary "
"resolution is also known as _late resolution_."
msgstr "展开时解析也称为_早期解析_。主解析也称为_后期解析_。"

#: src/names/name-resolution.md:28
msgid "General"
msgstr "通用"

#: src/names/name-resolution.md:34
msgid "The rules within this section apply to all stages of name resolution."
msgstr "本节中的规则适用于名称解析的所有阶段。"

#: src/names/name-resolution.md:50
msgid ""
"This is a placeholder for future expansion about resolution of names within "
"various scopes."
msgstr "这是一个占位内容，供日后扩展各种作用域内名称解析的说明。"

#: src/names/name-resolution.md:59
msgid "Expansion-time name resolution"
msgstr "展开时名称解析"

#: src/names/name-resolution.md:65
msgid ""
"Expansion-time name resolution is the stage of name resolution necessary to "
"complete macro expansion and fully generate a crate's [AST](../glossary.md#r-"
"glossary.ast). This stage requires the resolution of macro invocations and "
"`use` declarations. Resolving `use` declarations is required for macro "
"invocations that resolve via [path-based scope](../macros.md#r-"
"macro.invocation.name-resolution). Resolving macro invocations is required "
"in order to expand them."
msgstr ""
"展开时名称解析是完成宏展开并完整生成 crate 的 [AST](../glossary.md#r-"
"glossary.ast) 所必需的名称解析阶段。此阶段需要解析宏调用和 `use` 声明。对于通"
"过[基于路径的作用域](../macros.md#r-macro.invocation.name-resolution)解析的宏"
"调用，必须解析 `use` 声明。必须解析宏调用才能展开它们。"

#: src/names/name-resolution.md:71
msgid ""
"After expansion-time name resolution, the AST must not contain any "
"unexpanded macro invocations. Every macro invocation resolves to a valid "
"definition that exists in the final AST or in an external crate."
msgstr ""
"在展开时名称解析之后，AST 不得包含任何未展开的宏调用。每个宏调用都会解析为一"
"个有效定义，该定义存在于最终 AST 或外部 crate 中。"

#: src/names/name-resolution.md:74
msgid "// ERROR: Cannot find macro `m` in this scope.\n"
msgstr "// ERROR: Cannot find macro `m` in this scope.\n"

#: src/names/name-resolution.md:81
msgid ""
"The resolution of names must be stable. After expansion, names in the fully "
"expanded AST must resolve to the same definition regardless of the order in "
"which macros are expanded and imports are resolved."
msgstr ""
"名称解析必须是稳定的。展开之后，完全展开的 AST 中的名称必须解析为同一定义，而"
"不受宏展开和导入解析顺序影响。"

#: src/names/name-resolution.md:87
msgid ""
"All name resolution candidates selected during macro expansion are "
"considered speculative. Once the crate has been fully expanded, all "
"speculative import resolutions are validated to ensure that macro expansion "
"did not introduce any new ambiguities."
msgstr ""
"宏展开期间选择的所有名称解析候选都被视为推测性的。一旦 crate 已完全展开，所有"
