#: src/inline-assembly.md:2689
msgid ""
"On arm64ec, [call checkers with appropriate thunks](https://"
"learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/arm/arm64ec-abi#authoring-arm64ec-in-"
"assembly) are mandatory when calling functions."
msgstr ""
"在 arm64ec 上，调用函数时必须使用[带有适当 thunk 的调用检查器](https://"
"learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/arm/arm64ec-abi#authoring-arm64ec-in-"
"assembly)。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2695
msgid ""
"The requirement of restoring the stack pointer and non-output registers to "
"their original value only applies when exiting the assembly code."
msgstr "将栈指针和非输出寄存器恢复为原始值的要求，仅适用于退出汇编代码时。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2696
msgid ""
"This means that assembly code that does not fall through and does not jump "
"to any `label` blocks, even if not marked `noreturn`, doesn't need to "
"preserve these registers."
msgstr ""
"这意味着不会直落执行且不会跳转到任何 `label` 块的汇编代码，即使未标记为 "
"`noreturn`，也不需要保留这些寄存器。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2697
msgid ""
"When returning to the assembly code of a different `asm!` block than you "
"entered (e.g. for context switching), these registers must contain the value "
"they had upon entering the `asm!` block that you are _exiting_."
msgstr ""
"当返回到与你进入的 `asm!` 块不同的另一个 `asm!` 块的汇编代码时（例如用于上下"
"文切换），这些寄存器必须包含进入你正在<em>退出</em>的那个 `asm!` 块时它们所具"
"有的值。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2698
msgid ""
"You cannot exit the assembly code of an `asm!` block that has not been "
"entered. Neither can you exit the assembly code of an `asm!` block whose "
"assembly code has already been exited (without first entering it again)."
msgstr ""
"不能退出尚未进入过的 `asm!` 块的汇编代码。也不能退出其汇编代码已经被退出过的 "
"`asm!` 块的汇编代码（除非先再次进入它）。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2699
msgid ""
"You are responsible for switching any target-specific state (e.g. thread-"
"local storage, stack bounds)."
msgstr "你负责切换任何目标特定状态（例如线程局部存储、栈边界）。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2700
msgid ""
"You cannot jump from an address in one `asm!` block to an address in "
"another, even within the same function or block, without treating their "
"contexts as potentially different and requiring context switching. You "
"cannot assume that any particular value in those contexts (e.g. current "
"stack pointer or temporary values below the stack pointer) will remain "
"unchanged between the two `asm!` blocks."
msgstr ""
"不能从一个 `asm!` 块中的地址跳转到另一个 `asm!` 块中的地址，即使它们位于同一"
"函数或同一块中也不能这样做，除非将它们的上下文视为可能不同并要求进行上下文切"
"换。不能假定这些上下文中的任何特定值（例如当前栈指针或栈指针下方的临时值）会"
"在两个 `asm!` 块之间保持不变。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2701
msgid ""
"The set of memory locations that you may access is the intersection of those "
"allowed by the `asm!` blocks you entered and exited."
msgstr ""
"你可以访问的内存位置集合，是你进入和退出的 `asm!` 块所允许访问集合的交集。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2707
msgid ""
"You cannot assume that two `asm!` blocks adjacent in source code, even "
"without any other code between them, will end up in successive addresses in "
"the binary without any other instructions between them."
msgstr ""
"不能假定源代码中相邻的两个 `asm!` 块，即使它们之间没有任何其他代码，也会在二"
"进制中最终位于连续地址且中间没有任何其他指令。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2713
msgid ""
"You cannot assume that an `asm!` block will appear exactly once in the "
"output binary. The compiler is allowed to instantiate multiple copies of the "
"`asm!` block, for example when the function containing it is inlined in "
"multiple places."
msgstr ""
"不能假定一个 `asm!` 块在输出二进制中只会出现一次。编译器可以实例化该 `asm!` "
"块的多个副本，例如当包含它的函数在多处被内联时。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2719
msgid ""
"On x86, inline assembly must not end with an instruction prefix (such as "
"`LOCK`) that would apply to instructions generated by the compiler."
msgstr ""
"在 x86 上，内联汇编不得以会应用到编译器生成指令的指令前缀（例如 `LOCK`）结"
"束。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2720
msgid ""
"The compiler is currently unable to detect this due to the way inline "
"assembly is compiled, but may catch and reject this in the future."
msgstr ""
"由于内联汇编的编译方式，编译器目前无法检测这一点，但将来可以捕获并拒绝这种情"
"况。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2730
msgid ""
"As a general rule, the flags covered by `preserves_flags` are those which "
"are _not_ preserved when performing a function call."
msgstr ""
"一般规则是，`preserves_flags` 覆盖的标志，是执行函数调用时<em>不会</em>被保留"
"的那些标志。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2739
msgid "Rules for naked inline assembly"
msgstr "裸内联汇编规则"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2745
msgid ""
"To avoid undefined behavior, these rules must be followed when using "
"function-scope inline assembly in naked functions (`naked_asm!`):"
msgstr ""
"为避免未定义行为，在裸函数中使用函数作用域内联汇编（`naked_asm!`）时，必须遵"
"守这些规则："

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2751
msgid ""
"Any registers not used for function inputs according to the calling "
"convention and function signature will contain an undefined value on entry "
"to the `naked_asm!` block."
msgstr ""
"根据调用约定和函数签名未用于函数输入的任何寄存器，在进入 `naked_asm!` 块时都"
"将包含未定义值。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2758
msgid ""
"All callee-saved registers must have the same value upon return as they had "
"on entry."
msgstr "所有被调用者保存寄存器在返回时必须具有与进入时相同的值。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2764
msgid "Caller-saved registers may be used freely."
msgstr "调用者保存寄存器可以自由使用。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2770
msgid ""
"Behavior is undefined if execution falls through past the end of the "
"assembly code."
msgstr "如果执行直落越过汇编代码末尾，则行为是未定义的。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2771
msgid ""
"Every path through the assembly code is expected to terminate with a return "
"instruction or to diverge."
msgstr "穿过汇编代码的每条路径都预期以返回指令终止，或发散。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2783
msgid ""
"The compiler cannot assume that the instructions in the `naked_asm!` block "
"are the ones that will actually be executed."
msgstr "编译器不能假定 `naked_asm!` 块中的指令就是实际将被执行的指令。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2784
msgid ""
"This effectively means that the compiler must treat the `naked_asm!` as a "
"black box and only take the interface specification into account, not the "
"instructions themselves."
msgstr ""
"这实际上意味着编译器必须将 `naked_asm!` 视为黑盒，并且只考虑接口规范，而不是"
"指令本身。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2791
msgid "Unwinding out of a `naked_asm!` block is allowed."
msgstr "允许从 `naked_asm!` 块中展开。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2792
msgid ""
"For correct behavior, the appropriate assembler directives that emit "
"unwinding metadata must be used."
msgstr "为获得正确行为，必须使用会发出展开元数据的适当汇编器指令。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2797 src/inline-assembly.md:2851
msgid "\"sysv64-unwind\""
msgstr "\"sysv64-unwind\""

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2799
msgid ""
"// \"CFI\" here stands for \"call frame information\".\n"
"        \".cfi_startproc\""
msgstr ""
"// \"CFI\" here stands for \"call frame information\".\n"
"        \".cfi_startproc\""

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2801
msgid ""
"// The CFA (canonical frame address) is the value of `rsp`\n"
"        // before the `call`, i.e. before the return address, `rip`,\n"
"        // was pushed to `rsp`, so it's eight bytes higher in memory\n"
"        // than `rsp` upon function entry (after `rip` has been\n"
"        // pushed).\n"
"        //\n"
"        // This is the default, so we don't have to write it.\n"
"        //\".cfi_def_cfa rsp, 8\",\n"
"        //\n"
"        // The traditional thing to do is to preserve the base\n"
"        // pointer, so we'll do that.\n"
"        \"push rbp\""
msgstr ""
"// The CFA (canonical frame address) is the value of `rsp`\n"
"        // before the `call`, i.e. before the return address, `rip`,\n"
"        // was pushed to `rsp`, so it's eight bytes higher in memory\n"
"        // than `rsp` upon function entry (after `rip` has been\n"
"        // pushed).\n"
"        //\n"
"        // This is the default, so we don't have to write it.\n"
"        //\".cfi_def_cfa rsp, 8\",\n"
"        //\n"
"        // The traditional thing to do is to preserve the base\n"
"        // pointer, so we'll do that.\n"
"        \"push rbp\""

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2813
msgid ""
"// Since we've now extended the stack downward by 8 bytes in\n"
"        // memory, we need to adjust the offset to the CFA from `rsp`\n"
"        // by another 8 bytes.\n"
"        \".cfi_adjust_cfa_offset 8\""
msgstr ""
"// Since we've now extended the stack downward by 8 bytes in\n"
"        // memory, we need to adjust the offset to the CFA from `rsp`\n"
"        // by another 8 bytes.\n"
"        \".cfi_adjust_cfa_offset 8\""

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2817
msgid ""
"// We also then annotate where we've stored the caller's value\n"
"        // of `rbp`, relative to the CFA, so that when unwinding into\n"
"        // the caller we can find it, in case we need it to calculate\n"
"        // the caller's CFA relative to it.\n"
"        //\n"
"        // Here, we've stored the caller's `rbp` starting 16 bytes\n"
"        // below the CFA.  I.e., starting from the CFA, there's first\n"
"        // the `rip` (which starts 8 bytes below the CFA and continues\n"
"        // up to it), then there's the caller's `rbp` that we just\n"
"        // pushed.\n"
"        \".cfi_offset rbp, -16\""
msgstr ""
"// We also then annotate where we've stored the caller's value\n"
"        // of `rbp`, relative to the CFA, so that when unwinding into\n"
"        // the caller we can find it, in case we need it to calculate\n"
"        // the caller's CFA relative to it.\n"
"        //\n"
"        // Here, we've stored the caller's `rbp` starting 16 bytes\n"
"        // below the CFA.  I.e., starting from the CFA, there's first\n"
"        // the `rip` (which starts 8 bytes below the CFA and continues\n"
"        // up to it), then there's the caller's `rbp` that we just\n"
"        // pushed.\n"
"        \".cfi_offset rbp, -16\""

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2828
msgid ""
"// As is traditional, we set the base pointer to the value of\n"
"        // the stack pointer.  This way, the base pointer stays the\n"
"        // same throughout the function body.\n"
"        \"mov rbp, rsp\""
msgstr ""
"// As is traditional, we set the base pointer to the value of\n"
"        // the stack pointer.  This way, the base pointer stays the\n"
"        // same throughout the function body.\n"
"        \"mov rbp, rsp\""

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2832
msgid ""
"// We can now track the offset to the CFA from the base\n"
"        // pointer.  This means we don't need to make any further\n"
"        // adjustments until the end, as we don't change `rbp`.\n"
"        \".cfi_def_cfa_register rbp\""
msgstr ""
"// We can now track the offset to the CFA from the base\n"
"        // pointer.  This means we don't need to make any further\n"
"        // adjustments until the end, as we don't change `rbp`.\n"
"        \".cfi_def_cfa_register rbp\""

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2836
msgid ""
"// We can now call a function that may panic.\n"
"        \"call {f}\""
msgstr ""
"// We can now call a function that may panic.\n"
"        \"call {f}\""

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2838
msgid ""
"// Upon return, we restore `rbp` in preparation for returning\n"
"        // ourselves.\n"
"        \"pop rbp\""
msgstr ""
"// Upon return, we restore `rbp` in preparation for returning\n"
"        // ourselves.\n"
"        \"pop rbp\""

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2841
msgid ""
"// Now that we've restored `rbp`, we must specify the offset\n"
"        // to the CFA again in terms of `rsp`.\n"
"        \".cfi_def_cfa rsp, 8\""
msgstr ""
"// Now that we've restored `rbp`, we must specify the offset\n"
"        // to the CFA again in terms of `rsp`.\n"
"        \".cfi_def_cfa rsp, 8\""

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2844
msgid ""
"// Now we can return.\n"
"        \"ret\""
msgstr ""
"// Now we can return.\n"
"        \"ret\""

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2862
msgid ""
"For more information on the `cfi` assembler directives above, see these "
"resources:"
msgstr "有关上述 `cfi` 汇编器指令的更多信息，请参阅这些资源："

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2864
msgid ""
"[Using `as` - CFI directives](https://sourceware.org/binutils/docs/as/CFI-"
"directives.html)"
msgstr ""
"[Using `as` - CFI directives](https://sourceware.org/binutils/docs/as/CFI-"
"directives.html)"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2865
msgid ""
"[DWARF Debugging Information Format Version 5](https://dwarfstd.org/doc/"
"DWARF5.pdf)"
msgstr ""
"[DWARF Debugging Information Format Version 5](https://dwarfstd.org/doc/"
"DWARF5.pdf)"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2866
msgid ""
"[ImperialViolet - CFI directives in assembly files](https://"
"www.imperialviolet.org/2017/01/18/cfi.html)"
msgstr ""
"[ImperialViolet - CFI directives in assembly files](https://"
"www.imperialviolet.org/2017/01/18/cfi.html)"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2875
msgid "Correctness and validity"
msgstr "正确性和有效性"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2881
msgid ""
"In addition to all of the previous rules, the string argument to `asm!` must "
"ultimately become---after all other arguments are evaluated, formatting is "
"performed, and operands are translated---assembly that is both syntactically "
"correct and semantically valid for the target architecture. The formatting "
"rules allow the compiler to generate assembly with correct syntax. Rules "
"concerning operands permit valid translation of Rust operands into and out "
"of the assembly code. Adherence to these rules is necessary, but not "
"sufficient, for the final expanded assembly to be both correct and valid. "
"For instance:"
msgstr ""
"除前述所有规则外，传给 `asm!` 的字符串实参最终必须在所有其他实参求值、格式化"
"完成、操作数转换之后，成为对目标架构而言语法正确且语义有效的汇编。格式化规则"
"允许编译器生成语法正确的汇编。关于操作数的规则允许将 Rust 操作数有效地转换进"
"出汇编代码。遵守这些规则是最终展开后的汇编既正确又有效的必要条件，但并非充分"
"条件。例如："

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2883
msgid ""
"arguments may be placed in positions which are syntactically incorrect after "
"formatting"
msgstr "实参在格式化后可能被放置到语法不正确的位置"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2884
msgid ""
"an instruction may be correctly written, but given architecturally invalid "
"operands"
msgstr "一条指令可能写法正确，但给定了架构上无效的操作数"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2885
msgid ""
"an architecturally unspecified instruction may be assembled into unspecified "
"code"
msgstr "架构未指定的指令可能被汇编成未指定的代码"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2886
msgid ""
"a set of instructions, each correct and valid, may cause undefined behavior "
"if placed in immediate succession"
msgstr "一组各自正确且有效的指令，如果紧接排列，可能导致未定义行为"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2892
msgid ""
"As a result, these rules are _non-exhaustive_. The compiler is not required "
"to check the correctness and validity of the initial string nor the final "
"assembly that is generated. The assembler may check for correctness and "
"validity but is not required to do so. When using `asm!`, a typographical "
"error may be sufficient to make a program unsound, and the rules for "
"assembly may include thousands of pages of architectural reference manuals. "
"Programmers should exercise appropriate care, as invoking this `unsafe` "
"capability comes with assuming the responsibility of not violating rules of "
"both the compiler or the architecture."
msgstr ""
"因此，这些规则是<em>非穷尽的</em>。编译器不需要检查初始字符串或最终生成的汇编"
"的正确性和有效性。汇编器可以检查正确性和有效性，但不要求这样做。使用 `asm!` "
"时，一个排印错误就可能足以使程序不健全，而汇编规则可能包含数千页架构参考手"
"册。程序员应当保持适当谨慎，因为调用这种 `unsafe` 能力意味着承担不违反编译器"
"和架构双方规则的责任。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2898
msgid "Directives support"
msgstr "指令支持"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2904
msgid ""
"Inline assembly supports a subset of the directives supported by both GNU AS "
"and LLVM's internal assembler, given as follows. The result of using other "
"directives is assembler-specific (and may cause an error, or may be accepted "
"as-is)."
msgstr ""
"内联汇编支持 GNU AS 和 LLVM 内部汇编器共同支持的指令子集，如下所示。使用其他"
"指令的结果取决于汇编器（并且可能导致错误，也可能按原样被接受）。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2910
msgid ""
"If inline assembly includes any \"stateful\" directive that modifies how "
"subsequent assembly is processed, the assembly code must undo the effects of "
"any such directives before the inline assembly ends."
msgstr ""
"如果内联汇编包含任何会修改后续汇编处理方式的“有状态”指令，则汇编代码必须在内"
"联汇编结束前撤销任何此类指令的影响。"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2916
msgid ""
"The following directives are guaranteed to be supported by the assembler:"
msgstr "保证汇编器支持以下指令："

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2918
msgid "`.2byte`"
msgstr "`.2byte`"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2919
msgid "`.4byte`"
msgstr "`.4byte`"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2920
msgid "`.8byte`"
msgstr "`.8byte`"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2921
msgid "`.align`"
msgstr "`.align`"

#: src/inline-assembly.md:2922
msgid "`.alt_entry`"
